<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gretl-functions>
<gretl-function-package name="EViewsCompat" minver="2026a">
<author>EViewsCompat contributors</author>
<version>0.6</version>
<date>2026-11-15</date>
<description>EViews-style LS, NLS, ARMA, systems, VAR/VEC, forecasts, Wald, diagnostics and at-functions</description>
<tags>C10 C20 C51</tags>
<label>EViews-style equation (LS)</label>
<menu-attachment>MAINWIN/Model/LinearModels</menu-attachment>
<help>
EViewsCompat: EViews-style estimation and functions for gretl

GUI: Model &gt; Linear models &gt; EViews-style equation (LS)
  Type the equation exactly as in EViews' &quot;Equation Estimation&quot; box, e.g.
      dlog(lrm) c dlog(lry) lrm(-1) ibo ide
  and select (at least) the series the equation uses. The result window
  shows the EViews-style table; its graph button draws Actual/Fitted/Residual.
  Save the result as an icon to keep it in the session (like an EViews
  workfile object).

Note: hansl names are case-sensitive, so type series names as they appear
in gretl. EViews keywords (c, log, d, dlog, the @-functions) are not.

Functions (CLI / console). &quot;dataset&quot; means: all series in the dataset.

  ev_ls(spec, dataset [, cov] [, quiet])  -&gt; bundle
      Least squares. spec in EViews syntax. cov: &quot;ordinary&quot; (default),
      &quot;white&quot; or &quot;hac&quot;. Prints the EViews-style table unless quiet = 1.
      Supported terms: c, x, x(-k), log(x), d(x), dlog(x), exp(), abs(),
      sqr(), any gretl expression, @trend, @seas(k), @pch, @pc,
      @pchy, @pcy, @movav(x,n), @movsum(x,n), @cumsum,
      @mean, @stdev.
      Bundle members: coeff, stderr, tstat, pval, vcv, rsq, adjrsq, sigma,
      ssr, lnl, dw, aic, sc, hq, F, Fp, T, k, uhat, yhat, y, X, sample.
      aic/sc/hq use EViews' per-observation scaling (gretl value / T).

  ev_wald(eq, &quot;c(2)=0, c(3)=c(4)&quot;)      -&gt; bundle (F, Fp, chi2, chi2p)
      Linear coefficient restrictions in EViews c(i) notation.

  ev_diag(eq [, lags])                  -&gt; bundle
      Jarque-Bera, Breusch-Godfrey LM (default 2 lags), White test with
      cross terms; F and Obs*R-squared versions as in EViews.

  ev_freeze(eq, &quot;file.csv&quot;)             save table (.txt .csv .tex .html)
      Relative names are written in the gretl working directory.

  ev_print(&amp;eq), ev_plot(&amp;eq)           print table / Actual-Fitted-Residual

  ev_gen(&quot;expr&quot;, dataset)               EViews expression -&gt; series
  ev_trend(), ev_seas(k), ev_pch(x), ev_pc(x), ev_pchy(x), ev_pcy(x),
  ev_movav(x,n), ev_movsum(x,n), ev_mean(x), ev_stdev(x) (n-1),
  ev_var(x) (population, n), ev_obs(x), ev_elem(x, &quot;1990:1&quot;)

Forecasts (eq.forecast). The forecast sample is the current sample.

  ev_forecast(eq, dataset [, dynamic=1] [, quiet])   -&gt; bundle
      Static (0) or dynamic (1). Dynamic forecasts replace lags of a plain
      dependent variable, y(-k), by earlier forecasts. Bundle: yf, se,
      actual, rmse, mae, mape, theil, bias_prop, var_prop, cov_prop.
  series f = ev_fcast_series(fc)     series s = ev_fcast_se(fc)
  ev_fplot(&amp;fc [, &quot;file.png&quot;])       forecast with +/- 2 S.E. and actual

VAR objects (var v.ls 1 2 y1 y2 @ c x)

  ev_varest(&quot;1 2 y1 y2 @ c x&quot;, dataset [, quiet] [, &quot;names&quot;])  -&gt; bundle
      Lag pairs (1 2 = lags 1 to 2), endogenous variables, then exogenous
      after the at-sign; c = constant (included by default when there is no
      exogenous part). Use series names so lags can use pre-sample data;
      &quot;names&quot; gives display names, e.g. &quot;dlog(cons) dlog(gdp)&quot;.
  ev_varprint(&amp;v)               EViews-style estimates: coef, (s.e.), [t]
  ev_vargranger(v)              Granger causality / block exogeneity Wald
  ev_varirf(v, 10)              impulse responses (Cholesky)
  ev_varirfplot(v, 10 [, &quot;file.png&quot;])   grid of response graphs
  ev_vardecomp(v, 10)           variance decomposition (percent)
  ev_varlaglen(v, dataset, 8)   lag length criteria
  series r = ev_varresid(v, 1)  residuals of equation 1

Explicit equations, ARMA terms (ev_ls dispatches automatically)

  ev_ls(&quot;y = c(1) + c(2)*x^c(3)&quot;, dataset)    nonlinear least squares
  ev_ls(&quot;y c x ar(1) ar(4) ma(1)&quot;, dataset)    regression with ARMA errors (ML)
      ARMA output shows SIGMASQ and the inverted AR/MA roots. Forecasts of
      either kind use the same ev_forecast call.

Forecasts of transformed dependents

  ev_forecast(eq, dataset, 1, 0, 1)   dynamic forecast reported in levels:
      for log(Y), d(Y), dlog(Y) the forecast of Y is built step by step and
      every regressor that uses Y is recomputed. ev_fcast_series(fc, 1) and
      ev_fcast_se(fc, 1) give the level forecast and its S.E. Dynamic S.E.
      follow the lags of the dependent variable (innovation uncertainty).

Systems (system sys1 / sys1.sur)

  ev_system(deps, xspecs, cnums, dataset, &quot;sur&quot; [, &quot;z1 z2&quot;])
      deps: array of dependent variables; xspecs: regressors per equation
      (&quot;c x1 x2&quot;); cnums: coefficient numbers per equation (&quot;1 2 3&quot;); the same
      number in two equations shares the coefficient. Methods ls, sur, tsls,
      3sls; instruments get a constant added. ev_wald works with c(i).

VEC models (var v.ec(c, 1) 1 2 y1 y2)

  ev_vecm(&quot;1 2 y1 y2 [@ x]&quot;, dataset, &quot;c&quot;, 1)   trend case a-e, rank
  ev_coint(&quot;y1 y2&quot;, dataset, &quot;c&quot;, 4)            Johansen test
      The VAR views (ev_varirf, ev_varirfplot, ev_vardecomp) work on VEC results.

More system estimators
  ev_system(..., &quot;wls&quot; | &quot;wtsls&quot; | &quot;gmm&quot;, &quot;z1 z2&quot;)   weighted LS, weighted TSLS,
      two-step GMM with White weighting (J-statistic reported)
  FIML: estimate with gretl's system command (method=fiml), then
      ev_sysfrom(&quot;fiml&quot;, $coeff, $vcv, $uhat, $yhat, pos, cnums, kk, deps, eqtext, $t1, $lnl)
      gives the EViews-style result (the translator and evqt do this for you)

Structural VAR (v.svar)
  ev_svar(&amp;v, A, B)   short-run A e = B u: in A and B, numbers are fixed and NA
                      entries are estimated (ML); LR test of over-identification
  ev_svar_lr(&amp;v)      long-run (Blanchard-Quah) restrictions
      Afterwards ev_varirf, ev_varirfplot and ev_vardecomp use the structural shocks.

Model objects (model m / m.merge eq / m.append identity / m.solve)
  ev_modelsolve(bundles eqs, strings identities, dataset [, dynamic=1])
      Solves least-squares and explicit equations plus identities period by period
      (Newton). ev_modelseries(m, k) is the solution of endogenous variable k.

Nonlinear systems and HAC GMM
  ev_nlsystem(eqs, dataset, &quot;ls|wls|sur|tsls|3sls|gmm&quot; [, &quot;z1 z2&quot;] [, quiet] [, haclag])
      equations written as y = f(x, c(i)); shared c(i) across equations;
      Levenberg-Marquardt with numerical derivatives
  ev_system(..., &quot;gmm&quot;, &quot;z1 z2&quot;, quiet, eqtext, haclag)   haclag 0 = Newey-West
      automatic lag, k = Bartlett lag k, -1 (default) = White

Text-form structural restrictions (EViews @e / @u / @lr) are turned into A/B
patterns or a long-run ordering by the translator and evqt; in hansl call
ev_svar(&amp;v, A, B) or ev_svar_lr(&amp;v, 0, {order}).

Model options: ev_modelsolve(eqs, identities, dataset, dynamic, quiet, opts)
  opts = _(overrides = defarray(&quot;x&quot;), suffix = &quot;_1&quot;, addfactors = 1, reps = 100, seed = 1)
  overrides use series x_1 in place of x; add factors are series &lt;variable&gt;_a
  (ev_eqres(eq, dataset) makes an equation fit exactly); reps &gt; 0 runs a
  stochastic simulation: ev_modelseries(m, k, &quot;mean&quot;) and (m, k, &quot;sd&quot;).

ARCH models (needs the gig package, installed with gretl)
  ev_garch(&quot;y c x&quot;, dataset, &quot;garch|tarch|egarch&quot;, narch, ngarch [, quiet]
           [, &quot;sd|var|log&quot; (ARCH-M term)] [, nthr (threshold order, -1 = default)])  -&gt; bundle
      EViews equation.arch(narch, ngarch[, t|e]). Coefficients are in EViews order and
      parameterisation: mean equation, then C(.) of the variance equation
      GARCH  : h = w + a e(-1)^2 + b h(-1)
      TARCH  : h = w + a e(-1)^2 + g e(-1)^2 (e(-1) &lt; 0) + b h(-1)
      EGARCH : log h = w + a |z(-1)| + g z(-1) + b log h(-1),  z = e/sqrt(h)
      b.failed = 1 when the estimation does not converge (a warning is printed).
  ev_garchprint(&amp;b)            EViews-style output with the variance equation
  ev_garchseries(b [, &quot;h&quot;|&quot;resid&quot;])   conditional variance or residual series

Panel pages
  setobs id time --panel-vars        (EViews pagestruct id @date(time))
  adf k x --c                        on a panel prints the Im-Pesaran-Shin test
  ev_unstack(x)   -&gt; T x N matrix, one column per cross-section unit
  ev_panelids(id) -&gt; the identifier of each unit, in panel order

Panel least squares (EViews ls on a panel page)
  ev_panel(&quot;y c x&quot;, dataset [, &quot;none|fixed|random&quot;] [, period_fe] [, quiet])  -&gt; bundle
      ls(cx=f) / ls(cx=r) / ls(per=f); only the regressors are reported, as in EViews
  ev_panelprint(&amp;b); ev_resid(b) and ev_fit(b) give residual and fitted series

pagestack helpers
  ev_stackids(&quot;x_?&quot;, dataset)   -&gt; strings: the identifiers ? of matching series
  ev_stack(&quot;x_?&quot;, dataset [, ids]) -&gt; T x N matrix, one column per identifier
</help>
<depends count="1">
gig </depends>
<gretl-function name="ev_gen" type="series">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="expr" type="string">
<description>EViews expression, e.g. dlog(y)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list">
<description>Series referenced in the expression</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code># Evaluate an EViews-syntax expression and return the series.
string evx_e = ev__prep(expr, vars)
if instring(evx_e, &quot;ev_&quot;)
  # expression calls package functions: catch is not allowed here
  series evx_out = @evx_e
else
  catch series evx_out = @evx_e
endif
errorif($error, sprintf(&quot;Cannot evaluate '%s' (hansl: %s). Check the series names and that they are in the list you passed.&quot;, expr, evx_e))
return evx_out
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_ls" type="bundle">
 <params count="4">
  <param name="spec" type="string">
<description>Equation, e.g. y c x x(-1)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list" optional="true">
<description>Series used (e.g. dataset)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="cov" type="string" optional="true">
<description>ordinary, white or hac</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0">
<description>Suppress printed output</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code>errorif(!exists(vars), &quot;Pass the series to use as second argument, e.g. ev_ls(\&quot;y c x\&quot;, dataset)&quot;)
string evx_cov = exists(cov) ? tolower(cov) : &quot;ordinary&quot;
# explicit form y = c(1) + c(2)*x  -&gt; nonlinear least squares
if instring(spec, &quot;=&quot;)
  return ev_nls(spec, vars, evx_cov, quiet)
endif
# ARMA error terms ar(k) / ma(k) -&gt; regression with ARMA errors (exact ML)
if regsub(tolower(&quot; &quot; ~ spec ~ &quot; &quot;), &quot;.*\s(ar|ma)\([0-9]+\)\s.*&quot;, &quot;ARMA&quot;) == &quot;ARMA&quot;
  return ev_arma(spec, vars, quiet)
endif
errorif(!instring(&quot; ordinary white hac &quot;, &quot; &quot; ~ evx_cov ~ &quot; &quot;), &quot;cov must be ordinary, white or hac&quot;)
strings evx_tok = strsplit(spec)
errorif(nelem(evx_tok) &lt; 2, &quot;The specification needs a dependent variable and at least one regressor&quot;)

series evx_y = ev_gen(evx_tok[1], vars)
list evx_X = null
strings evx_lab = array(0)
scalar evx_hascon = 0
loop evx_i = 2..nelem(evx_tok)
  string evx_t = evx_tok[evx_i]
  if tolower(evx_t) == &quot;c&quot;
    list evx_X += const
    evx_lab += &quot;C&quot;
    evx_hascon = 1
  else
    string evx_v = sprintf(&quot;evx_r%d&quot;, evx_i)
    series @evx_v = ev_gen(evx_t, vars)
    list evx_X += @evx_v
    evx_lab += toupper(evx_t)
  endif
endloop

scalar evx_n0 = $nobs
if evx_cov == &quot;white&quot;
  set force_hc on
  ols evx_y evx_X --robust --quiet
elif evx_cov == &quot;hac&quot;
  errorif($datatype != 2, &quot;HAC covariance needs time-series data&quot;)
  ols evx_y evx_X --robust --quiet
else
  ols evx_y evx_X --quiet
endif

bundle b
b.spec = spec
b.depvar = toupper(evx_tok[1])
b.labels = evx_lab
b.covtype = evx_cov
b.coeff = $coeff
b.stderr = $stderr
b.vcv = $vcv
b.T = $T
b.k = $ncoeff
b.rsq = $rsq
b.adjrsq = 1 - (1 - $rsq) * ($T - 1) / ($T - $ncoeff)
b.sigma = $sigma
b.ssr = $ess
b.lnl = $lnl
b.dw = $dw
b.hascon = evx_hascon
b.adjusted = $T &lt; evx_n0
b.estdate = strftime($now[1], &quot;%m/%d/%y   Time: %H:%M&quot;)

series evx_u = $uhat
series evx_f = $yhat
smpl ok(evx_u) --restrict
b.y = {evx_y}
b.X = {evx_X}
b.uhat = {evx_u}
b.yhat = {evx_f}
series evx_o = obs
b.tobs = {evx_o}
b.sample =sprintf(&quot;%s %s&quot;, obslabel($t1), obslabel($t2))

scalar n = b.T
scalar k = b.k
matrix d = b.y - meanc(b.y)
b.meany = meanc(b.y)
b.sdy = sqrt(d'd / (n - 1))
b.aic = -2 * b.lnl / n + 2 * k / n
b.sc = -2 * b.lnl / n + k * log(n) / n
b.hq = -2 * b.lnl / n + 2 * k * log(log(n)) / n
if evx_hascon &amp;&amp; k &gt; 1
  b.F = (b.rsq / (k - 1)) / ((1 - b.rsq) / (n - k))
  b.Fp = pvalue(F, k - 1, n - k, b.F)
else
  b.F = NA
  b.Fp = NA
endif
b.tstat = b.coeff ./ b.stderr
matrix p = zeros(k, 1)
loop i = 1..k
  p[i] = 2 * pvalue(t, n - k, abs(b.tstat[i]))
endloop
b.pval = p

if !quiet
  ev_print(&amp;b)
endif
return b
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_print" type="void" pkg-role="bundle-print">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="b" type="bundleref"/>
 </params>
<code>errorif(!inbundle(b, &quot;coeff&quot;), &quot;Not an ev_ls result&quot;)
printf &quot;\nDependent Variable: %s\n&quot;, b.depvar
printf &quot;Method: %s\n&quot;, inbundle(b, &quot;method&quot;) ? b.method : &quot;Least Squares&quot;
printf &quot;Date: %s\n&quot;, b.estdate
printf &quot;Sample%s: %s\n&quot;, b.adjusted ? &quot; (adjusted)&quot; : &quot;&quot;, b.sample
printf &quot;Included observations: %d%s\n&quot;, b.T, b.adjusted ? &quot; after adjustments&quot; : &quot;&quot;
if b.covtype == &quot;white&quot;
  printf &quot;White heteroskedasticity-consistent standard errors &amp; covariance\n&quot;
elif b.covtype == &quot;hac&quot;
  printf &quot;HAC standard errors &amp; covariance (Bartlett kernel, Newey-West)\n&quot;
endif
if inbundle(b, &quot;eqline&quot;)
  printf &quot;%s\n&quot;, b.eqline
endif
printf &quot;\n&quot;
ev__line(78)
printf &quot;%-26s%13s%13s%14s%12s\n&quot;, &quot;Variable&quot;, &quot;Coefficient&quot;, &quot;Std. Error&quot;, &quot;t-Statistic&quot;, &quot;Prob.&quot;
ev__line(78)
matrix ord = inbundle(b, &quot;order&quot;) ? b.order : seq(1, b.k)
loop r = 1..cols(ord)
  scalar i = ord[r]
  printf &quot;%-26s%13.6f%13.6f%14.6f%12.4f\n&quot;, b.labels[i], b.coeff[i], b.stderr[i], b.tstat[i], b.pval[i]
endloop
if inbundle(b, &quot;sigmasq&quot;)
  printf &quot;%-26s%13.6f%13.6f%14.6f%12.4f\n&quot;, &quot;SIGMASQ&quot;, b.sigmasq, b.sigmasq_se, b.sigmasq / b.sigmasq_se, 2 * pvalue(t, b.T - b.k, abs(b.sigmasq / b.sigmasq_se))
endif
ev__line(78)
if inbundle(b, &quot;iv&quot;)
  # instrumental variables: no likelihood-based statistics (as EViews)
  printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f    %-24s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;R-squared&quot;, b.rsq, &quot;Mean dependent var&quot;, b.meany
  printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f    %-24s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Adjusted R-squared&quot;, b.adjrsq, &quot;S.D. dependent var&quot;, b.sdy
  printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f    %-24s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;S.E. of regression&quot;, b.sigma, &quot;Sum squared resid&quot;, b.ssr
  printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f    %-24s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Durbin-Watson stat&quot;, b.dw, &quot;J-statistic&quot;, b.J
  printf &quot;%-22s%14d    %-24s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Instrument rank&quot;, b.instrank, &quot;Prob(J-statistic)&quot;, b.Jp
  ev__line(78)
  return
endif
printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f    %-24s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;R-squared&quot;, b.rsq, &quot;Mean dependent var&quot;, b.meany
printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f    %-24s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Adjusted R-squared&quot;, b.adjrsq, &quot;S.D. dependent var&quot;, b.sdy
printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f    %-24s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;S.E. of regression&quot;, b.sigma, &quot;Akaike info criterion&quot;, b.aic
printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f    %-24s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Sum squared resid&quot;, b.ssr, &quot;Schwarz criterion&quot;, b.sc
printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f    %-24s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Log likelihood&quot;, b.lnl, &quot;Hannan-Quinn criter.&quot;, b.hq
if ok(b.F)
  printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f    %-24s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;F-statistic&quot;, b.F, &quot;Durbin-Watson stat&quot;, b.dw
  printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Prob(F-statistic)&quot;, b.Fp
else
  printf &quot;%-22s%14s    %-24s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;&quot;, &quot;&quot;, &quot;Durbin-Watson stat&quot;, b.dw
endif
ev__line(78)
if inbundle(b, &quot;ar_roots&quot;)
  printf &quot;%-22s%s\n&quot;, &quot;Inverted AR Roots&quot;, b.ar_roots
endif
if inbundle(b, &quot;ma_roots&quot;)
  printf &quot;%-22s%s\n&quot;, &quot;Inverted MA Roots&quot;, b.ma_roots
endif
if inbundle(b, &quot;ar_roots&quot;) || inbundle(b, &quot;ma_roots&quot;)
  ev__line(78)
endif
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_plot" type="void" pkg-role="bundle-plot">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="b" type="bundleref"/>
 </params>
<code># EViews View &gt; Actual, Fitted, Residual
errorif(!inbundle(b, &quot;uhat&quot;), &quot;Not an ev_ls result&quot;)
matrix M = b.y ~ b.yhat ~ b.uhat
cnameset(M, defarray(&quot;Actual&quot;, &quot;Fitted&quot;, &quot;Residual&quot;))
gnuplot 1 2 3 --matrix=M --time-series --with-lines --y2axis=3 --output=display {set title &quot;Actual, Fitted, Residual&quot;; set ylabel &quot;Actual / Fitted&quot;; set y2label &quot;Residual&quot;;}
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_wald" type="bundle">
 <params count="3">
  <param name="b" type="bundle">
<description>ev_ls result</description>
  </param>
  <param name="restr" type="string">
<description>Restrictions, e.g. c(2)=0, c(3)=0</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
 </params>
<code>errorif(!inbundle(b, &quot;coeff&quot;), &quot;First argument must be an ev_ls result&quot;)
strings R = strsplit(restr, &quot;,&quot;)
scalar J = nelem(R)
scalar k = b.k
scalar n = b.T
matrix Rm = zeros(J, k)
matrix q = zeros(J, 1)
# coefficient numbers: c(i) is the i-th coefficient, except in systems
# where the numbers used may have gaps
matrix cpos = inbundle(b, &quot;cnums&quot;) ? b.cnums : seq(1, k)
scalar K = maxr(cpos)
matrix evw_c = zeros(K, 1)
loop j = 1..J
  strings sides = strsplit(R[j], &quot;=&quot;)
  errorif(nelem(sides) != 2, sprintf(&quot;Restriction '%s' must contain exactly one '='&quot;, R[j]))
  string ex = sprintf(&quot;(%s)-(%s)&quot;, sides[1], sides[2])
  ex = regsub(ex, &quot;(?i)\bc\(([0-9]+)\)&quot;, &quot;evw_c[\1]&quot;)
  matrix idx = {}
  evw_c = zeros(K, 1)
  catch scalar f0 = @ex
  errorif($error, sprintf(&quot;Cannot parse restriction '%s' (coefficients are c(1)..c(%d))&quot;, R[j], k))
  loop i = 1..k
    evw_c = zeros(K, 1)
    evw_c[cpos[i]] = 1
    Rm[j, i] = (@ex) - f0
  endloop
  # linearity check at a random point
  matrix rc = mnormal(k, 1)
  evw_c = zeros(K, 1)
  evw_c[cpos] = rc
  errorif(abs((@ex) - (Rm[j,] * rc + f0)) &gt; 1e-8 * (1 + abs(f0)), sprintf(&quot;Restriction '%s' is not linear&quot;, R[j]))
  q[j] = -f0
endloop
matrix dev = Rm * b.coeff - q
scalar W = qform(dev', inv(qform(Rm, b.vcv)))
bundle w
w.restr = restr
w.chi2 = W
w.chi2p = pvalue(X, J, W)
w.F = W / J
w.Fp = pvalue(F, J, n - k, w.F)
w.df1 = J
w.df2 = n - k
w.R = Rm
w.q = q
if !quiet
  printf &quot;\nWald Test:\nEquation: %s\n\n&quot;, b.spec
  printf &quot;%-20s%14s%14s%14s\n&quot;, &quot;Test Statistic&quot;, &quot;Value&quot;, &quot;df&quot;, &quot;Probability&quot;
  printf &quot;%-20s%14.6f%14s%14.4f\n&quot;, &quot;F-statistic&quot;, w.F, sprintf(&quot;(%d, %d)&quot;, J, n - k), w.Fp
  printf &quot;%-20s%14.6f%14d%14.4f\n&quot;, &quot;Chi-square&quot;, w.chi2, J, w.chi2p
  printf &quot;\nNull Hypothesis: %s\n\n&quot;, toupper(restr)
endif
return w
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_diag" type="bundle">
 <params count="3">
  <param name="b" type="bundle">
<description>ev_ls result</description>
  </param>
  <param name="nlags" type="int" min="1" default="2">
<description>Serial correlation LM nlags</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
 </params>
<code>errorif(!inbundle(b, &quot;uhat&quot;), &quot;First argument must be an ev_ls result&quot;)
matrix u = b.uhat
matrix Xm = b.X
scalar n = rows(u)
scalar k = cols(Xm)
bundle r

# Jarque-Bera
matrix uc = u - meanc(u)
scalar m2 = meanc(uc.^2)
r.skew = meanc(uc.^3) / m2^1.5
r.kurt = meanc(uc.^4) / m2^2
r.jb = n / 6 * (r.skew^2 + (r.kurt - 3)^2 / 4)
r.jbp = pvalue(X, 2, r.jb)

# Breusch-Godfrey (presample residuals set to zero, as EViews)
matrix UL = zeros(n, nlags)
loop j = 1..nlags
  UL[j+1:n, j] = u[1:n-j]
endloop
scalar ssr0 = 0
scalar df0 = 0
scalar ssr1 = 0
scalar df1 = 0
scalar r2 = ev__fit(u, Xm ~ UL, &amp;ssr1, &amp;df1)
ev__fit(u, Xm, &amp;ssr0, &amp;df0)
r.bg_lags = nlags
r.bg_obsr2 = n * r2
r.bg_chi2p = pvalue(X, nlags, r.bg_obsr2)
r.bg_F = ((ssr0 - ssr1) / nlags) / (ssr1 / (n - df1))
r.bg_Fp = pvalue(F, nlags, n - df1, r.bg_F)

# White test with cross terms
matrix nc = selifc(Xm, sdc(Xm) .&gt; 1e-12)
matrix Z = ones(n, 1) ~ nc
loop i = 1..cols(nc)
  loop j = i..cols(nc)
    Z ~= nc[,i] .* nc[,j]
  endloop
endloop
scalar ssrw = 0
scalar dfw = 0
scalar r2w = ev__fit(u.^2, Z, &amp;ssrw, &amp;dfw)
scalar m = dfw - 1
r.white_obsr2 = n * r2w
r.white_df = m
r.white_chi2p = pvalue(X, m, r.white_obsr2)
r.white_F = (r2w / m) / ((1 - r2w) / (n - dfw))
r.white_Fp = pvalue(F, m, n - dfw, r.white_F)

if !quiet
  printf &quot;\nResidual Diagnostics\nEquation: %s\n&quot;, b.spec
  ev__line(70)
  printf &quot;Normality: Jarque-Bera\n&quot;
  printf &quot;  %-26s%12.6f    Prob.%21.4f\n&quot;, &quot;Jarque-Bera&quot;, r.jb, r.jbp
  printf &quot;  %-26s%12.6f    %-14s%12.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Skewness&quot;, r.skew, &quot;Kurtosis&quot;, r.kurt
  ev__line(70)
  printf &quot;Breusch-Godfrey Serial Correlation LM Test (%d lags)\n&quot;, nlags
  printf &quot;  %-26s%12.6f    %-18s%8.4f\n&quot;, &quot;F-statistic&quot;, r.bg_F, sprintf(&quot;Prob. F(%d,%d)&quot;, nlags, n - df1), r.bg_Fp
  printf &quot;  %-26s%12.6f    %-18s%8.4f\n&quot;, &quot;Obs*R-squared&quot;, r.bg_obsr2, sprintf(&quot;Prob. Chi-Square(%d)&quot;, nlags), r.bg_chi2p
  ev__line(70)
  printf &quot;Heteroskedasticity Test: White (with cross terms)\n&quot;
  printf &quot;  %-26s%12.6f    %-18s%8.4f\n&quot;, &quot;F-statistic&quot;, r.white_F, sprintf(&quot;Prob. F(%d,%d)&quot;, m, n - dfw), r.white_Fp
  printf &quot;  %-26s%12.6f    %-18s%8.4f\n&quot;, &quot;Obs*R-squared&quot;, r.white_obsr2, sprintf(&quot;Prob. Chi-Square(%d)&quot;, m), r.white_chi2p
  ev__line(70)
endif
return r
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_freeze" type="void">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="b" type="bundle">
<description>ev_ls result</description>
  </param>
  <param name="fname" type="string">
<description>Output file: .txt, .csv, .tex or .html</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code>errorif(!inbundle(b, &quot;coeff&quot;), &quot;First argument must be an ev_ls result&quot;)
string ext = tolower(regsub(fname, &quot;.*\.&quot;, &quot;&quot;))
if ext == &quot;txt&quot;
  outfile @fname --quiet
    ev_print(&amp;b)
  end outfile
elif ext == &quot;csv&quot;
  outfile @fname --quiet
    printf &quot;Variable,Coefficient,Std. Error,t-Statistic,Prob.\n&quot;
    loop i = 1..b.k
      printf &quot;\&quot;%s\&quot;,%.10g,%.10g,%.10g,%.10g\n&quot;, b.labels[i], b.coeff[i], b.stderr[i], b.tstat[i], b.pval[i]
    endloop
    printf &quot;\nR-squared,%.10g\nAdjusted R-squared,%.10g\nS.E. of regression,%.10g\n&quot;, b.rsq, b.adjrsq, b.sigma
    printf &quot;Sum squared resid,%.10g\nLog likelihood,%.10g\nDurbin-Watson stat,%.10g\n&quot;, b.ssr, b.lnl, b.dw
    printf &quot;Akaike info criterion,%.10g\nSchwarz criterion,%.10g\nIncluded observations,%d\n&quot;, b.aic, b.sc, b.T
  end outfile
elif ext == &quot;tex&quot;
  outfile @fname --quiet
    printf &quot;\\begin{tabular}{lrrrr}\n\\hline\n&quot;
    printf &quot;Variable &amp; Coefficient &amp; Std. Error &amp; t-Statistic &amp; Prob. \\\\\n\\hline\n&quot;
    loop i = 1..b.k
      printf &quot;%s &amp; %.6f &amp; %.6f &amp; %.4f &amp; %.4f \\\\\n&quot;, b.labels[i], b.coeff[i], b.stderr[i], b.tstat[i], b.pval[i]
    endloop
    printf &quot;\\hline\nR-squared &amp; %.6f &amp; &amp; Durbin-Watson &amp; %.4f \\\\\n&quot;, b.rsq, b.dw
    printf &quot;Observations &amp; %d &amp; &amp; S.E. of regression &amp; %.6f \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{tabular}\n&quot;, b.T, b.sigma
  end outfile
elif ext == &quot;html&quot;
  outfile @fname --quiet
    printf &quot;&lt;table border=\&quot;1\&quot; cellpadding=\&quot;4\&quot;&gt;\n&lt;caption&gt;Dependent Variable: %s (%s)&lt;/caption&gt;\n&quot;, b.depvar, b.sample
    printf &quot;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;Variable&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Coefficient&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Std. Error&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;t-Statistic&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Prob.&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n&quot;
    loop i = 1..b.k
      printf &quot;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;%s&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;%.6f&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;%.6f&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;%.4f&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;%.4f&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n&quot;, b.labels[i], b.coeff[i], b.stderr[i], b.tstat[i], b.pval[i]
    endloop
    printf &quot;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;R-squared&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;%.6f&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan=\&quot;2\&quot;&gt;Durbin-Watson stat&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;%.4f&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n&quot;, b.rsq, b.dw
    printf &quot;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Observations&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;%d&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan=\&quot;2\&quot;&gt;S.E. of regression&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;%.6f&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;/table&gt;\n&quot;, b.T, b.sigma
  end outfile
else
  funcerr &quot;Unsupported extension: use .txt, .csv, .tex or .html&quot;
endif
printf &quot;Frozen table written to %s\n&quot;, fname
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_trend" type="series">
<code>series t = obs - 1
return t
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_seas" type="series">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="k" type="int" min="1"/>
 </params>
<code>errorif(k &gt; $pd, sprintf(&quot;Season %d exceeds data frequency %d&quot;, k, $pd))
series s = $obsminor == k
return s
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_pch" type="series">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="x" type="series"/>
 </params>
<code>return x / x(-1) - 1
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_pc" type="series">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="x" type="series"/>
 </params>
<code>return 100 * (x / x(-1) - 1)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_pchy" type="series">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="x" type="series"/>
 </params>
<code>return x / x(-$pd) - 1
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_pcy" type="series">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="x" type="series"/>
 </params>
<code>return 100 * (x / x(-$pd) - 1)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_movav" type="series">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="x" type="series"/>
  <param name="n" type="int" min="1"/>
 </params>
<code>if n == 1
  return x
endif
return movavg(x, n)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_movsum" type="series">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="x" type="series"/>
  <param name="n" type="int" min="1"/>
 </params>
<code>if n == 1
  return x
endif
return n * movavg(x, n)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_mean" type="scalar">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="x" type="series"/>
 </params>
<code>return mean(x)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_stdev" type="scalar">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="x" type="series"/>
 </params>
<code># sample standard deviation (n-1), as EViews
return sd(x)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_var" type="scalar">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="x" type="series"/>
 </params>
<code># population variance (divisor n), as EViews
return sd(x)^2 * (nobs(x) - 1) / nobs(x)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_obs" type="scalar">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="x" type="series"/>
 </params>
<code>return nobs(x)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_elem" type="scalar">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="x" type="series"/>
  <param name="ob" type="string">
<description>Observation, e.g. 1990:1</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code>return x[obsnum(ob)]
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_fit" type="series">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="b" type="bundle">
<description>ev_ls result</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code>errorif(!inbundle(b, &quot;tobs&quot;), &quot;Not an ev_ls result (or estimated with an older EViewsCompat)&quot;)
return ev__toseries(b.yhat, b.tobs)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_resid" type="series">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="b" type="bundle">
<description>ev_ls result</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code>errorif(!inbundle(b, &quot;tobs&quot;), &quot;Not an ev_ls result (or estimated with an older EViewsCompat)&quot;)
return ev__toseries(b.uhat, b.tobs)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_forecast" type="bundle">
 <params count="5">
  <param name="b" type="bundle">
<description>ev_ls result</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list">
<description>Series used (e.g. dataset)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="dynamic" type="bool" default="1">
<description>Dynamic (1) or static (0)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
  <param name="level" type="bool" default="0">
<description>Report the level of the dependent variable, e.g. Y for dlog(Y)</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code>errorif(!inbundle(b, &quot;coeff&quot;), &quot;First argument must be an equation (ev_ls result)&quot;)
string kind = inbundle(b, &quot;kind&quot;) ? b.kind : &quot;ls&quot;
string dep = kind == &quot;nls&quot; ? b.lhs : strsplit(b.spec)[1]
string base = &quot;&quot;
scalar form = ev__depform(dep, &amp;base, vars)
series evf_y = ev_gen(dep, vars)
matrix y = {evf_y}
series evf_o = obs
matrix tobs = {evf_o}
scalar T = rows(y)
scalar k = b.k
matrix beta = b.coeff
scalar s2 = b.sigma^2

# actual level and its previous value (pre-sample visible through the lag)
matrix Ylev = mshape(NA, T, 1)
matrix Yprev = mshape(NA, T, 1)
if form &gt;= 0
  string e1 = &quot;vars.&quot; ~ base
  string e2 = &quot;vars.&quot; ~ base ~ &quot;(-1)&quot;
  series evf_L = @e1
  series evf_Lp = @e2
  Ylev = {evf_L}
  Yprev = {evf_Lp}
endif

# how the right-hand side is evaluated
strings tok = array(0)
matrix X = {}
matrix usesY = {}
if kind == &quot;arma&quot;
  return ev__fc_arma(b, vars, dynamic, quiet, level, form, base)
elif kind == &quot;nls&quot;
  loop j = 1..k
    string pn = sprintf(&quot;evn_c%d&quot;, b.cidx[j])
    scalar @pn = beta[j]
  endloop
  string rhx = ev__prep(b.rhs, vars)
  series evf_r0 = @rhx
  matrix r0 = {evf_r0}
  # gradient for the coefficient part of the S.E.
  matrix J = {}
  loop j = 1..k
    string pn = sprintf(&quot;evn_c%d&quot;, b.cidx[j])
    scalar h = 1e-6 * (1 + abs(beta[j]))
    scalar @pn = beta[j] + h
    series evf_rp = @rhx
    scalar @pn = beta[j]
    J ~= ({evf_rp} - r0) / h
  endloop
else
  tok = strsplit(b.spec)
  loop i = 2..nelem(tok)
    if tolower(tok[i]) == &quot;c&quot;
      series evf_r = 1
    else
      series evf_r = ev_gen(tok[i], vars)
    endif
    X ~= {evf_r}
    scalar u_ = form &gt;= 0 &amp;&amp; regsub(tok[i], &quot;(?i)(?&lt;![A-Za-z0-9_])&quot; ~ base ~ &quot;(?![A-Za-z0-9_])&quot;, &quot;#&quot;) != tok[i]
    usesY ~= u_
  endloop
  errorif(cols(X) != k, &quot;Could not rebuild the regressors of the equation&quot;)
endif

# AR terms in the dependent variable -&gt; psi weights for multi-step S.E.
matrix phi = zeros(1, 24)
scalar dyn_ok = dynamic &amp;&amp; form &gt;= 0
if kind == &quot;ls&quot; &amp;&amp; form &gt;= 0
  string dl = tolower(regsub(dep, &quot;\s&quot;, &quot;&quot;))
  loop L = 1..24
    string cand = regsub(dl, &quot;(?&lt;![a-z0-9_])&quot; ~ tolower(base) ~ &quot;(?![a-z0-9_])&quot;, tolower(base) ~ sprintf(&quot;(-%d)&quot;, L))
    if form == 0
      cand = tolower(base) ~ sprintf(&quot;(-%d)&quot;, L)
    endif
    loop i = 2..nelem(tok)
      if tolower(regsub(tok[i], &quot;\s&quot;, &quot;&quot;)) == cand
        phi[L] = beta[i-1]
      endif
    endloop
  endloop
endif
matrix psi = zeros(T, 1)
psi[1] = 1
loop j = 2..T
  loop L = 1..min(24, j - 1)
    psi[j] += phi[L] * psi[j - L]
  endloop
endloop
matrix psiC = cum(psi)

# step through the forecast sample
matrix yf = mshape(NA, T, 1)
matrix se = mshape(NA, T, 1)
matrix yfl = mshape(NA, T, 1)
matrix sel = mshape(NA, T, 1)
series evf_dlt = 0          # forecast minus actual level (dynamic forecasts)
loop t = 1..T
  scalar v = NA
  scalar st = tobs[t]
  matrix g = {}
  if kind == &quot;nls&quot;
    v = r0[t]
    if dyn_ok &amp;&amp; t &gt; 1
      series evf_rr = ev__gen2(b.rhs, vars, base, evf_dlt)
      v = evf_rr[st]
    endif
    g = J[t,]
  else
    matrix x = X[t,]
    if dyn_ok &amp;&amp; t &gt; 1
      loop i = 1..cols(x)
        if usesY[i]
          series evf_rc = ev__gen2(tok[i+1], vars, base, evf_dlt)
          if ok(evf_rc[st])
            x[i] = evf_rc[st]
          endif
        endif
      endloop
    endif
    if sum(!ok(x)) == 0
      v = x * beta
    endif
    g = x
  endif
  if !ok(v)
    continue
  endif
  yf[t] = v
  scalar h = dynamic ? t : 1
  # static: innovation and coefficient uncertainty; dynamic: innovation
  # uncertainty propagated through the lags of the dependent variable (as gretl)
  scalar cvar = (!dynamic &amp;&amp; sum(!ok(g)) == 0) ? qform(g, b.vcv) : 0
  se[t] = sqrt(s2 * sumc(psi[1:h].^2) + cvar)
  if form &gt;= 0
    scalar prev = (t &gt; 1 &amp;&amp; dynamic &amp;&amp; ok(yfl[t-1])) ? yfl[t-1] : Yprev[t]
    if form == 0
      yfl[t] = v
      sel[t] = se[t]
    elif form == 1
      yfl[t] = exp(v)
      sel[t] = yfl[t] * se[t]
    elif form == 2
      yfl[t] = prev + v
      sel[t] = dynamic ? sqrt(s2 * sumc(psiC[1:h].^2)) : se[t]
    else
      yfl[t] = prev * exp(v)
      sel[t] = yfl[t] * (dynamic ? sqrt(s2 * sumc(psiC[1:h].^2)) : se[t])
    endif
    if dyn_ok
      evf_dlt[st] = yfl[t] - Ylev[t]
    endif
  endif
endloop
return ev__fc_finish(b, dep, base, form, dynamic, level, y, yf, se, Ylev, yfl, sel, tobs, quiet, kind == &quot;nls&quot; &amp;&amp; dynamic)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_fprint" type="void">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="f" type="bundleref"/>
 </params>
<code>string nm = f.level ? f.base : f.depvar
printf &quot;\nForecast: %sF\nActual: %s\n&quot;, f.level ? f.base : f.depvar, nm
printf &quot;Forecast sample: %s\n&quot;, f.sample
printf &quot;Method: %s\n&quot;, f.dynamic ? &quot;Dynamic forecast&quot; : &quot;Static forecast&quot;
printf &quot;Included observations: %d\n&quot;, f.nobs
if f.nobs &gt; 0
  printf &quot;%-34s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Root Mean Squared Error&quot;, f.rmse
  printf &quot;%-34s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Mean Absolute Error&quot;, f.mae
  printf &quot;%-34s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Mean Abs. Percent Error&quot;, f.mape
  printf &quot;%-34s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Theil Inequality Coef.&quot;, f.theil
  printf &quot;%-34s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;     Bias Proportion&quot;, f.bias_prop
  printf &quot;%-34s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;     Variance Proportion&quot;, f.var_prop
  printf &quot;%-34s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;     Covariance Proportion&quot;, f.cov_prop
endif
if f.se_note != &quot;&quot;
  printf &quot;Note: %s\n&quot;, f.se_note
endif
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_fcast_series" type="series">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="f" type="bundle">
<description>ev_forecast result</description>
  </param>
  <param name="level" type="bool" default="0">
<description>Level of the dependent variable</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code>return ev__toseries(level ? f.yfl : f.yf, f.tobs)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_fcast_se" type="series">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="f" type="bundle">
<description>ev_forecast result</description>
  </param>
  <param name="level" type="bool" default="0">
<description>Level of the dependent variable</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code>return ev__toseries(level ? f.sel : f.se, f.tobs)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_fplot" type="void">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="f" type="bundleref"/>
  <param name="fname" type="string" optional="true"/>
 </params>
<code># forecast with +/- 2 S.E. bands, and the actual series
matrix p = f.level ? f.yfl : f.yf
matrix s = f.level ? f.sel : f.se
matrix a = f.level ? f.actual_level : f.actual
matrix M = p ~ (p + 2 * s) ~ (p - 2 * s) ~ a
cnameset(M, defarray(&quot;Forecast&quot;, &quot;+2 S.E.&quot;, &quot;-2 S.E.&quot;, &quot;Actual&quot;))
string out = exists(fname) ? fname : &quot;display&quot;
gnuplot 1 2 3 4 --matrix=M --time-series --with-lines --single-yaxis --output=&quot;@out&quot; {set title &quot;Forecast with +/- 2 S.E.&quot;;}
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_depbase" type="string">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="b" type="bundle">
<description>Equation (ev_ls result)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list">
<description>Series used (e.g. dataset)</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code># the series Y when the dependent variable is log(Y), d(Y) or dlog(Y); &quot;&quot; otherwise
string dep = inbundle(b, &quot;lhs&quot;) ? b.lhs : strsplit(b.spec)[1]
string base = &quot;&quot;
scalar f = ev__depform(dep, &amp;base, vars)
return f &gt; 0 ? base : &quot;&quot;
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_varest" type="bundle">
 <params count="4">
  <param name="spec" type="string">
<description>Lag pairs, endogenous, then exogenous after the at-sign</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list">
<description>Series used (e.g. dataset)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
  <param name="names" type="string" optional="true">
<description>Display names for the variables, space separated</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code># Plain series names are used directly, so lags reach before the sample start
# as in gretl's var. Expressions are evaluated inside this function, where
# pre-sample values are not available: create them as series first if that matters.
string AT = &quot;@&quot;
strings LB = exists(names) ? strsplit(names) : array(0)
scalar nexpr = 0
strings parts = strsplit(spec, AT)
errorif(nelem(parts) &gt; 2, &quot;Use the at-sign once, before the exogenous variables&quot;)
strings L = strsplit(parts[1])
# leading integers are lag pairs
matrix lagv = {}
scalar i0 = 1
loop while i0 + 1 &lt;= nelem(L) &amp;&amp; regsub(L[i0], &quot;^[0-9]+$&quot;, &quot;&quot;) == &quot;&quot; &amp;&amp; regsub(L[i0+1], &quot;^[0-9]+$&quot;, &quot;&quot;) == &quot;&quot;
  scalar a = atof(L[i0])
  scalar z = atof(L[i0+1])
  errorif(a &lt; 1 || z &lt; a, &quot;Lag pairs must be like 1 2 (from 1 to 2)&quot;)
  lagv ~= seq(a, z)
  i0 += 2
endloop
errorif(cols(lagv) == 0, &quot;Start the specification with lag pairs, e.g. 1 2&quot;)
lagv = values(lagv')'
errorif(nelem(L) - i0 + 1 &lt; 1, &quot;No endogenous variables&quot;)
list Y = null
strings ylab = array(0)
strings ytok = array(0)
strings xtok = array(0)
loop i = i0..nelem(L)
  matrix pp = instrings(varnames(vars), L[i])
  if rows(pp) &gt; 0
    list Y += vars[pp[1]]
  else
    string v = sprintf(&quot;evv_y%d&quot;, i)
    series @v = ev_gen(L[i], vars)
    list Y += @v
    nexpr++
  endif
  scalar li = nelem(ytok) + 1
  ylab += nelem(LB) &gt;= li ? toupper(LB[li]) : toupper(L[i])
  ytok += L[i]
endloop
list X = null
strings xlab = array(0)
scalar hasc = nelem(parts) == 1   # no exogenous part: constant by default
if nelem(parts) == 2
  strings R = strsplit(parts[2])
  loop i = 1..nelem(R)
    if tolower(R[i]) == &quot;c&quot;
      hasc = 1
    else
      matrix pp = instrings(varnames(vars), R[i])
      if rows(pp) &gt; 0
        list X += vars[pp[1]]
      else
        string v = sprintf(&quot;evv_x%d&quot;, i)
        series @v = ev_gen(R[i], vars)
        list X += @v
        nexpr++
      endif
      scalar li = nelem(ytok) + nelem(xtok) + 1
      xlab += nelem(LB) &gt;= li ? toupper(LB[li]) : toupper(R[i])
      xtok += R[i]
    endif
  endloop
endif
scalar n0 = $nobs
if nelem(X) &gt; 0
  if hasc
    var lagv Y ; X --silent
  else
    var lagv Y ; X --silent --nc
  endif
else
  if hasc
    var lagv Y --silent
  else
    var lagv Y --silent --nc
  endif
endif
bundle sys = $system
if nexpr &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; !quiet
  printf &quot;Note: %d variable(s) given as expressions lose their pre-sample lags;\n&quot;, nexpr
  printf &quot;      create them as series first to use the full sample.\n&quot;
endif

bundle b
b.spec = spec
b.sys = sys
b.ylab = ylab
b.xlab = xlab
b.ytok = ytok
b.xtok = xtok
b.lags = lagv
b.hasc = hasc
b.n = nelem(Y)
b.T = sys.T
b.k = sys.ncoeff
b.coeff = sys.coeff
b.adjusted = sys.T &lt; n0
b.sample = sprintf(&quot;%s %s&quot;, obslabel(sys.t1), obslabel(sys.t2))
b.estdate = strftime($now[1], &quot;%m/%d/%y   Time: %H:%M&quot;)
# coefficient labels in gretl's order: const, lagv of each endogenous, exogenous
strings clab = array(0)
if hasc
  clab += &quot;C&quot;
endif
loop j = 1..b.n
  loop l = 1..cols(lagv)
    clab += sprintf(&quot;%s(-%d)&quot;, ylab[j], lagv[l])
  endloop
endloop
loop j = 1..nelem(xlab)
  clab += xlab[j]
endloop
errorif(nelem(clab) != b.k, &quot;Internal error: coefficient labels do not match&quot;)
b.clab = clab

# per-equation statistics
scalar T = b.T
scalar k = b.k
matrix E = sys.uhat
matrix Ym = sys.Y
matrix ssr = sumc(E.^2)
matrix dev = Ym .- meanc(Ym)
matrix sst = sumc(dev.^2)
b.ssr = ssr
b.rsq = 1 - ssr ./ sst
b.adjrsq = 1 - (1 - b.rsq) * (T - 1) / (T - k)
b.seeq = sqrt(ssr / (T - k))
b.se = sqrt(diag(sys.xtxinv)) * b.seeq       # k x n
b.tstat = b.coeff ./ b.se
b.Fstat = hasc ? (b.rsq / (k - 1)) ./ ((1 - b.rsq) / (T - k)) : mshape(NA, 1, b.n)
b.lnl_eq = -T / 2 * (1 + log(2 * $pi) + log(ssr / T))
b.aic_eq = -2 * b.lnl_eq / T + 2 * k / T
b.sc_eq = -2 * b.lnl_eq / T + k * log(T) / T
b.meany = meanc(Ym)
b.sdy = sqrt(sst / (T - 1))
matrix S = E'E / T
b.det_adj = det(E'E / (T - k))
b.det = det(S)
b.lnl = sys.lnl
b.aic = -2 * b.lnl / T + 2 * b.n * k / T
b.sc = -2 * b.lnl / T + b.n * k * log(T) / T
if !quiet
  ev_varprint(&amp;b)
endif
return b
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_varprint" type="void">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="b" type="bundleref"/>
 </params>
<code>errorif(!inbundle(b, &quot;sys&quot;), &quot;Not an ev_varest result&quot;)
scalar n = b.n
printf &quot;\nVector Autoregression Estimates\nDate: %s\n&quot;, b.estdate
printf &quot;Sample%s: %s\n&quot;, b.adjusted ? &quot; (adjusted)&quot; : &quot;&quot;, b.sample
printf &quot;Included observations: %d%s\n&quot;, b.T, b.adjusted ? &quot; after adjustments&quot; : &quot;&quot;
printf &quot;Standard errors in ( ) &amp; t-statistics in [ ]\n\n&quot;
scalar w = 22 + 16 * n
ev__line(w)
printf &quot;%-22s&quot;, &quot;&quot;
loop j = 1..n
  printf &quot;%16s&quot;, b.ylab[j]
endloop
printf &quot;\n&quot;
ev__line(w)
# EViews order: lags first, then C, then exogenous
matrix ord = {}
scalar c0 = b.hasc ? 2 : 1
scalar nl = b.n * cols(b.lags)
ord ~= seq(c0, c0 + nl - 1)
if b.hasc
  ord ~= 1
endif
if b.k &gt; nl + b.hasc
  ord ~= seq(c0 + nl, b.k)
endif
loop r = 1..cols(ord)
  scalar i = ord[r]
  printf &quot;%-22s&quot;, b.clab[i]
  loop j = 1..n
    printf &quot;%16.6f&quot;, b.coeff[i,j]
  endloop
  printf &quot;\n%-22s&quot;, &quot;&quot;
  loop j = 1..n
    printf &quot;%16s&quot;, sprintf(&quot;(%.5f)&quot;, b.se[i,j])
  endloop
  printf &quot;\n%-22s&quot;, &quot;&quot;
  loop j = 1..n
    printf &quot;%16s&quot;, sprintf(&quot;[%.5f]&quot;, b.tstat[i,j])
  endloop
  printf &quot;\n\n&quot;
endloop
ev__line(w)
strings nm = defarray(&quot;R-squared&quot;, &quot;Adj. R-squared&quot;, &quot;Sum sq. resids&quot;, &quot;S.E. equation&quot;, &quot;F-statistic&quot;, &quot;Log likelihood&quot;, &quot;Akaike AIC&quot;, &quot;Schwarz SC&quot;, &quot;Mean dependent&quot;, &quot;S.D. dependent&quot;)
matrices st = defarray(b.rsq, b.adjrsq, b.ssr, b.seeq, b.Fstat, b.lnl_eq, b.aic_eq, b.sc_eq, b.meany, b.sdy)
loop r = 1..nelem(nm)
  printf &quot;%-22s&quot;, nm[r]
  matrix v = st[r]
  loop j = 1..n
    printf &quot;%16.6f&quot;, v[j]
  endloop
  printf &quot;\n&quot;
endloop
ev__line(w)
printf &quot;%-44s%16.6g\n&quot;, &quot;Determinant resid covariance (dof adj.)&quot;, b.det_adj
printf &quot;%-44s%16.6g\n&quot;, &quot;Determinant resid covariance&quot;, b.det
printf &quot;%-44s%16.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Log likelihood&quot;, b.lnl
printf &quot;%-44s%16.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Akaike information criterion&quot;, b.aic
printf &quot;%-44s%16.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Schwarz criterion&quot;, b.sc
ev__line(w)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_vargranger" type="matrix">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="b" type="bundle">
<description>ev_varest result</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
 </params>
<code># VAR Granger causality / block exogeneity Wald tests (chi-square), EViews style.
# Returns rows: dependent j, excluded i (0 = all), chi2, df, p
scalar n = b.n
scalar p = cols(b.lags)
scalar c0 = b.hasc ? 2 : 1
matrix V0 = b.sys.xtxinv
matrix out = {}
if !quiet
  printf &quot;\nVAR Granger Causality/Block Exogeneity Wald Tests\nSample: %s\nIncluded observations: %d\n&quot;, b.sample, b.T
endif
loop j = 1..n
  if !quiet
    printf &quot;\nDependent variable: %s\n\n%-22s%14s%8s%10s\n&quot;, b.ylab[j], &quot;Excluded&quot;, &quot;Chi-sq&quot;, &quot;df&quot;, &quot;Prob.&quot;
  endif
  scalar s2 = b.seeq[j]^2
  matrix allidx = {}
  loop i = 1..n
    if i != j
      matrix idx = seq(c0 + (i - 1) * p, c0 + i * p - 1)
      allidx ~= idx
      matrix bb = b.coeff[idx, j]
      scalar W = qform(bb', inv(s2 * V0[idx, idx]))
      out |= {j, i, W, p, pvalue(X, p, W)}
      if !quiet
        printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f%8d%10.4f\n&quot;, b.ylab[i], W, p, pvalue(X, p, W)
      endif
    endif
  endloop
  if n &gt; 1
    matrix bb = b.coeff[allidx, j]
    scalar W = qform(bb', inv(s2 * V0[allidx, allidx]))
    out |= {j, 0, W, cols(allidx), pvalue(X, cols(allidx), W)}
    if !quiet
      printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f%8d%10.4f\n&quot;, &quot;All&quot;, W, cols(allidx), pvalue(X, cols(allidx), W)
    endif
  endif
endloop
return out
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_varirf" type="matrix">
 <params count="3">
  <param name="b" type="bundle">
<description>ev_varest result</description>
  </param>
  <param name="h" type="int" min="1" default="10">
<description>Horizon</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
 </params>
<code># Impulse responses (Cholesky, one S.D. innovations). Column (s-1)*n+t holds
# the response of variable t to a shock in variable s.
scalar n = b.n
set horizon h
matrix R = {}
if inbundle(b, &quot;svarS&quot;)
  # structural shocks: responses Psi_j * inverse(A) * B
  matrix Psi = ev__psi(b.sys, n, h)
  matrix Rs = zeros(h, n * n)
  loop i = 1..h
    matrix Ri = Psi[, (i - 1) * n + 1:i * n] * b.svarS
    loop s = 1..n
      loop t = 1..n
        Rs[i, (s - 1) * n + t] = Ri[t, s]
      endloop
    endloop
  endloop
  R = Rs
else
  loop s = 1..n
    loop t = 1..n
      matrix r = irf(t, s, 0, b.sys)
      R ~= r[1:h, 1]
    endloop
  endloop
endif
if !quiet
  loop t = 1..n
    printf &quot;\nResponse of %s:\n%-8s&quot;, b.ylab[t], &quot;Period&quot;
    loop s = 1..n
      printf &quot;%16s&quot;, b.ylab[s]
    endloop
    printf &quot;\n&quot;
    loop i = 1..h
      printf &quot;%-8d&quot;, i
      loop s = 1..n
        printf &quot;%16.6f&quot;, R[i, (s - 1) * n + t]
      endloop
      printf &quot;\n&quot;
    endloop
  endloop
  if inbundle(b, &quot;svarS&quot;)
    printf &quot;\nStructural decomposition (%s)\n&quot;, b.svar_type
  else
    printf &quot;\nCholesky ordering: &quot;
    loop s = 1..n
      printf &quot;%s &quot;, b.ylab[s]
    endloop
    printf &quot;\n&quot;
  endif
endif
return R
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_varirfplot" type="void">
 <params count="3">
  <param name="b" type="bundle">
<description>ev_varest result</description>
  </param>
  <param name="h" type="int" min="1" default="10"/>
  <param name="fname" type="string" optional="true"/>
 </params>
<code># grid of impulse-response graphs: row = responding variable, column = shock
matrix R = ev_varirf(b, h, 1)
scalar n = b.n
strings plots = array(0)
loop t = 1..n
  loop s = 1..n
    matrix M = R[, (s - 1) * n + t]
    string ttl = sprintf(&quot;Response of %s to %s&quot;, b.ylab[t], b.ylab[s])
    string buf = &quot;&quot;
    gnuplot 1 --matrix=M --time-series --with-lines --outbuf=buf {set title &quot;@ttl&quot; font &quot;,9&quot;; unset key; set xlabel &quot;&quot;; set ylabel &quot;&quot;; set xzeroaxis lt 1 lc rgb &quot;#c0392b&quot;;}
    plots += buf
  endloop
endloop
string out = exists(fname) ? fname : &quot;display&quot;
gridplot plots --rows=n --width=900 --height=700 --fontsize=9 --output=&quot;@out&quot;
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_vardecomp" type="matrix">
 <params count="3">
  <param name="b" type="bundle">
<description>ev_varest result</description>
  </param>
  <param name="h" type="int" min="1" default="10"/>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
 </params>
<code># Variance decomposition in percent; block t holds rows 1..h for variable t
scalar n = b.n
set horizon h
matrix D = {}
if inbundle(b, &quot;svarS&quot;)
  matrix Rr = ev_varirf(b, h, 1)
  loop t = 1..n
    matrix c = {}
    loop s = 1..n
      c ~= cum(Rr[, (s - 1) * n + t].^2)
    endloop
    D |= 100 * c ./ sumr(c)
  endloop
else
  loop t = 1..n
    matrix d = fevd(t, 0, b.sys)
    D |= 100 * d[1:h, 1:n]
  endloop
endif
if !quiet
  matrix R = ev_varirf(b, h, 1)
  loop t = 1..n
    printf &quot;\nVariance Decomposition of %s:\n%-8s%14s&quot;, b.ylab[t], &quot;Period&quot;, &quot;S.E.&quot;
    loop s = 1..n
      printf &quot;%14s&quot;, b.ylab[s]
    endloop
    printf &quot;\n&quot;
    loop i = 1..h
      scalar v = 0
      loop s = 1..n
        v += sumc(R[1:i, (s - 1) * n + t].^2)
      endloop
      printf &quot;%-8d%14.6f&quot;, i, sqrt(v)
      loop s = 1..n
        printf &quot;%14.4f&quot;, D[(t - 1) * h + i, s]
      endloop
      printf &quot;\n&quot;
    endloop
  endloop
  if inbundle(b, &quot;svarS&quot;)
    printf &quot;\nStructural decomposition (%s)\n&quot;, b.svar_type
  else
    printf &quot;\nCholesky ordering: &quot;
    loop s = 1..n
      printf &quot;%s &quot;, b.ylab[s]
    endloop
    printf &quot;\n&quot;
  endif
endif
return D
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_varlaglen" type="void">
 <params count="3">
  <param name="b" type="bundle">
<description>ev_varest result</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list">
<description>Series used (e.g. dataset)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="maxlag" type="int" min="1" default="8"/>
 </params>
<code># lag length criteria (gretl's var --lagselect)
list Y = null
loop i = 1..b.n
  string v = sprintf(&quot;evl_y%d&quot;, i)
  series @v = ev_gen(b.ytok[i], vars)
  list Y += @v
endloop
list X = null
loop i = 1..nelem(b.xtok)
  string v = sprintf(&quot;evl_x%d&quot;, i)
  series @v = ev_gen(b.xtok[i], vars)
  list X += @v
endloop
printf &quot;\nVAR Lag Order Selection Criteria\nEndogenous variables: &quot;
loop i = 1..b.n
  printf &quot;%s &quot;, b.ylab[i]
endloop
printf &quot;\n&quot;
if nelem(X) &gt; 0
  if b.hasc
    var maxlag Y ; X --lagselect
  else
    var maxlag Y ; X --lagselect --nc
  endif
elif b.hasc
  var maxlag Y --lagselect
else
  var maxlag Y --lagselect --nc
endif
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_varresid" type="series">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="b" type="bundle">
<description>ev_varest result</description>
  </param>
  <param name="i" type="int" min="1" default="1">
<description>Equation number</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code>matrix t = seq(b.sys.t1, b.sys.t2)'
return ev__toseries(b.sys.uhat[, i], t)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_nls" type="bundle">
 <params count="4">
  <param name="spec" type="string">
<description>Explicit equation, e.g. y = c(1) + c(2)*x^c(3)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list">
<description>Series used (e.g. dataset)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="cov" type="string" optional="true">
<description>ordinary, white or hac</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
 </params>
<code>string covt = exists(cov) ? tolower(cov) : &quot;ordinary&quot;
strings sides = strsplit(spec, &quot;=&quot;)
errorif(nelem(sides) != 2, &quot;Use exactly one '=' in an explicit equation&quot;)
string lhs = strstrip(sides[1])
string rhs0 = strstrip(sides[2])
string low = tolower(rhs0)
matrix cidx = {}
loop i = 1..99
  if instring(low, sprintf(&quot;c(%d)&quot;, i))
    cidx ~= i
  endif
endloop
errorif(cols(cidx) == 0, &quot;No coefficients c(1), c(2), ... in the equation&quot;)
string rhs = regsub(rhs0, &quot;(?i)(?&lt;![A-Za-z0-9_])c\(([0-9]+)\)&quot;, &quot;evn_c\1&quot;)
string rhx = ev__prep(rhs, vars)
series evn_y = ev_gen(lhs, vars)
string plist = &quot;&quot;
loop j = 1..cols(cidx)
  string pn = sprintf(&quot;evn_c%d&quot;, cidx[j])
  scalar @pn = 0
  plist ~= &quot; &quot; ~ pn
endloop
scalar n0 = $nobs
if covt == &quot;ordinary&quot;
  nls evn_y = @rhx
    params @plist
  end nls --quiet
else
  nls evn_y = @rhx
    params @plist
  end nls --quiet --robust
endif
bundle b
b.kind = &quot;nls&quot;
b.spec = spec
b.lhs = lhs
b.rhs = rhs
b.cidx = cidx
b.depvar = toupper(lhs)
b.method = &quot;Least Squares (Gauss-Newton / Marquardt steps)&quot;
b.eqline = regsub(toupper(lhs ~ &quot;=&quot; ~ rhs0), &quot;\s&quot;, &quot;&quot;)
strings lab = array(0)
loop j = 1..cols(cidx)
  lab += sprintf(&quot;C(%d)&quot;, cidx[j])
endloop
b.labels = lab
b.covtype = covt
b.coeff = $coeff
b.stderr = $stderr
b.vcv = $vcv
b.k = $ncoeff
b.lnl = $lnl
b.sigma = $sigma
b.adjusted = $T &lt; n0
b.estdate = strftime($now[1], &quot;%m/%d/%y   Time: %H:%M&quot;)
series evn_u = $uhat
series evn_f = $yhat
smpl ok(evn_u) --restrict
b.y = {evn_y}
b.uhat = {evn_u}
b.yhat = {evn_f}
series evn_o = obs
b.tobs = {evn_o}
b.sample = sprintf(&quot;%s %s&quot;, obslabel($t1), obslabel($t2))
# numerical gradient: used as regressors by the residual diagnostics
matrix J = {}
loop j = 1..b.k
  string pn = sprintf(&quot;evn_c%d&quot;, cidx[j])
  scalar h = 1e-6 * (1 + abs(b.coeff[j]))
  scalar @pn = b.coeff[j] + h
  series evn_fp = @rhx
  scalar @pn = b.coeff[j]
  J ~= ({evn_fp} - b.yhat) / h
endloop
b.X = J
ev__stats(&amp;b)
if !quiet
  ev_print(&amp;b)
endif
return b
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_arma" type="bundle">
 <params count="3">
  <param name="spec" type="string">
<description>Equation with ar(k) / ma(k) terms, e.g. y c x ar(1) ma(1)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list">
<description>Series used (e.g. dataset)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
 </params>
<code>strings tok = strsplit(spec)
series eva_y = ev_gen(tok[1], vars)
list evaX = null
strings xlab = array(0)
strings xtok = array(0)
scalar hasc = 0
matrix pl = {}
matrix ql = {}
loop i = 2..nelem(tok)
  string t = tolower(tok[i])
  if t == &quot;c&quot;
    hasc = 1
  elif regsub(t, &quot;^ar\([0-9]+\)$&quot;, &quot;&quot;) == &quot;&quot;
    pl ~= atof(regsub(t, &quot;[^0-9]&quot;, &quot;&quot;))
  elif regsub(t, &quot;^ma\([0-9]+\)$&quot;, &quot;&quot;) == &quot;&quot;
    ql ~= atof(regsub(t, &quot;[^0-9]&quot;, &quot;&quot;))
  else
    string v = sprintf(&quot;eva_x%d&quot;, i)
    series @v = ev_gen(tok[i], vars)
    list evaX += @v
    xlab += toupper(tok[i])
    xtok += tok[i]
  endif
endloop
if cols(pl)
  pl = values(pl')'
endif
if cols(ql)
  ql = values(ql')'
endif
matrix eva_pl = pl
matrix eva_ql = ql
string pa = cols(pl) ? &quot;eva_pl&quot; : &quot;0&quot;
string qa = cols(ql) ? &quot;eva_ql&quot; : &quot;0&quot;
scalar n0 = $nobs
# with regressors gretl needs the constant listed explicitly
if hasc &amp;&amp; nelem(evaX) &gt; 0
  arima @pa 0 @qa ; eva_y const evaX --quiet
elif hasc
  arima @pa 0 @qa ; eva_y --quiet
elif nelem(evaX) &gt; 0
  arima @pa 0 @qa ; eva_y evaX --quiet --nc
else
  arima @pa 0 @qa ; eva_y --quiet --nc
endif
matrix cf = $coeff
matrix sd = $stderr
bundle b
b.kind = &quot;arma&quot;
b.spec = spec
b.depvar = toupper(tok[1])
b.method = &quot;ARMA Maximum Likelihood (BFGS)&quot;
b.covtype = &quot;ordinary&quot;
b.hasc = hasc
b.pl = pl
b.ql = ql
b.xtok = xtok
# gretl order: const, AR, MA, regressors;  EViews order: C, regressors, AR, MA
scalar np = cols(pl)
scalar nq = cols(ql)
scalar nx = nelem(xtok)
strings lab = array(0)
if hasc
  lab += &quot;C&quot;
endif
loop i = 1..np
  lab += sprintf(&quot;AR(%d)&quot;, pl[i])
endloop
loop i = 1..nq
  lab += sprintf(&quot;MA(%d)&quot;, ql[i])
endloop
loop i = 1..nx
  lab += xlab[i]
endloop
b.labels = lab
matrix ord = {}
if hasc
  ord ~= 1
endif
scalar o1 = hasc + np + nq + 1
scalar o2 = hasc + np + nq + nx
scalar o3 = hasc + 1
scalar o4 = hasc + np + nq
if nx
  ord ~= seq(o1, o2)
endif
if np + nq
  ord ~= seq(o3, o4)
endif
b.order = ord
b.coeff = cf
b.stderr = sd
b.vcv = $vcv
b.k = rows(cf)
b.lnl = $lnl
scalar i1 = hasc + 1
scalar i2 = hasc + np
scalar i3 = hasc + np + 1
scalar i4 = hasc + np + nq
scalar i5 = hasc + np + nq + 1
scalar i6 = hasc + np + nq + nx
b.phi = np ? cf[i1:i2]' : {}
b.theta = nq ? cf[i3:i4]' : {}
matrix bb = {}
if hasc
  bb |= cf[1]
endif
if nx
  bb |= cf[i5:i6]
endif
b.beta = bb
b.adjusted = $T &lt; n0
b.estdate = strftime($now[1], &quot;%m/%d/%y   Time: %H:%M&quot;)
series eva_u = $uhat
series eva_f = $yhat
smpl ok(eva_u) --restrict
b.y = {eva_y}
b.uhat = {eva_u}
b.yhat = {eva_f}
series eva_o = obs
b.tobs = {eva_o}
b.sample = sprintf(&quot;%s %s&quot;, obslabel($t1), obslabel($t2))
matrix Xm = hasc ? ones(rows(b.y), 1) : {}
if nx
  Xm ~= {evaX}
endif
b.X = cols(Xm) ? Xm : ones(rows(b.y), 1)
b.ureg = cols(Xm) ? b.y - Xm * bb : b.y
scalar T = rows(b.y)
b.sigmasq = (b.uhat'b.uhat) / T
b.sigmasq_se = b.sigmasq * sqrt(2 / T)
b.sigma = sqrt((b.uhat'b.uhat) / (T - b.k))
if np
  b.ar_roots = ev__roots(b.phi, pl, 1)
endif
if nq
  b.ma_roots = ev__roots(b.theta, ql, -1)
endif
ev__stats(&amp;b)
if !quiet
  ev_print(&amp;b)
endif
return b
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_system" type="bundle">
 <params count="9">
  <param name="deps" type="strings">
<description>Dependent variable of each equation</description>
  </param>
  <param name="xspecs" type="strings">
<description>Regressors of each equation, e.g. c x1 x2</description>
  </param>
  <param name="cnums" type="strings">
<description>Coefficient numbers of each equation, e.g. 1 2 3</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list">
<description>Series used (e.g. dataset)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="method" type="string" optional="true">
<description>ls, sur, tsls or 3sls</description>
  </param>
  <param name="inst" type="string" optional="true">
<description>Instruments (a constant is added)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
  <param name="eqtext" type="strings" optional="true">
<description>Equations as written, for the output</description>
  </param>
  <param name="haclag" type="int" min="-1" default="-1">
<description>GMM weighting: -1 White, 0 Newey-West automatic lag, k lag k</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code>string meth = exists(method) ? tolower(method) : &quot;ls&quot;
errorif(!instring(&quot; ls ols wls sur tsls 2sls wtsls 3sls gmm &quot;, &quot; &quot; ~ meth ~ &quot; &quot;), &quot;method must be ls, wls, sur, tsls, wtsls, 3sls or gmm (fiml: see ev_sysfrom)&quot;)
meth = meth == &quot;ols&quot; ? &quot;ls&quot; : (meth == &quot;2sls&quot; ? &quot;tsls&quot; : meth)
scalar n = nelem(deps)
errorif(nelem(xspecs) != n || nelem(cnums) != n, &quot;deps, xspecs and cnums must have one entry per equation&quot;)
set skip_missing off          # rows with missing values are dropped below, jointly
# series of every equation, over the current sample
matrix Yall = {}
matrices XX = array(n)
matrices CC = array(n)
loop i = 1..n
  series evs_y = ev_gen(deps[i], vars)
  Yall ~= {evs_y}
  strings tk = strsplit(xspecs[i])
  strings cn = strsplit(cnums[i])
  errorif(nelem(tk) != nelem(cn), sprintf(&quot;equation %d: regressors and coefficient numbers differ&quot;, i))
  matrix Xi = {}
  matrix ci = {}
  loop j = 1..nelem(tk)
    if tolower(tk[j]) == &quot;c&quot;
      series evs_x = 1
    else
      series evs_x = ev_gen(tk[j], vars)
    endif
    Xi ~= {evs_x}
    ci ~= atof(cn[j])
  endloop
  XX[i] = Xi
  CC[i] = ci
endloop
matrix Z = {}
if exists(inst) &amp;&amp; strstrip(inst) != &quot;&quot;
  series evs_one = 1
  Z = {evs_one}
  strings zt = strsplit(inst)
  loop j = 1..nelem(zt)
    if tolower(zt[j]) != &quot;c&quot;
      series evs_z = ev_gen(zt[j], vars)
      Z ~= {evs_z}
    endif
  endloop
endif
scalar ivm = meth == &quot;tsls&quot; || meth == &quot;wtsls&quot; || meth == &quot;3sls&quot; || meth == &quot;gmm&quot;
errorif(ivm &amp;&amp; cols(Z) == 0, meth ~ &quot; needs instruments&quot;)
# balanced sample: rows complete in every equation
matrix okr = sumr(!ok(Yall)) .= 0
loop i = 1..n
  okr = okr .* (sumr(!ok(XX[i])) .= 0)
endloop
if cols(Z)
  okr = okr .* (sumr(!ok(Z)) .= 0)
  Z = selifr(Z, okr)
endif
series evs_o = obs
matrix tobs = selifr({evs_o}, okr)
Yall = selifr(Yall, okr)
scalar T = rows(Yall)
# unique coefficient numbers -&gt; columns of the stacked design
matrix allc = {}
loop i = 1..n
  XX[i] = selifr(XX[i], okr)
  allc ~= CC[i]
endloop
matrix cu = values(allc')'
scalar p = cols(cu)
matrix Xs = zeros(n * T, p)
matrix kk = zeros(1, n)
loop i = 1..n
  matrix ci = CC[i]
  kk[i] = cols(ci)
  loop j = 1..cols(ci)
    scalar col = imaxr(cu .= ci[j])
    scalar r1 = (i - 1) * T + 1
    scalar r2 = i * T
    matrix xij = XX[i]
    Xs[r1:r2, col] += xij[, j]
  endloop
endloop
matrix ys = vec(Yall)
# instruments: project each equation's block
matrix Xh = Xs
if ivm
  matrix P = Z * inv(Z'Z) * Z'
  loop i = 1..n
    scalar r1 = (i - 1) * T + 1
    scalar r2 = i * T
    Xh[r1:r2, ] = P * Xs[r1:r2, ]
  endloop
endif
# first stage: equation by equation (OLS or 2SLS), with sandwich covariance
matrix A = inv(Xh'Xs)
matrix b = A * (Xh'ys)
matrix E = mshape(ys - Xs * b, T, n)
matrix S = E'E / T
matrix V = {}
if meth == &quot;ls&quot; || meth == &quot;tsls&quot;
  matrix dfa = sqrt((T - kk)' * (T - kk))
  matrix Sd = (E'E) ./ dfa
  V = A * Xh' * (Sd ** I(T)) * Xh * A'
elif meth == &quot;gmm&quot;
  # two-step GMM, White weighting across equations and periods (EViews default):
  # moments (I_n ** Z)'(y - X b); S = sum_t (e_t ** z_t)'(e_t ** z_t)
  matrix Zb = I(n) ** Z
  matrix G = Zb' * Xs
  matrix gy = Zb' * ys
  scalar m = cols(Z)
  matrix Um = {}
  loop t = 1..T
    Um |= E[t,] ** Z[t,]
  endloop
  matrix Sg = ev__gmmS(Um, haclag)
  matrix Wg = inv(Sg)
  V = inv(G' * Wg * G)
  b = V * (G' * Wg * gy)
  E = mshape(ys - Xs * b, T, n)
  matrix gb = Zb' * vec(E)
  scalar Jst = qform(gb', Wg)
else
  # SUR / 3SLS: Sigma from the first stage; WLS / weighted TSLS: variances only
  matrix Sw = (meth == &quot;wls&quot; || meth == &quot;wtsls&quot;) ? I(n) .* S : S
  matrix Wi = inv(Sw) ** I(T)
  V = inv(Xh' * Wi * Xh)
  b = V * (Xh' * Wi * ys)
  E = mshape(ys - Xs * b, T, n)
endif
bundle bs
bs.kind = &quot;system&quot;
bs.method = meth
if meth == &quot;gmm&quot;
  bs.weighting = haclag &lt; 0 ? &quot;White&quot; : sprintf(&quot;HAC (Bartlett kernel, Newey-West lag %d)&quot;, ev__nwlag(T, haclag))
  bs.J = Jst
  bs.Jdf = n * cols(Z) - cols(b')
  bs.Jp = bs.Jdf &gt; 0 ? pvalue(X, bs.Jdf, Jst) : NA
endif
bs.spec = &quot;system&quot;
bs.coeff = b
bs.vcv = V
bs.stderr = sqrt(diag(V))
bs.cnums = cu
strings lab = array(0)
loop j = 1..p
  lab += sprintf(&quot;C(%d)&quot;, cu[j])
endloop
bs.labels = lab
bs.k = p
bs.n = n
bs.Tobs = T
bs.T = n * T                 # total system observations (for Wald F df)
bs.uhat = E
bs.sigma_mat = E'E / T
bs.detS = det(E'E / T)
bs.tobs = tobs
bs.sample = sprintf(&quot;%s %s&quot;, obslabel(minc(tobs)), obslabel(maxc(tobs)))
bs.estdate = strftime($now[1], &quot;%m/%d/%y   Time: %H:%M&quot;)
bs.tstat = b ./ bs.stderr
matrix pv = zeros(p, 1)
loop j = 1..p
  pv[j] = 2 * pvalue(t, n * T - p, abs(bs.tstat[j]))
endloop
bs.pval = pv
strings dl = array(0)
loop i = 1..n
  dl += toupper(deps[i])
endloop
bs.deps = dl
if exists(eqtext)
  bs.eqtext = eqtext
else
  bs.eqtext = dl
endif
# per-equation statistics
matrix st = {}
loop i = 1..n
  matrix u = E[, i]
  matrix y = Yall[, i]
  matrix d = y - meanc(y)
  scalar ssr = u'u
  scalar r2 = 1 - ssr / (d'd)
  matrix du = u[2:T] - u[1:T-1]
  st |= {r2, 1 - (1 - r2) * (T - 1) / (T - kk[i]), sqrt(ssr / (T - kk[i])), (du'du) / ssr, meanc(y), sqrt(d'd / (T - 1)), ssr}
endloop
bs.eqstats = st
if !quiet
  ev_sysprint(&amp;bs)
endif
return bs
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_sysprint" type="void">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="b" type="bundleref"/>
 </params>
<code>strings mkey = defarray(&quot;ls&quot;, &quot;wls&quot;, &quot;sur&quot;, &quot;tsls&quot;, &quot;wtsls&quot;, &quot;3sls&quot;, &quot;gmm&quot;, &quot;fiml&quot;)
strings mname = defarray(&quot;Least Squares&quot;, &quot;Weighted Least Squares&quot;, &quot;Seemingly Unrelated Regression&quot;, &quot;Two-Stage Least Squares&quot;, &quot;Weighted Two-Stage Least Squares&quot;, &quot;Three-Stage Least Squares&quot;, &quot;Generalized Method of Moments (two-step)&quot;, &quot;Full Information Maximum Likelihood&quot;)
scalar mi = instrings(mkey, b.method)[1]
printf &quot;\nSystem: %s\nEstimation Method: %s\nDate: %s\n&quot;, inbundle(b, &quot;name&quot;) ? b.name : &quot;UNTITLED&quot;, mname[mi], b.estdate
if inbundle(b, &quot;weighting&quot;)
  printf &quot;Weighting matrix: %s\n&quot;, b.weighting
endif
if inbundle(b, &quot;nonlinear&quot;)
  printf &quot;Convergence achieved after %d iterations\n&quot;, b.iters
endif
printf &quot;Sample: %s\nIncluded observations: %d\n&quot;, b.sample, b.Tobs
printf &quot;Total system (balanced) observations %d\n\n&quot;, b.T
ev__line(78)
printf &quot;%-26s%13s%13s%14s%12s\n&quot;, &quot;&quot;, &quot;Coefficient&quot;, &quot;Std. Error&quot;, &quot;t-Statistic&quot;, &quot;Prob.&quot;
ev__line(78)
loop j = 1..b.k
  printf &quot;%-26s%13.6f%13.6f%14.6f%12.4f\n&quot;, b.labels[j], b.coeff[j], b.stderr[j], b.tstat[j], b.pval[j]
endloop
ev__line(78)
printf &quot;%-40s%16.6g\n&quot;, &quot;Determinant residual covariance&quot;, b.detS
if inbundle(b, &quot;J&quot;)
  printf &quot;%-40s%16.6f\n&quot;, &quot;J-statistic&quot;, b.J
  if ok(b.Jp)
    printf &quot;%-40s%16.4f  (df %d)\n&quot;, &quot;Prob(J-statistic)&quot;, b.Jp, b.Jdf
  endif
endif
if inbundle(b, &quot;lnl&quot;)
  printf &quot;%-40s%16.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Log likelihood&quot;, b.lnl
endif
ev__line(78)
loop i = 1..b.n
  printf &quot;\nEquation: %s\nObservations: %d\n&quot;, b.eqtext[i], b.Tobs
  matrix s = b.eqstats[i,]
  printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f    %-24s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;R-squared&quot;, s[1], &quot;Mean dependent var&quot;, s[5]
  printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f    %-24s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Adjusted R-squared&quot;, s[2], &quot;S.D. dependent var&quot;, s[6]
  printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f    %-24s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;S.E. of regression&quot;, s[3], &quot;Sum squared resid&quot;, s[7]
  printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Durbin-Watson stat&quot;, s[4]
  ev__line(78)
endloop
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_sysresid" type="series">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="b" type="bundle">
<description>ev_system result</description>
  </param>
  <param name="i" type="int" min="1" default="1">
<description>Equation number</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code>return ev__toseries(b.uhat[, i], b.tobs)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_vecm" type="bundle">
 <params count="8">
  <param name="spec" type="string">
<description>Lag pairs of the differences, endogenous, then exogenous after the at-sign</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list">
<description>Series used (e.g. dataset)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="tcase" type="string" optional="true">
<description>Trend case a, b, c (default), d or e</description>
  </param>
  <param name="crank" type="int" min="1" default="1">
<description>Number of cointegrating equations</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
  <param name="names" type="string" optional="true">
<description>Display names, space separated</description>
  </param>
  <param name="Rr" type="matrix" optional="true">
<description>Restrictions on vec(beta): R</description>
  </param>
  <param name="qr" type="matrix" optional="true">
<description>Restrictions on vec(beta): q</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code>string AT = &quot;@&quot;
string cs = exists(tcase) ? tolower(tcase) : &quot;c&quot;
errorif(!instring(&quot; a b c d e &quot;, &quot; &quot; ~ cs ~ &quot; &quot;), &quot;trend case must be a, b, c, d or e&quot;)
strings LB = exists(names) ? strsplit(names) : array(0)
strings parts = strsplit(spec, AT)
strings L = strsplit(parts[1])
matrix lagv = {}
scalar i0 = 1
loop while i0 + 1 &lt;= nelem(L) &amp;&amp; regsub(L[i0], &quot;^[0-9]+$&quot;, &quot;&quot;) == &quot;&quot; &amp;&amp; regsub(L[i0+1], &quot;^[0-9]+$&quot;, &quot;&quot;) == &quot;&quot;
  lagv ~= seq(atof(L[i0]), atof(L[i0+1]))
  i0 += 2
endloop
errorif(cols(lagv) == 0, &quot;Start with lag pairs for the differences, e.g. 1 2&quot;)
lagv = values(lagv')'
errorif(lagv[1] != 1 || maxr(lagv) != cols(lagv), &quot;VEC lags must run from 1 without gaps, e.g. 1 2&quot;)
scalar order = maxr(lagv) + 1          # gretl's order counts lags in levels
list Y = null
strings ylab = array(0)
strings ytok = array(0)
loop i = i0..nelem(L)
  matrix pp = instrings(varnames(vars), L[i])
  if rows(pp) &gt; 0
    list Y += vars[pp[1]]
  else
    string v = sprintf(&quot;evc_y%d&quot;, i)
    series @v = ev_gen(L[i], vars)
    list Y += @v
  endif
  scalar li = nelem(ytok) + 1
  ylab += nelem(LB) &gt;= li ? toupper(LB[li]) : toupper(L[i])
  ytok += L[i]
endloop
errorif(crank &lt; 1 || crank &gt;= nelem(Y), &quot;rank must be between 1 and the number of variables minus 1&quot;)
list X = null
strings xlab = array(0)
if nelem(parts) == 2
  strings R = strsplit(parts[2])
  loop i = 1..nelem(R)
    if tolower(R[i]) != &quot;c&quot;
      matrix pp = instrings(varnames(vars), R[i])
      if rows(pp) &gt; 0
        list X += vars[pp[1]]
      else
        string v = sprintf(&quot;evc_x%d&quot;, i)
        series @v = ev_gen(R[i], vars)
        list X += @v
      endif
      xlab += toupper(R[i])
    endif
  endloop
endif
string opt = cs == &quot;a&quot; ? &quot;--nc&quot; : (cs == &quot;b&quot; ? &quot;--rc&quot; : (cs == &quot;c&quot; ? &quot;--uc&quot; : (cs == &quot;d&quot; ? &quot;--crt&quot; : &quot;--ct&quot;)))
scalar n0 = $nobs
if nelem(X) &gt; 0
  vecm order crank Y ; X --silent @opt
else
  vecm order crank Y --silent @opt
endif
scalar lr_r = NA
scalar lr_p = NA
if exists(Rr)
  restrict --full --silent
    R = Rr
    q = qr
  end restrict
  catch lr_r = $test
  catch lr_p = $pvalue
endif
bundle sys = $system
bundle b
b.kind = &quot;vecm&quot;
if exists(Rr)
  b.lr_restr = lr_r
  b.lr_restr_p = lr_p
endif
b.spec = spec
b.case = cs
b.rank = crank
b.sys = sys
b.ylab = ylab
b.xlab = xlab
b.ytok = ytok
strings noxt = array(0)
b.xtok = noxt
b.lags = lagv
b.hasc = cs == &quot;c&quot; || cs == &quot;d&quot; || cs == &quot;e&quot;
b.n = nelem(Y)
b.T = sys.T
b.coeff = $coeff
b.se = $stderr
b.tstat = b.coeff ./ b.se
b.beta = $jbeta
b.alpha = $jalpha
b.beta_se = sqrt(abs(diag($jvbeta)))
b.k = rows(b.coeff)
b.adjusted = sys.T &lt; n0
b.sample = sprintf(&quot;%s %s&quot;, obslabel(sys.t1), obslabel(sys.t2))
b.estdate = strftime($now[1], &quot;%m/%d/%y   Time: %H:%M&quot;)
b.lnl = $lnl
b.aic = -2 * b.lnl / b.T + 2 * (b.n * b.k) / b.T
b.sc = -2 * b.lnl / b.T + (b.n * b.k) * log(b.T) / b.T
matrix E = sys.uhat
b.det = det(E'E / b.T)
# gretl order: const, lagged differences, exogenous, trend, EC terms
strings clab = array(0)
if b.hasc
  clab += &quot;C&quot;
endif
loop j = 1..b.n
  loop l = 1..cols(lagv)
    clab += sprintf(&quot;D(%s(-%d))&quot;, ylab[j], lagv[l])
  endloop
endloop
loop j = 1..nelem(xlab)
  clab += xlab[j]
endloop
if cs == &quot;e&quot;
  clab += &quot;@TREND&quot;
endif
loop r = 1..crank
  clab += sprintf(&quot;CointEq%d&quot;, r)
endloop
errorif(nelem(clab) != b.k, sprintf(&quot;Internal error: %d labels for %d coefficients&quot;, nelem(clab), b.k))
b.clab = clab
if !quiet
  ev_vecprint(&amp;b)
endif
return b
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_vecprint" type="void">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="b" type="bundleref"/>
 </params>
<code>scalar n = b.n
printf &quot;\nVector Error Correction Estimates\nDate: %s\n&quot;, b.estdate
printf &quot;Sample%s: %s\n&quot;, b.adjusted ? &quot; (adjusted)&quot; : &quot;&quot;, b.sample
printf &quot;Included observations: %d%s\n&quot;, b.T, b.adjusted ? &quot; after adjustments&quot; : &quot;&quot;
printf &quot;Standard errors in ( ) &amp; t-statistics in [ ]\n\n&quot;
scalar w = 22 + 16 * max(n, b.rank)
ev__line(w)
printf &quot;%-22s&quot;, &quot;Cointegrating Eq:&quot;
loop r = 1..b.rank
  printf &quot;%16s&quot;, sprintf(&quot;CointEq%d&quot;, r)
endloop
printf &quot;\n&quot;
ev__line(w)
scalar nb = rows(b.beta)
loop i = 1..nb
  string nm = i &lt;= n ? sprintf(&quot;%s(-1)&quot;, b.ylab[i]) : (b.case == &quot;b&quot; ? &quot;C&quot; : &quot;@TREND(-1)&quot;)
  printf &quot;%-22s&quot;, nm
  loop r = 1..b.rank
    printf &quot;%16.6f&quot;, b.beta[i, r]
  endloop
  printf &quot;\n&quot;
  # gretl gives the variance of the freely estimated elements only
  scalar fi = (i - b.rank - 1) * b.rank + 1
  if i &gt; b.rank &amp;&amp; rows(b.beta_se) &gt;= fi + b.rank - 1
    printf &quot;%-22s&quot;, &quot;&quot;
    loop r = 1..b.rank
      printf &quot;%16s&quot;, sprintf(&quot;(%.5f)&quot;, b.beta_se[fi + r - 1])
    endloop
    printf &quot;\n%-22s&quot;, &quot;&quot;
    loop r = 1..b.rank
      printf &quot;%16s&quot;, sprintf(&quot;[%.5f]&quot;, b.beta[i, r] / b.beta_se[fi + r - 1])
    endloop
    printf &quot;\n&quot;
  endif
endloop
printf &quot;\n&quot;
ev__line(w)
printf &quot;%-22s&quot;, &quot;Error Correction:&quot;
loop j = 1..n
  printf &quot;%16s&quot;, sprintf(&quot;D(%s)&quot;, b.ylab[j])
endloop
printf &quot;\n&quot;
ev__line(w)
# EViews order: CointEq, lagged differences, C, exogenous
scalar k = b.k
matrix ord = seq(k - b.rank + 1, k)
scalar c0 = b.hasc ? 2 : 1
scalar nl = n * cols(b.lags)
ord ~= seq(c0, c0 + nl - 1)
if b.hasc
  ord ~= 1
endif
if k - b.rank &gt;= c0 + nl
  ord ~= seq(c0 + nl, k - b.rank)
endif
loop r = 1..cols(ord)
  scalar i = ord[r]
  printf &quot;%-22s&quot;, b.clab[i]
  loop j = 1..n
    printf &quot;%16.6f&quot;, b.coeff[i, j]
  endloop
  printf &quot;\n%-22s&quot;, &quot;&quot;
  loop j = 1..n
    printf &quot;%16s&quot;, sprintf(&quot;(%.5f)&quot;, b.se[i, j])
  endloop
  printf &quot;\n%-22s&quot;, &quot;&quot;
  loop j = 1..n
    printf &quot;%16s&quot;, sprintf(&quot;[%.5f]&quot;, b.tstat[i, j])
  endloop
  printf &quot;\n\n&quot;
endloop
ev__line(w)
printf &quot;%-44s%16.6g\n&quot;, &quot;Determinant resid covariance&quot;, b.det
printf &quot;%-44s%16.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Log likelihood&quot;, b.lnl
printf &quot;%-44s%16.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Akaike information criterion&quot;, b.aic
printf &quot;%-44s%16.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Schwarz criterion&quot;, b.sc
ev__line(w)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_coint" type="void">
 <params count="4">
  <param name="names" type="string">
<description>Endogenous series, e.g. y1 y2</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list">
<description>Series used (e.g. dataset)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="tcase" type="string" optional="true">
<description>Trend case a, b, c (default), d or e</description>
  </param>
  <param name="nlag" type="int" min="1" default="4">
<description>Lags of the differences</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code># Johansen cointegration test (gretl's coint2)
string cs = exists(tcase) ? tolower(tcase) : &quot;c&quot;
string opt = cs == &quot;a&quot; ? &quot;--nc&quot; : (cs == &quot;b&quot; ? &quot;--rc&quot; : (cs == &quot;c&quot; ? &quot;&quot; : (cs == &quot;d&quot; ? &quot;--crt&quot; : &quot;--ct&quot;)))
list Y = null
strings L = strsplit(names)
loop i = 1..nelem(L)
  matrix pp = instrings(varnames(vars), L[i])
  errorif(rows(pp) == 0, sprintf(&quot;%s: use series names for the Johansen test&quot;, L[i]))
  list Y += vars[pp[1]]
endloop
scalar order = nlag + 1
printf &quot;\nJohansen Cointegration Test\nSeries: %s\nLags interval (in first differences): 1 to %d\n&quot;, toupper(names), nlag
coint2 order Y @opt
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_sysfrom" type="bundle">
 <params count="13">
  <param name="method" type="string">
<description>Estimator used, e.g. fiml</description>
  </param>
  <param name="coef" type="matrix">
<description>$coeff of the estimated system</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vcv" type="matrix">
<description>$vcv</description>
  </param>
  <param name="U" type="matrix">
<description>$uhat</description>
  </param>
  <param name="Yh" type="matrix">
<description>$yhat</description>
  </param>
  <param name="pos" type="matrix">
<description>Position in coef of each coefficient number</description>
  </param>
  <param name="cu" type="matrix">
<description>Coefficient numbers</description>
  </param>
  <param name="kk" type="matrix">
<description>Regressors per equation</description>
  </param>
  <param name="deps" type="strings"/>
  <param name="eqtext" type="strings"/>
  <param name="t1" type="scalar"/>
  <param name="lnl" type="scalar" default="NA"/>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
 </params>
<code># EViews-style system result from an estimate made with gretl's system command
scalar T = rows(U)
scalar n = cols(U)
bundle bs
bs.kind = &quot;system&quot;
bs.method = method
bs.spec = &quot;system&quot;
bs.coeff = coef[pos]
bs.vcv = vcv[pos, pos]
bs.stderr = sqrt(diag(bs.vcv))
bs.cnums = cu
strings lab = array(0)
loop j = 1..cols(cu)
  lab += sprintf(&quot;C(%d)&quot;, cu[j])
endloop
bs.labels = lab
scalar p = cols(cu)
bs.k = p
bs.n = n
bs.Tobs = T
bs.T = n * T
bs.uhat = U
bs.detS = det(U'U / T)
bs.tobs = seq(t1, t1 + T - 1)'
bs.sample = sprintf(&quot;%s %s&quot;, obslabel(t1), obslabel(t1 + T - 1))
bs.estdate = strftime($now[1], &quot;%m/%d/%y   Time: %H:%M&quot;)
bs.tstat = bs.coeff ./ bs.stderr
matrix pv = zeros(p, 1)
loop j = 1..p
  pv[j] = 2 * pvalue(t, n * T - p, abs(bs.tstat[j]))
endloop
bs.pval = pv
bs.deps = deps
bs.eqtext = eqtext
if ok(lnl)
  bs.lnl = lnl
endif
matrix st = {}
matrix Y = Yh + U
loop i = 1..n
  matrix u = U[, i]
  matrix d = Y[, i] - meanc(Y[, i])
  scalar ssr = u'u
  scalar r2 = 1 - ssr / (d'd)
  matrix du = u[2:T] - u[1:T-1]
  st |= {r2, 1 - (1 - r2) * (T - 1) / (T - kk[i]), sqrt(ssr / (T - kk[i])), (du'du) / ssr, meanc(Y[, i]), sqrt(d'd / (T - 1)), ssr}
endloop
bs.eqstats = st
if !quiet
  ev_sysprint(&amp;bs)
endif
return bs
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_svar" type="void">
 <params count="4">
  <param name="v" type="bundleref">
<description>VAR result (ev_varest)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="Apat" type="matrix">
<description>Pattern of A: numbers are fixed, NA are estimated</description>
  </param>
  <param name="Bpat" type="matrix">
<description>Pattern of B: numbers are fixed, NA are estimated</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
 </params>
<code>errorif(!inbundle(v, &quot;sys&quot;), &quot;First argument must be a VAR&quot;)
scalar n = v.n
errorif(rows(Apat) != n || cols(Apat) != n || rows(Bpat) != n || cols(Bpat) != n, sprintf(&quot;A and B must be %d x %d&quot;, n, n))
matrix E = v.sys.uhat
scalar T = rows(E)
matrix S = E'E / T
scalar na = sum(!ok(vec(Apat)))
scalar nb = sum(!ok(vec(Bpat)))
scalar nf = na + nb
errorif(nf &gt; n * (n + 1) / 2, sprintf(&quot;Too many free parameters (%d) for %d equations: at most %d&quot;, nf, n, n * (n + 1) / 2))
# starting values: A free -&gt; 0 off the diagonal, 1 on it; B free -&gt; sqrt of variances
matrix th = zeros(nf, 1)
matrix ia = selifr(seq(1, n * n)', !ok(vec(Apat)))
matrix ib = selifr(seq(1, n * n)', !ok(vec(Bpat)))
loop i = 1..na
  th[i] = (ia[i] - 1) % (n + 1) == 0 ? 1 : 0
endloop
loop i = 1..nb
  scalar d = (ib[i] - 1) % (n + 1) == 0
  th[na + i] = d ? sqrt(S[(ib[i] - 1) / (n + 1) + 1, (ib[i] - 1) / (n + 1) + 1]) : 0.1
endloop
set max_verbose off
scalar ll = BFGSmax(&amp;th, ev__svar_ll(th, Apat, Bpat, S, T))
matrix H = fdjac(th, ev__svar_grad(th, Apat, Bpat, S, T))
matrix V = inv(-0.5 * (H + H'))
matrix A = Apat
matrix B = Bpat
if na
  A = ev__fill(A, ia, th[1:na])
endif
if nb
  B = ev__fill(B, ib, th[na+1:nf])
endif
# normalise signs: positive impact of each shock on its own variable
matrix Sim = inv(A) * B
matrix sg = sgn(diag(Sim))'
sg = sg + (sg .= 0)
B = B .* sg
Sim = inv(A) * B
if nb
  th[na+1:nf] = ev__pick(B, ib)
endif
v.svarA = A
v.svarB = B
v.svarS = Sim
v.svar_type = &quot;short-run pattern (A e = B u)&quot;
v.svar_coef = th
v.svar_se = sqrt(abs(diag(V)))
v.svar_lnl = ll
scalar llu = -T * n / 2 * (log(2 * $pi) + 1) - T / 2 * log(det(S))
v.svar_df = n * (n + 1) / 2 - nf
v.svar_lr = 2 * (llu - ll)
v.svar_lrp = v.svar_df &gt; 0 ? pvalue(X, v.svar_df, v.svar_lr) : NA
if !quiet
  ev_svarprint(&amp;v)
endif
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_svar_lr" type="void">
 <params count="3">
  <param name="v" type="bundleref">
<description>VAR result (ev_varest)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
  <param name="order" type="matrix" optional="true">
<description>Recursive ordering of the variables for the long-run zeros</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code># long-run (Blanchard-Quah) identification: the accumulated response of
# variable i to shock j is zero for j &gt; i
errorif(!inbundle(v, &quot;sys&quot;) || (inbundle(v, &quot;kind&quot;) &amp;&amp; v.kind == &quot;vecm&quot;), &quot;Long-run restrictions need a VAR in stationary variables&quot;)
scalar n = v.n
matrix E = v.sys.uhat
scalar T = rows(E)
matrix S = E'E / T
matrix A = v.sys.A
scalar p = cols(A) / n
matrix sumA = zeros(n, n)
loop l = 1..p
  sumA += A[1:n, (l - 1) * n + 1:l * n]
endloop
matrix C1 = inv(I(n) - sumA)
matrix perm = seq(1, n)
if exists(order)
  perm = vec(order)'
endif
errorif(cols(perm) != n, &quot;order must list every variable once&quot;)
# Cholesky of the long-run covariance in the given ordering, mapped back
matrix C1p = C1[perm, perm]
matrix Lp = cholesky(C1p * S[perm, perm] * C1p')
matrix Sp = inv(C1p) * Lp
matrix Sim = zeros(n, n)
matrix L = zeros(n, n)
loop i = 1..n
  scalar pi = perm[i]
  loop j = 1..n
    scalar pj = perm[j]
    Sim[pi, pj] = Sp[i, j]
    L[pi, pj] = Lp[i, j]
  endloop
endloop
v.svarS = Sim
v.svarA = I(n)
v.svarB = v.svarS
v.svar_lrmat = L
v.svar_type = &quot;long-run (Blanchard-Quah)&quot;
if !quiet
  ev_svarprint(&amp;v)
endif
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_svarprint" type="void">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="v" type="bundleref"/>
 </params>
<code>printf &quot;\nStructural VAR Estimates\nSample: %s\nIncluded observations: %d\n&quot;, v.sample, v.T
printf &quot;Restriction type: %s\nModel: Ae = Bu where E[uu']=I\n&quot;, v.svar_type
scalar n = v.n
if inbundle(v, &quot;svar_coef&quot;)
  ev__line(70)
  printf &quot;%-14s%14s%14s%14s%12s\n&quot;, &quot;&quot;, &quot;Coefficient&quot;, &quot;Std. Error&quot;, &quot;z-Statistic&quot;, &quot;Prob.&quot;
  ev__line(70)
  loop i = 1..rows(v.svar_coef)
    scalar z = v.svar_coef[i] / v.svar_se[i]
    printf &quot;%-14s%14.6f%14.6f%14.6f%12.4f\n&quot;, sprintf(&quot;C(%d)&quot;, i), v.svar_coef[i], v.svar_se[i], z, 2 * pvalue(z, abs(z))
  endloop
  ev__line(70)
  printf &quot;%-30s%16.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Log likelihood&quot;, v.svar_lnl
  if v.svar_df &gt; 0
    printf &quot;LR test for over-identification:\nChi-square(%d)%17.6f      Probability %.4f\n&quot;, v.svar_df, v.svar_lr, v.svar_lrp
  endif
  ev__line(70)
endif
printf &quot;Estimated A matrix:\n&quot;
printf &quot;%14.6f&quot;, v.svarA
printf &quot;Estimated B matrix:\n&quot;
printf &quot;%14.6f&quot;, v.svarB
printf &quot;Impact of the structural shocks (inverse(A) * B):\n&quot;
printf &quot;%14.6f&quot;, v.svarS
if inbundle(v, &quot;svar_lrmat&quot;)
  printf &quot;Long-run response (lower triangular):\n&quot;
  printf &quot;%14.6f&quot;, v.svar_lrmat
endif
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_modelsolve" type="bundle">
 <params count="6">
  <param name="eqs" type="bundles">
<description>Estimated equations (ev_ls results)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="idents" type="strings">
<description>Identities, e.g. Y = C + I + G</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list">
<description>Series used (e.g. dataset)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="dynamic" type="bool" default="1">
<description>Dynamic (1) or static (0) solution</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
  <param name="opts" type="bundle" optional="true">
<description>overrides (strings), suffix, addfactors (1/0), reps, seed</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code>scalar ne = nelem(eqs)
scalar m = ne + nelem(idents)
errorif(m == 0, &quot;The model has no equations&quot;)
strings bases = array(0)
matrix forms = zeros(1, m)
strings rhs = array(0)          # expression to evaluate (identities and NLS)
matrices XX = array(m)
matrices uses = array(m)
loop k = 1..m
  string dep = &quot;&quot;
  if k &lt;= ne
    bundle b = eqs[k]
    string kind = inbundle(b, &quot;kind&quot;) ? b.kind : &quot;ls&quot;
    errorif(kind != &quot;ls&quot; &amp;&amp; kind != &quot;nls&quot;, &quot;Models can use least squares and explicit (NLS) equations&quot;)
    if kind == &quot;nls&quot;
      dep = b.lhs
      string r = b.rhs
      loop j = 1..b.k
        r = regsub(r, sprintf(&quot;evn_c%d(?![0-9])&quot;, b.cidx[j]), sprintf(&quot;(%.17g)&quot;, b.coeff[j]))
      endloop
      rhs += r
    else
      dep = strsplit(b.spec)[1]
      rhs += &quot;&quot;
    endif
  else
    strings sd = strsplit(idents[k - ne], &quot;=&quot;)
    errorif(nelem(sd) != 2, sprintf(&quot;Identity '%s' needs one '='&quot;, idents[k - ne]))
    dep = strstrip(sd[1])
    rhs += strstrip(sd[2])
  endif
  string bs = &quot;&quot;
  forms[k] = ev__depform(dep, &amp;bs, vars)
  errorif(forms[k] &lt; 0, sprintf(&quot;'%s': the left-hand side must be Y, log(Y), d(Y) or dlog(Y) of a series&quot;, dep))
  errorif(rows(instrings(bases, bs)) &gt; 0, sprintf(&quot;%s is determined by two equations&quot;, bs))
  bases += bs
endloop
# regressors of least-squares equations; which terms involve endogenous variables
loop k = 1..ne
  bundle b = eqs[k]
  if !inbundle(b, &quot;kind&quot;) || b.kind == &quot;ls&quot;
    strings tok = strsplit(b.spec)
    matrix X = {}
    matrix u = {}
    loop i = 2..nelem(tok)
      if tolower(tok[i]) == &quot;c&quot;
        series evm_r = 1
        u ~= 0
      else
        series evm_r = ev_gen(tok[i], vars)
        scalar f = 0
        loop j = 1..m
          f = f || regsub(tok[i], &quot;(?i)(?&lt;![A-Za-z0-9_])&quot; ~ bases[j] ~ &quot;(?![A-Za-z0-9_])&quot;, &quot;#&quot;) != tok[i]
        endloop
        u ~= f
      endif
      X ~= {evm_r}
    endloop
    XX[k] = X
    uses[k] = u
  endif
endloop
# actual levels and their previous values
matrix L = {}
matrix Lp = {}
loop k = 1..m
  string e1 = &quot;vars.&quot; ~ bases[k]
  string e2 = &quot;vars.&quot; ~ bases[k] ~ &quot;(-1)&quot;
  series evm_a = @e1
  series evm_ap = @e2
  L ~= {evm_a}
  Lp ~= {evm_ap}
endloop
series evm_o = obs
matrix tobs = {evm_o}
scalar T = rows(L)
matrix Sol = L
loop i = 1..T
  loop k = 1..m
    if !ok(Sol[i, k])
      Sol[i, k] = Lp[i, k]
    endif
  endloop
endloop
matrix D = zeros(T, m)
bundle C
C.eqs = eqs
C.rhs = rhs
C.XX = XX
C.uses = uses
C.forms = forms
C.bases = bases
C.L = L
C.Lp = Lp
C.tobs = tobs
C.ne = ne
C.m = m
C.dynamic = dynamic
# options: scenario overrides, add factors, stochastic simulation
strings ovr = array(0)
string suf = &quot;_0&quot;
scalar use_af = 0
scalar reps = 0
if exists(opts)
  if inbundle(opts, &quot;overrides&quot;)
    ovr = opts.overrides
  endif
  suf = inbundle(opts, &quot;suffix&quot;) ? opts.suffix : (nelem(ovr) ? &quot;_1&quot; : &quot;_0&quot;)
  use_af = inbundle(opts, &quot;addfactors&quot;) ? opts.addfactors : 0
  reps = inbundle(opts, &quot;reps&quot;) ? opts.reps : 0
  if inbundle(opts, &quot;seed&quot;)
    set seed opts.seed
  endif
endif
loop k = 1..nelem(ovr)
  errorif(rows(instrings(varnames(vars), ovr[k] ~ suf)) == 0, sprintf(&quot;Override series %s%s does not exist&quot;, ovr[k], suf))
  errorif(rows(instrings(bases, ovr[k])) &gt; 0, sprintf(&quot;%s is endogenous and cannot be overridden&quot;, ovr[k]))
endloop
C.ovr = ovr
C.suf = suf
# regressors that use an overridden series must be recomputed in each period
matrices UU = C.uses
loop k = 1..ne
  if C.rhs[k] == &quot;&quot;
    bundle b = eqs[k]
    strings tok = strsplit(b.spec)
    matrix u = UU[k]
    loop i = 2..nelem(tok)
      loop j = 1..nelem(ovr)
        if regsub(tok[i], &quot;(?i)(?&lt;![A-Za-z0-9_])&quot; ~ ovr[j] ~ &quot;(?![A-Za-z0-9_])&quot;, &quot;#&quot;) != tok[i]
          u[i-1] = 1
        endif
      endloop
    endloop
    UU[k] = u
  endif
endloop
C.uses = UU
# add factors: series &lt;endogenous&gt;_a, in the units of each equation's left-hand side
matrix AF = zeros(T, m)
if use_af
  loop k = 1..m
    matrix pp = instrings(varnames(vars), bases[k] ~ &quot;_a&quot;)
    if rows(pp) &gt; 0
      series evm_af = vars[pp[1]]
      AF[, k] = misszero({evm_af})
    endif
  endloop
endif
scalar maxit = 0
scalar unconverged = 0
Sol = ev__msolve(C, vars, AF, Sol, &amp;maxit, &amp;unconverged)
# stochastic simulation: normal shocks with each equation's S.E. of regression
matrix smean = {}
matrix ssd = {}
if reps &gt; 0
  matrix sig = zeros(1, m)
  loop k = 1..ne
    bundle b = eqs[k]
    sig[k] = b.sigma
  endloop
  matrix s1 = zeros(T, m)
  matrix s2 = zeros(T, m)
  loop rr = 1..reps
    matrix sh = mnormal(T, m) .* sig
    scalar mi = 0
    scalar un = 0
    matrix Sr = ev__msolve(C, vars, AF + sh, Sol, &amp;mi, &amp;un)
    s1 += Sr
    s2 += Sr.^2
  endloop
  smean = s1 / reps
  ssd = sqrt(abs(s2 / reps - smean.^2) * reps / (reps - 1))
endif
bundle ms
ms.kind = &quot;model&quot;
ms.suffix = suf
ms.reps = reps
if reps &gt; 0
  ms.mean = smean
  ms.sd = ssd
endif
ms.names = bases
ms.sol = Sol
ms.actual = L
ms.tobs = tobs
ms.dynamic = dynamic
ms.maxit = maxit
ms.unconverged = unconverged
ms.sample = sprintf(&quot;%s %s&quot;, obslabel($t1), obslabel($t2))
if !quiet
  printf &quot;\nModel solution\nSolver: Newton, %s\nSample: %s\n&quot;, dynamic ? &quot;dynamic solution&quot; : &quot;static solution&quot;, ms.sample
  if nelem(ovr)
    printf &quot;Scenario: overrides&quot;
    loop k = 1..nelem(ovr)
      printf &quot; %s -&gt; %s%s&quot;, toupper(ovr[k]), toupper(ovr[k]), suf
    endloop
    printf &quot;\n&quot;
  endif
  if use_af
    printf &quot;Add factors: series &lt;variable&gt;_a\n&quot;
  endif
  if reps &gt; 0
    printf &quot;Stochastic simulation: %d repetitions (mean %sm, std. dev. %ss)\n&quot;, reps, suf, suf
  endif
  printf &quot;Endogenous variables (solution series get the suffix %s):&quot;, suf
  loop k = 1..m
    printf &quot; %s&quot;, toupper(bases[k])
  endloop
  printf &quot;\n&quot;
  if unconverged
    printf &quot;Warning: %d period(s) did not converge in 100 iterations\n&quot;, unconverged
  else
    printf &quot;Converged in at most %d iterations per period\n&quot;, maxit
  endif
  matrix ok2 = ok(L) .* ok(Sol)
  printf &quot;\n%-16s%16s%16s\n&quot;, &quot;Variable&quot;, &quot;RMSE&quot;, &quot;Mean abs. % err&quot;
  loop k = 1..m
    matrix a = selifr(L[, k], ok2[, k])
    matrix s2 = selifr(Sol[, k], ok2[, k])
    printf &quot;%-16s%16.6f%16.4f\n&quot;, toupper(bases[k]), sqrt(meanc((s2 - a).^2)), 100 * meanc(abs((s2 - a) ./ a))
  endloop
endif
return ms
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_modelseries" type="series">
 <params count="3">
  <param name="ms" type="bundle">
<description>ev_modelsolve result</description>
  </param>
  <param name="k" type="int" min="1" default="1">
<description>Endogenous variable number</description>
  </param>
  <param name="what" type="string" optional="true">
<description>empty: solution; mean or sd: stochastic simulation</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code>string w = exists(what) ? tolower(what) : &quot;&quot;
if w == &quot;mean&quot;
  return ev__toseries(ms.mean[, k], ms.tobs)
elif w == &quot;sd&quot;
  return ev__toseries(ms.sd[, k], ms.tobs)
endif
return ev__toseries(ms.sol[, k], ms.tobs)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_eqres" type="series">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="b" type="bundle">
<description>Estimated equation (ev_ls result)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list">
<description>Series used (e.g. dataset)</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code># residual of an equation over the current sample, in the units of its
# left-hand side (used to initialise model add factors)
string kind = inbundle(b, &quot;kind&quot;) ? b.kind : &quot;ls&quot;
errorif(kind != &quot;ls&quot; &amp;&amp; kind != &quot;nls&quot;, &quot;Least squares or explicit equations only&quot;)
if kind == &quot;nls&quot;
  series evr_y = ev_gen(b.lhs, vars)
  string r = b.rhs
  loop j = 1..b.k
    r = regsub(r, sprintf(&quot;evn_c%d(?![0-9])&quot;, b.cidx[j]), sprintf(&quot;(%.17g)&quot;, b.coeff[j]))
  endloop
  series evr_f = ev_gen(r, vars)
  return evr_y - evr_f
endif
strings tok = strsplit(b.spec)
series evr_y = ev_gen(tok[1], vars)
series evr_f = 0
loop i = 2..nelem(tok)
  if tolower(tok[i]) == &quot;c&quot;
    evr_f += b.coeff[i-1]
  else
    series evr_x = ev_gen(tok[i], vars)
    evr_f += b.coeff[i-1] * evr_x
  endif
endloop
return evr_y - evr_f
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_nlsystem" type="bundle">
 <params count="6">
  <param name="eqs" type="strings">
<description>Explicit equations, e.g. y = c(1) + c(2)*x^c(3)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list">
<description>Series used (e.g. dataset)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="method" type="string" optional="true">
<description>ls, wls, sur, tsls, 3sls or gmm</description>
  </param>
  <param name="inst" type="string" optional="true">
<description>Instruments (a constant is added)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
  <param name="haclag" type="int" min="-1" default="-1">
<description>GMM weighting: -1 White, 0 Newey-West automatic, k lag</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code># systems of equations that are nonlinear in the coefficients c(i):
# Gauss-Newton on the (weighted) stacked residuals, numerical derivatives
string meth = exists(method) ? tolower(method) : &quot;ls&quot;
errorif(!instring(&quot; ls wls sur tsls 3sls gmm &quot;, &quot; &quot; ~ meth ~ &quot; &quot;), &quot;method must be ls, wls, sur, tsls, 3sls or gmm&quot;)
set skip_missing off
scalar n = nelem(eqs)
strings deps = array(0)
strings rhx = array(0)
strings rhs0 = array(0)
matrix allc = {}
matrix Y = {}
loop i = 1..n
  strings sd = strsplit(eqs[i], &quot;=&quot;)
  errorif(nelem(sd) != 2, sprintf(&quot;Equation %d needs one '='&quot;, i))
  string lhs = strstrip(sd[1])
  string rr = strstrip(sd[2])
  deps += toupper(lhs)
  rhs0 += rr
  series evq_y = ev_gen(lhs, vars)
  Y ~= {evq_y}
  string low = tolower(rr)
  loop k = 1..99
    if instring(low, sprintf(&quot;c(%d)&quot;, k))
      allc ~= k
    endif
  endloop
  rhx += ev__prep(regsub(rr, &quot;(?i)(?&lt;![A-Za-z0-9_])c\(([0-9]+)\)&quot;, &quot;evq_c\1&quot;), vars)
endloop
matrix cu = values(allc')'
scalar p = cols(cu)
errorif(p == 0, &quot;No coefficients c(i) in the equations&quot;)
# start: zeros (as EViews' C vector), rows complete at a small perturbation
matrix c = 0.001 * ones(p, 1)
loop j = 1..p
  string pn = sprintf(&quot;evq_c%d&quot;, cu[j])
  scalar @pn = c[j]
endloop
matrix F0 = {}
loop i = 1..n
  string e = rhx[i]
  series evq_f = @e
  F0 ~= {evq_f}
endloop
matrix mask = (sumr(!ok(Y)) .= 0) .* (sumr(!ok(F0)) .= 0)
matrix Z = {}
if exists(inst) &amp;&amp; strstrip(inst) != &quot;&quot;
  series evq_one = 1
  Z = {evq_one}
  strings zt = strsplit(inst)
  loop j = 1..nelem(zt)
    if tolower(zt[j]) != &quot;c&quot;
      series evq_z = ev_gen(zt[j], vars)
      Z ~= {evq_z}
    endif
  endloop
  mask = mask .* (sumr(!ok(Z)) .= 0)
  Z = selifr(Z, mask)
endif
scalar ivm = meth == &quot;tsls&quot; || meth == &quot;3sls&quot; || meth == &quot;gmm&quot;
errorif(ivm &amp;&amp; cols(Z) == 0, meth ~ &quot; needs instruments&quot;)
series evq_o = obs
matrix tobs = selifr({evq_o}, mask)
scalar T = rows(tobs)
matrix P = ivm ? Z * inv(Z'Z) * Z' : I(T)
# weighting of the stacked residuals
matrix M = I(n) ** P
scalar iters = 0
scalar mu = 1e-3
loop stage = 1..2
  loop it = 1..200
    matrix r = ev__nlres(rhx, Y, mask, vars, cu, c)
    matrix J = zeros(n * T, p)
    loop j = 1..p
      matrix ch = c
      scalar h = 1e-6 * (1 + abs(c[j]))
      ch[j] += h
      J[, j] = -(ev__nlres(rhx, Y, mask, vars, cu, ch) - r) / h
    endloop
    # Levenberg-Marquardt step: rejected steps are not applied
    matrix H = J' * M * J
    matrix gr = J' * M * r
    scalar obj = qform(r', M)
    scalar accepted = 0
    matrix step = zeros(p, 1)
    loop 40
      matrix stp = inv(H + mu * (I(p) .* H)) * gr
      matrix rn = ev__nlres(rhx, Y, mask, vars, cu, c + stp)
      rn = ok(rn) ? rn : 1e300     # undefined values make the step unacceptable
      if maxc(abs(rn)) &lt; 1e150
        if qform(rn', M) &lt;= obj
          accepted = 1
          step = stp
          mu = max(mu / 10, 1e-12)
          break
        endif
      endif
      mu = mu * 10
    endloop
    if !accepted
      break
    endif
    c = c + step
    iters++
    if maxc(abs(step) ./ (1 + abs(c))) &lt; 1e-9
      break
    endif
  endloop
  matrix E = mshape(ev__nlres(rhx, Y, mask, vars, cu, c), T, n)
  if stage == 1
    # second stage weights for the system estimators
    if meth == &quot;sur&quot; || meth == &quot;wls&quot;
      matrix S = E'E / T
      S = meth == &quot;wls&quot; ? I(n) .* S : S
      M = inv(S) ** I(T)
    elif meth == &quot;3sls&quot;
      M = inv(E'E / T) ** P
    elif meth == &quot;gmm&quot;
      matrix Zb = I(n) ** Z
      matrix Um = {}
      loop t = 1..T
        Um |= E[t,] ** Z[t,]
      endloop
      M = Zb * inv(ev__gmmS(Um, haclag)) * Zb'
    else
      break
    endif
  endif
endloop
# covariance
matrix r = vec(E)
matrix J = zeros(n * T, p)
loop j = 1..p
  matrix ch = c
  scalar h = 1e-6 * (1 + abs(c[j]))
  ch[j] += h
  J[, j] = -(ev__nlres(rhx, Y, mask, vars, cu, ch) - r) / h
endloop
matrix kk = zeros(1, n)
loop i = 1..n
  scalar ki = 0
  loop j = 1..p
    ki += instring(tolower(rhs0[i]), sprintf(&quot;c(%d)&quot;, cu[j])) &gt; 0
  endloop
  kk[i] = ki
endloop
matrix A = inv(J' * M * J)
matrix V = {}
if meth == &quot;ls&quot; || meth == &quot;tsls&quot;
  matrix Sd = (E'E) ./ sqrt((T - kk)' * (T - kk))
  V = A * J' * M * (Sd ** I(T)) * M * J * A
else
  V = A
endif
bundle bs
bs.kind = &quot;system&quot;
bs.nonlinear = 1
bs.iters = iters
bs.method = meth
bs.spec = &quot;system&quot;
if meth == &quot;gmm&quot;
  bs.weighting = haclag &lt; 0 ? &quot;White&quot; : sprintf(&quot;HAC (Bartlett kernel, Newey-West lag %d)&quot;, ev__nwlag(T, haclag))
  matrix gb = (I(n) ** Z)' * r
  bs.J = qform(gb', inv(ev__gmmS(Um, haclag)))
  bs.Jdf = n * cols(Z) - p
  bs.Jp = bs.Jdf &gt; 0 ? pvalue(X, bs.Jdf, bs.J) : NA
endif
bs.coeff = c
bs.vcv = V
bs.stderr = sqrt(diag(V))
bs.cnums = cu
strings lab = array(0)
loop j = 1..p
  lab += sprintf(&quot;C(%d)&quot;, cu[j])
endloop
bs.labels = lab
bs.k = p
bs.n = n
bs.Tobs = T
bs.T = n * T
bs.uhat = E
bs.sigma_mat = E'E / T
bs.detS = det(E'E / T)
bs.tobs = tobs
bs.sample = sprintf(&quot;%s %s&quot;, obslabel(minc(tobs)), obslabel(maxc(tobs)))
bs.estdate = strftime($now[1], &quot;%m/%d/%y   Time: %H:%M&quot;)
bs.tstat = c ./ bs.stderr
matrix pv = zeros(p, 1)
loop j = 1..p
  pv[j] = 2 * pvalue(t, n * T - p, abs(bs.tstat[j]))
endloop
bs.pval = pv
bs.deps = deps
strings et = array(0)
loop i = 1..n
  et += regsub(toupper(eqs[i]), &quot;\s&quot;, &quot;&quot;)
endloop
bs.eqtext = et
matrix st = {}
matrix Ys = selifr(Y, mask)
loop i = 1..n
  matrix u = E[, i]
  matrix d = Ys[, i] - meanc(Ys[, i])
  scalar ssr = u'u
  scalar r2 = 1 - ssr / (d'd)
  matrix du = u[2:T] - u[1:T-1]
  st |= {r2, 1 - (1 - r2) * (T - 1) / (T - kk[i]), sqrt(ssr / (T - kk[i])), (du'du) / ssr, meanc(Ys[, i]), sqrt(d'd / (T - 1)), ssr}
endloop
bs.eqstats = st
if !quiet
  ev_sysprint(&amp;bs)
endif
return bs
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_garch" type="bundle">
 <params count="9">
  <param name="spec" type="string">
<description>Mean equation, e.g. y c x</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list">
<description>Series used (e.g. dataset)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="model" type="string" optional="true">
<description>garch, tarch or egarch</description>
  </param>
  <param name="narch" type="int" min="0" default="1">
<description>ARCH order</description>
  </param>
  <param name="ngarch" type="int" min="0" default="1">
<description>GARCH order</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
  <param name="archm" type="string" optional="true">
<description>ARCH-in-mean term: var, sd or log</description>
  </param>
  <param name="nthr" type="int" min="-1" default="-1">
<description>Threshold (asymmetric) order; -1 = EViews default</description>
  </param>
  <param name="dist" type="string" optional="true">
<description>Error distribution: normal (default), t or ged</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code>string md = exists(model) ? tolower(model) : &quot;garch&quot;
errorif(!instring(&quot; garch tarch egarch &quot;, &quot; &quot; ~ md ~ &quot; &quot;), &quot;model must be garch, tarch or egarch&quot;)
if md == &quot;garch&quot; &amp;&amp; nthr &gt; 0
  md = &quot;tarch&quot;                  # EViews: arch(p,q,thrsh=k) is a threshold model
endif
scalar mt = 0
string mlab = &quot;&quot;
if exists(archm) &amp;&amp; archm != &quot;&quot;
  string am = tolower(archm)
  errorif(!instring(&quot; var sd log &quot;, &quot; &quot; ~ am ~ &quot; &quot;), &quot;archm must be var, sd or log&quot;)
  mt = am == &quot;var&quot; ? 1 : (am == &quot;sd&quot; ? 2 : 3)
  mlab = am == &quot;var&quot; ? &quot;GARCH&quot; : (am == &quot;sd&quot; ? &quot;@SQRT(GARCH)&quot; : &quot;LOG(GARCH)&quot;)
endif
scalar gtype = md == &quot;garch&quot; ? 1 : (md == &quot;tarch&quot; ? 3 : 7)
scalar ng0 = gtype == 1 ? 0 : narch       # threshold terms gig estimates
scalar nt = nthr &lt; 0 ? ng0 : nthr
errorif(gtype == 3 &amp;&amp; nt == 0, &quot;a threshold model needs thrsh &gt;= 1&quot;)
strings tok = strsplit(spec)
series evg_y = ev_gen(tok[1], vars)
list X = null
strings xlab = array(0)
loop i = 2..nelem(tok)
  if tolower(tok[i]) == &quot;c&quot;
    list X += const
    xlab += &quot;C&quot;
  else
    string v = sprintf(&quot;evg_x%d&quot;, i)
    series @v = ev_gen(tok[i], vars)
    list X += @v
    xlab += toupper(tok[i])
  endif
endloop
if nelem(X) &gt; 0
  bundle m = gig_setup(evg_y, gtype, X)
else
  bundle m = gig_setup(evg_y, gtype)
endif
gig_set_pq(&amp;m, ngarch, narch)
string dst = exists(dist) ? tolower(dist) : &quot;normal&quot;
dst = dst == &quot;n&quot; ? &quot;normal&quot; : (dst == &quot;tdist&quot; ? &quot;t&quot; : dst)
errorif(!instring(&quot; normal t ged &quot;, &quot; &quot; ~ dst ~ &quot; &quot;), &quot;dist must be normal, t or ged&quot;)
scalar cdist = dst == &quot;t&quot; ? 1 : (dst == &quot;ged&quot; ? 2 : 0)
errorif(cdist &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; (mt &gt; 0 || nt != (gtype == 1 ? 0 : narch)), &quot;t/GED errors are available with gig's models (no ARCH-M, threshold order = ARCH order)&quot;)
if cdist &gt; 0
  gig_set_dist(&amp;m, cdist)
endif
gig_estimate(&amp;m, 0)
scalar failed = !inbundle(m, &quot;criteria&quot;)
if !failed &amp;&amp; inbundle(m, &quot;errcode&quot;)
  failed = m.errcode != 0
endif
if failed
  # like EViews: warn and let the program go on (b.failed = 1, no estimates)
  printf &quot;Warning: %s estimation of %s failed (no convergence)\n&quot;, toupper(md), toupper(tok[1])
  return _(kind = &quot;garch&quot;, failed = 1, model = md, spec = spec)
endif
scalar nm = nelem(X)
scalar nv0 = 1 + narch + ng0 + ngarch
# gig's layout: mean, omega, alpha (narch), gamma (narch, fixed at 0 for GARCH),
# beta (ngarch), then distribution parameters; the vcv covers the active ones
matrix pos = seq(1, nm + 1 + narch)
if gtype != 1
  pos ~= seq(nm + 2 + narch, nm + 1 + 2 * narch)
endif
pos ~= seq(nm + 2 + 2 * narch, nm + 1 + 2 * narch + ngarch)
if cdist &gt; 0
  pos ~= nm + 2 + 2 * narch + ngarch          # distribution parameter (t dof / GED shape)
endif
matrix act = m.active
matrix vpos = zeros(1, cols(pos))
loop i = 1..cols(pos)
  scalar pi = pos[i]
  vpos[i] = imaxc(act .= pi)
endloop
matrix c = m.coeff[pos]
if inbundle(m, &quot;vcv&quot;)
  matrix V = m.vcv[vpos, vpos]
else
  # EViews also reports estimates when the covariance cannot be computed
  printf &quot;Warning: the coefficient covariance could not be computed (singular Hessian)\n&quot;
  matrix V = mshape(NA, cols(pos), cols(pos))
endif
# gig's GJR: h = w + a(|e| - g e)^2 + b h  -&gt;  EViews TARCH:
# h = w + A e^2 + G e^2 (e &lt; 0) + b h, with A = a(1-g)^2, G = 4ag (delta method)
if gtype == 3
  matrix Jm = I(rows(c))
  loop i = 1..narch
    scalar ia = nm + 1 + i
    scalar ig = nm + 1 + narch + i
    scalar a = c[ia]
    scalar g = c[ig]
    Jm[ia, ia] = (1 - g)^2
    Jm[ia, ig] = -2 * a * (1 - g)
    Jm[ig, ia] = 4 * g
    Jm[ig, ig] = 4 * a
    c[ia] = a * (1 - g)^2
    c[ig] = 4 * a * g
  endloop
  V = Jm * V * Jm'
endif
scalar lnl = m.criteria[1]
scalar T = m.nobs
matrix hm = {m.h}
matrix um = {m.uhat}
series evg_o = obs
matrix tob = {evg_o}
matrix okr = ok(hm) .* ok(um)
hm = selifr(hm, okr)
um = selifr(um, okr)
tob = selifr(tob, okr)
string meth = &quot;ML ARCH - Normal distribution (gig, BFGS)&quot;
if mt &gt; 0 || nt != ng0
  # ARCH-in-mean or other threshold orders: own likelihood (EViews recursion),
  # started from the estimates above; covariance from the numerical Hessian
  list LL = evg_y X evg_o
  matrix Dm = {LL}
  matrix yv = Dm[, 1]
  matrix XM = {}
  if nm &gt; 0
    XM = Dm[, 2:1 + nm]
  endif
  tob = Dm[, cols(Dm)]
  matrix th = c[1:nm + 1 + narch]
  loop k = 1..nt
    scalar gk = k &lt;= ng0 ? c[nm + 1 + narch + k] : 0
    th |= gk
  endloop
  if ngarch &gt; 0
    th |= c[nm + 2 + narch + ng0:nm + 1 + narch + ng0 + ngarch]
  endif
  if mt &gt; 0
    th = 0 | th
  endif
  scalar h0 = meanc(um.^2)
  scalar eg = gtype == 7
  set bfgs_toler 1e-9
  set max_verbose off
  scalar lnl = BFGSmax(&amp;th, &quot;ev__garchobj(th, yv, XM, eg, nm, narch, nt, ngarch, mt, h0)&quot;)
  matrix H = numhess(th, &quot;ev__garchobj(th, yv, XM, eg, nm, narch, nt, ngarch, mt, h0)&quot;)
  catch matrix V = -inv(H)
  if $error
    matrix V = mshape(NA, rows(th), rows(th))
  endif
  if sumc(!ok(V)) &gt; 0 || minc(diag(V)) &lt;= 0
    printf &quot;Warning: the coefficient covariance could not be computed (singular Hessian)\n&quot;
    V = mshape(NA, rows(th), rows(th))
  endif
  matrix R = ev__garchh(th, yv, XM, eg, nm, narch, nt, ngarch, mt, h0)
  c = th
  um = R[, 2]
  hm = R[, 3]
  T = rows(yv)
  meth = &quot;ML ARCH - Normal distribution (BFGS, numerical Hessian)&quot;
endif
scalar nmp = nm + (mt &gt; 0)              # mean-equation coefficients shown
if mt &gt; 0
  strings xl2 = defarray(mlab)
  loop i = 1..nelem(xlab)
    xl2 += xlab[i]
  endloop
  xlab = xl2
endif
bundle b
b.kind = &quot;garch&quot;
b.failed = 0
b.model = md
b.archm = mt
b.spec = spec
b.depvar = toupper(tok[1])
b.method = cdist == 0 ? meth : strsub(meth, &quot;Normal distribution&quot;, cdist == 1 ? &quot;Student's t distribution&quot; : &quot;Generalized error distribution (GED)&quot;)
b.dist = dst
strings lab = array(0)
loop i = 1..rows(c)
  lab += sprintf(&quot;C(%d)&quot;, i)
endloop
if cdist &gt; 0
  lab[nelem(lab)] = cdist == 1 ? &quot;T-DIST. DOF&quot; : &quot;GED PARAMETER&quot;
endif
b.clabels = lab
b.xlab = xlab
b.nm = nmp
b.narch = narch
b.ngarch = ngarch
b.nthr = nt
b.coeff = c
b.vcv = V
b.stderr = sqrt(diag(V))
b.k = rows(c)
b.lnl = lnl
b.T = T
b.h = hm
b.uhat = um
b.tobs = tob
b.sample = sprintf(&quot;%s %s&quot;, obslabel(minc(b.tobs)), obslabel(maxc(b.tobs)))
b.estdate = strftime($now[1], &quot;%m/%d/%y   Time: %H:%M&quot;)
# variance equation as EViews writes it
string ve = sprintf(&quot;C(%d)&quot;, nmp + 1)
if gtype == 7
  loop i = 1..narch
    ve ~= sprintf(&quot; + C(%d)*ABS(RESID(-%d)/@SQRT(GARCH(-%d)))&quot;, nmp + 1 + i, i, i)
  endloop
  loop i = 1..nt
    ve ~= sprintf(&quot; + C(%d)*RESID(-%d)/@SQRT(GARCH(-%d))&quot;, nmp + 1 + narch + i, i, i)
  endloop
  loop i = 1..ngarch
    ve ~= sprintf(&quot; + C(%d)*LOG(GARCH(-%d))&quot;, nmp + 1 + narch + nt + i, i)
  endloop
  ve = &quot;LOG(GARCH) = &quot; ~ ve
else
  loop i = 1..narch
    ve ~= sprintf(&quot; + C(%d)*RESID(-%d)^2&quot;, nmp + 1 + i, i)
  endloop
  loop i = 1..nt
    ve ~= sprintf(&quot; + C(%d)*RESID(-%d)^2*(RESID(-%d)&lt;0)&quot;, nmp + 1 + narch + i, i, i)
  endloop
  loop i = 1..ngarch
    ve ~= sprintf(&quot; + C(%d)*GARCH(-%d)&quot;, nmp + 1 + narch + nt + i, i)
  endloop
  ve = &quot;GARCH = &quot; ~ ve
endif
b.vareq = ve
scalar n = b.T
b.aic = -2 * b.lnl / n + 2 * b.k / n
b.sc = -2 * b.lnl / n + b.k * log(n) / n
b.hq = -2 * b.lnl / n + 2 * b.k * log(log(n)) / n
if !quiet
  ev_garchprint(&amp;b)
endif
return b
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_garchprint" type="void">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="b" type="bundleref"/>
 </params>
<code>printf &quot;\nDependent Variable: %s\nMethod: %s\nDate: %s\n&quot;, b.depvar, b.method, b.estdate
printf &quot;Sample: %s\nIncluded observations: %d\n&quot;, b.sample, b.T
printf &quot;%s\n\n&quot;, b.vareq
ev__line(78)
printf &quot;%-26s%13s%13s%14s%12s\n&quot;, &quot;Variable&quot;, &quot;Coefficient&quot;, &quot;Std. Error&quot;, &quot;z-Statistic&quot;, &quot;Prob.&quot;
ev__line(78)
loop i = 1..b.nm
  scalar z = b.coeff[i] / b.stderr[i]
  printf &quot;%-26s%13.6f%13.6f%14.6f%12.4f\n&quot;, b.xlab[i], b.coeff[i], b.stderr[i], z, 2 * pvalue(z, abs(z))
endloop
printf &quot;\n%38s\n\n&quot;, &quot;Variance Equation&quot;
loop i = b.nm + 1..b.k
  scalar z = b.coeff[i] / b.stderr[i]
  printf &quot;%-26s%13.6f%13.6f%14.6f%12.4f\n&quot;, b.clabels[i], b.coeff[i], b.stderr[i], z, 2 * pvalue(z, abs(z))
endloop
ev__line(78)
printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f    %-24s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Log likelihood&quot;, b.lnl, &quot;Akaike info criterion&quot;, b.aic
printf &quot;%-22s%14s    %-24s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;&quot;, &quot;&quot;, &quot;Schwarz criterion&quot;, b.sc
printf &quot;%-22s%14s    %-24s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;&quot;, &quot;&quot;, &quot;Hannan-Quinn criter.&quot;, b.hq
ev__line(78)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_garchseries" type="series">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="b" type="bundle">
<description>ev_garch result</description>
  </param>
  <param name="what" type="string" optional="true">
<description>h (conditional variance) or resid</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code>string w = exists(what) ? tolower(what) : &quot;h&quot;
return ev__toseries(w == &quot;h&quot; ? b.h : b.uhat, b.tobs)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_unstack" type="matrix">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="x" type="series">
<description>Series of a balanced panel</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code># T x N matrix: one column per cross-section unit
errorif($datatype != 3, &quot;The current page is not a panel (use pagestruct first)&quot;)
scalar T = $pd
scalar N = $nobs / T
errorif(N != int(N), &quot;The panel must be balanced&quot;)
set skip_missing off
return mshape({x}, T, N)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_panelids" type="matrix">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="id" type="series">
<description>Cross-section identifier</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code># value of the identifier for each unit, in panel order
errorif($datatype != 3, &quot;The current page is not a panel&quot;)
set skip_missing off
matrix v = {id}
return v[seq(1, rows(v), $pd)]
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_panel" type="bundle">
 <params count="5">
  <param name="spec" type="string">
<description>Equation, e.g. y c x</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list">
<description>Series used (e.g. dataset)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="cx" type="string" optional="true">
<description>Cross-section effects: none, fixed or random</description>
  </param>
  <param name="perfe" type="bool" default="0">
<description>Period fixed effects</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
 </params>
<code>errorif($datatype != 3, &quot;The current page is not a panel (use pagestruct first)&quot;)
string ce = exists(cx) &amp;&amp; cx != &quot;&quot; ? tolower(cx) : &quot;none&quot;
ce = ce == &quot;f&quot; ? &quot;fixed&quot; : (ce == &quot;r&quot; ? &quot;random&quot; : ce)
errorif(!instring(&quot; none fixed random &quot;, &quot; &quot; ~ ce ~ &quot; &quot;), &quot;cx must be none, fixed or random&quot;)
strings tok = strsplit(spec)
series evp_y = ev_gen(tok[1], vars)
list X = null
strings xlab = array(0)
loop i = 2..nelem(tok)
  if tolower(tok[i]) == &quot;c&quot;
    list X += const
    xlab += &quot;C&quot;
  else
    string v = sprintf(&quot;evp_x%d&quot;, i)
    series @v = ev_gen(tok[i], vars)
    list X += @v
    xlab += toupper(tok[i])
  endif
endloop
errorif(ce != &quot;none&quot; &amp;&amp; !inlist(X, &quot;const&quot;), &quot;fixed and random effects need a constant (c)&quot;)
if ce == &quot;fixed&quot;
  if perfe
    panel evp_y X --fixed-effects --time-dummies --quiet
  else
    panel evp_y X --fixed-effects --quiet
  endif
elif ce == &quot;random&quot;
  if perfe
    panel evp_y X --random-effects --time-dummies --quiet
  else
    panel evp_y X --random-effects --quiet
  endif
else
  if perfe
    panel evp_y X --pooled --time-dummies --quiet
  else
    panel evp_y X --pooled --quiet
  endif
endif
scalar k = nelem(X)
bundle b
b.kind = &quot;panel&quot;
b.spec = spec
b.depvar = toupper(tok[1])
b.effects = ce
b.perfe = perfe
b.method = ce == &quot;random&quot; ? &quot;Panel EGLS (Cross-section random effects)&quot; : &quot;Panel Least Squares&quot;
b.xlab = xlab
b.coeff = $coeff[1:k]
b.stderr = $stderr[1:k]
b.vcv = $vcv[1:k, 1:k]
b.k = k
b.ktot = $ncoeff
b.T = $T
# some statistics are not defined for every estimator (random effects): NA then
scalar df = $df
catch scalar r2 = $rsq
if $error
  r2 = NA
endif
catch scalar ssr = $ess
if $error
  ssr = NA
endif
catch scalar se = $sigma
if $error
  se = NA
endif
catch scalar lnl = $lnl
if $error
  lnl = NA
endif
b.df = df
series evp_u = $uhat
series evp_f = $yhat
series evp_o = obs
list LL = evp_u evp_f evp_o
matrix D = {LL}
b.uhat = D[, 1]
b.yhat = D[, 2]
b.tobs = D[, 3]
matrix yy = D[, 1] + D[, 2]
if !ok(ssr)
  ssr = sumc(D[, 1].^2)
  se = sqrt(ssr / df)
endif
if !ok(r2)
  r2 = corr(yy, D[, 2])^2
endif
b.y = yy
b.r2 = r2
b.ssr = ssr
b.se = se
b.lnl = lnl
b.r2adj = 1 - (1 - r2) * (b.T - 1) / df
b.ymean = meanc(D[, 1] + D[, 2])
b.ysd = sdc(D[, 1] + D[, 2])
matrix u = D[, 1]
b.dw = sumc((u[2:] - u[1:rows(u)-1]).^2) / sumc(u.^2)    # across the stacked rows
# panel dimensions in the estimation sample
series evp_un = $unit
series evp_tt = $obsminor
list L2 = evp_y X evp_un evp_tt
matrix Z = {L2}
b.ncross = rows(values(Z[, cols(Z) - 1]))
b.nper = rows(values(Z[, cols(Z)]))
b.balanced = b.T == b.ncross * b.nper
b.tstat = b.coeff ./ b.stderr
matrix pv = zeros(k, 1)
loop i = 1..k
  pv[i] = 2 * pvalue(t, b.df, abs(b.tstat[i]))
endloop
b.pval = pv
b.aic = -2 * b.lnl / b.T + 2 * b.ktot / b.T
b.sc = -2 * b.lnl / b.T + b.ktot * log(b.T) / b.T
b.estdate = strftime($now[1], &quot;%m/%d/%y   Time: %H:%M&quot;)
if !quiet
  ev_panelprint(&amp;b)
endif
return b
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_panelprint" type="void">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="b" type="bundleref"/>
 </params>
<code>printf &quot;\nDependent Variable: %s\nMethod: %s\nDate: %s\n&quot;, b.depvar, b.method, b.estdate
printf &quot;Periods included: %d\nCross-sections included: %d\n&quot;, b.nper, b.ncross
printf &quot;Total panel (%s) observations: %d\n\n&quot;, b.balanced ? &quot;balanced&quot; : &quot;unbalanced&quot;, b.T
ev__line(78)
printf &quot;%-26s%13s%13s%14s%12s\n&quot;, &quot;Variable&quot;, &quot;Coefficient&quot;, &quot;Std. Error&quot;, &quot;t-Statistic&quot;, &quot;Prob.&quot;
ev__line(78)
loop i = 1..b.k
  printf &quot;%-26s%13.6f%13.6f%14.6f%12.4f\n&quot;, b.xlab[i], b.coeff[i], b.stderr[i], b.tstat[i], b.pval[i]
endloop
ev__line(78)
if b.effects != &quot;none&quot; || b.perfe
  printf &quot;%38s\n&quot;, &quot;Effects Specification&quot;
  ev__line(78)
  if b.effects == &quot;fixed&quot;
    printf &quot;Cross-section fixed (dummy variables)\n&quot;
  elif b.effects == &quot;random&quot;
    printf &quot;Cross-section random\n&quot;
  endif
  if b.perfe
    printf &quot;Period fixed (dummy variables)\n&quot;
  endif
  ev__line(78)
endif
printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f    %-24s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;R-squared&quot;, b.r2, &quot;Mean dependent var&quot;, b.ymean
printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f    %-24s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Adjusted R-squared&quot;, b.r2adj, &quot;S.D. dependent var&quot;, b.ysd
printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f    %-24s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;S.E. of regression&quot;, b.se, &quot;Akaike info criterion&quot;, b.aic
printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f    %-24s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Sum squared resid&quot;, b.ssr, &quot;Schwarz criterion&quot;, b.sc
printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f    %-24s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Log likelihood&quot;, b.lnl, &quot;Durbin-Watson stat&quot;, b.dw
ev__line(78)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_stackids" type="strings">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="pattern" type="string">
<description>Pool series name, e.g. gdp_?</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list">
<description>Series (e.g. dataset)</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code># identifiers ? of the series that match the pattern, in workfile order
errorif(!instring(pattern, &quot;?&quot;), &quot;The pattern needs a ? for the identifier&quot;)
strings p2 = strsplit(pattern, &quot;?&quot;)
string lead = nelem(p2) &gt; 0 ? p2[1] : &quot;&quot;
string tail = nelem(p2) &gt; 1 ? p2[2] : &quot;&quot;
scalar la = strlen(lead)
scalar lt = strlen(tail)
strings nm = varnames(vars)
strings ids = array(0)
loop i = 1..nelem(nm)
  string x = toupper(nm[i])
  scalar n = strlen(x)
  if n &gt; la + lt
    if substr(x, 1, la) == toupper(lead) || la == 0
      if lt == 0 || substr(x, n - lt + 1, n) == toupper(tail)
        ids += substr(nm[i], la + 1, n - lt)
      endif
    endif
  endif
endloop
errorif(nelem(ids) == 0, &quot;No series match &quot; ~ pattern)
return ids
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_stack" type="matrix">
 <params count="3">
  <param name="pattern" type="string">
<description>Pool series name, e.g. gdp_?</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list">
<description>Series (e.g. dataset)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="ids" type="strings" optional="true">
<description>Identifiers (default: those of ev_stackids)</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code># T x N matrix: column j holds the series for identifier j (NA where missing)
strings u = exists(ids) ? ids : ev_stackids(pattern, vars)
strings nm = varnames(vars)
set skip_missing off
matrix M = mshape(NA, $nobs, nelem(u))
loop j = 1..nelem(u)
  string want = toupper(strsub(pattern, &quot;?&quot;, u[j]))
  loop i = 1..nelem(nm)
    if toupper(nm[i]) == want
      series evs_x = vars[i]
      M[, j] = {evs_x}
      break
    endif
  endloop
endloop
return M
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_tsls" type="bundle">
 <params count="5">
  <param name="spec" type="string">
<description>Equation and instruments, e.g. y c x @ c z1 z2</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list">
<description>Series used (e.g. dataset)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="cov" type="string" optional="true">
<description>ordinary or white</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
  <param name="liml" type="bool" default="0">
<description>Limited information maximum likelihood</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code>errorif(!instring(spec, &quot;@&quot;), &quot;Give the instruments after @, e.g. y c x @ c z&quot;)
strings parts = strsplit(spec, &quot;@&quot;)
strings tok = strsplit(strstrip(parts[1]))
strings itok = strsplit(strstrip(parts[2]))
string cv = exists(cov) ? tolower(cov) : &quot;ordinary&quot;
series evt_y = ev_gen(tok[1], vars)
list X = null
strings lab = array(0)
scalar hascon = 0
loop i = 2..nelem(tok)
  if tolower(tok[i]) == &quot;c&quot;
    list X += const
    lab += &quot;C&quot;
    hascon = 1
  else
    string v = sprintf(&quot;evt_x%d&quot;, i)
    series @v = ev_gen(tok[i], vars)
    list X += @v
    lab += toupper(tok[i])
  endif
endloop
list Z = null
string itxt = &quot;&quot;
loop i = 1..nelem(itok)
  itxt ~= &quot; &quot; ~ toupper(itok[i])
  if tolower(itok[i]) == &quot;c&quot;
    list Z += const
  else
    string v = sprintf(&quot;evt_z%d&quot;, i)
    series @v = ev_gen(itok[i], vars)
    list Z += @v
  endif
endloop
errorif(nelem(Z) &lt; nelem(X), &quot;Order condition: at least as many instruments as regressors are needed&quot;)
scalar n0 = $nobs
if liml
  tsls evt_y X ; Z --liml --quiet
elif cv == &quot;white&quot;
  set force_hc on
  tsls evt_y X ; Z --robust --quiet
else
  tsls evt_y X ; Z --quiet
endif
bundle b
b.kind = &quot;tsls&quot;
b.iv = 1
b.spec = spec
b.method = liml ? &quot;LIML / K-Class&quot; : &quot;Two-Stage Least Squares&quot;
b.eqline = &quot;Instrument specification:&quot; ~ itxt
b.depvar = toupper(tok[1])
b.labels = lab
b.covtype = cv
b.coeff = $coeff
b.stderr = $stderr
b.vcv = $vcv
b.T = $T
b.k = $ncoeff
catch scalar r2 = $rsq          # not defined after LIML
if $error
  r2 = NA
endif
b.rsq = r2
b.adjrsq = 1 - (1 - r2) * ($T - 1) / ($T - $ncoeff)
b.sigma = $sigma
b.ssr = $ess
catch scalar dwv = $dw
if $error
  dwv = NA
endif
b.dw = dwv
b.hascon = hascon
b.adjusted = $T &lt; n0
b.estdate = strftime($now[1], &quot;%m/%d/%y   Time: %H:%M&quot;)
series evt_u = $uhat
series evt_f = $yhat
smpl ok(evt_u) --restrict
b.y = {evt_y}
b.X = {X}
matrix Zm = {Z}
b.uhat = {evt_u}
b.yhat = {evt_f}
series evt_o = obs
b.tobs = {evt_o}
b.sample = sprintf(&quot;%s %s&quot;, obslabel($t1), obslabel($t2))
scalar n = b.T
scalar k = b.k
matrix d = b.y - meanc(b.y)
b.meany = meanc(b.y)
b.sdy = sqrt(d'd / (n - 1))
# J-statistic (Sargan form, as EViews reports for TSLS) and instrument rank
matrix u = b.uhat
b.instrank = rank(Zm)
b.J = qform(u', Zm * inv(Zm'Zm) * Zm') / (u'u / n)
b.Jdf = b.instrank - k
b.Jp = NA
if b.Jdf &gt; 0
  b.Jp = pvalue(c, b.Jdf, b.J)
endif
b.lnl = NA
b.aic = NA
b.sc = NA
b.hq = NA
b.F = NA
b.Fp = NA
b.tstat = b.coeff ./ b.stderr
matrix p = zeros(k, 1)
loop i = 1..k
  p[i] = 2 * pvalue(t, n - k, abs(b.tstat[i]))
endloop
b.pval = p
if !quiet
  ev_print(&amp;b)
endif
return b
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_binary" type="bundle">
 <params count="4">
  <param name="spec" type="string">
<description>Equation, e.g. y c x (y is 0/1)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list">
<description>Series used (e.g. dataset)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="dist" type="string" optional="true">
<description>logit (l) or probit (p)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
 </params>
<code>string ds = exists(dist) ? tolower(dist) : &quot;logit&quot;
ds = ds == &quot;l&quot; ? &quot;logit&quot; : (ds == &quot;p&quot; || ds == &quot;n&quot; ? &quot;probit&quot; : ds)
errorif(ds != &quot;logit&quot; &amp;&amp; ds != &quot;probit&quot;, &quot;d= must be l (logit) or p (probit)&quot;)
strings tok = strsplit(spec)
series evb_y = ev_gen(tok[1], vars)
list X = null
strings lab = array(0)
loop i = 2..nelem(tok)
  if tolower(tok[i]) == &quot;c&quot;
    list X += const
    lab += &quot;C&quot;
  else
    string v = sprintf(&quot;evb_x%d&quot;, i)
    series @v = ev_gen(tok[i], vars)
    list X += @v
    lab += toupper(tok[i])
  endif
endloop
scalar n0 = $nobs
if ds == &quot;logit&quot;
  logit evb_y X --quiet
else
  probit evb_y X --quiet
endif
bundle b
b.kind = &quot;binary&quot;
b.dist = ds
b.spec = spec
b.depvar = toupper(tok[1])
b.labels = lab
b.method = ds == &quot;logit&quot; ? &quot;ML - Binary Logit (Newton-Raphson)&quot; : &quot;ML - Binary Probit (Newton-Raphson)&quot;
b.coeff = $coeff
b.stderr = $stderr
b.vcv = $vcv
b.lnl = $lnl
b.T = $T
b.k = $ncoeff
b.adjusted = $T &lt; n0
series evb_p = $yhat
series evb_o = obs
list L = evb_y evb_p evb_o
matrix D = {L}
b.y = D[, 1]
b.yhat = D[, 2]                  # fitted probabilities
b.uhat = D[, 1] - D[, 2]
b.tobs = D[, 3]
b.sample = sprintf(&quot;%s %s&quot;, obslabel(minc(b.tobs)), obslabel(maxc(b.tobs)))
errorif(sumc((b.y .!= 0) .* (b.y .!= 1)) &gt; 0, &quot;The dependent variable must be 0 or 1&quot;)
scalar n = b.T
scalar k = b.k
scalar n1 = sumc(b.y)
scalar pbar = n1 / n
b.n1 = n1
b.n0 = n - n1
b.lnl0 = n1 * log(pbar) + (n - n1) * log(1 - pbar)       # constant-only model
b.mcfadden = 1 - b.lnl / b.lnl0
b.LR = 2 * (b.lnl - b.lnl0)
b.LRdf = k - 1
b.LRp = pvalue(c, k - 1, b.LR)
b.avglnl = b.lnl / n
b.meany = pbar
b.sdy = sqrt(pbar * (1 - pbar) * n / (n - 1))
b.ssr = sumc(b.uhat.^2)
b.sigma = sqrt(b.ssr / (n - k))
b.aic = -2 * b.lnl / n + 2 * k / n
b.sc = -2 * b.lnl / n + k * log(n) / n
b.hq = -2 * b.lnl / n + 2 * k * log(log(n)) / n
b.tstat = b.coeff ./ b.stderr
b.pval = 2 * cnorm(-abs(b.tstat))
b.estdate = strftime($now[1], &quot;%m/%d/%y   Time: %H:%M&quot;)
if !quiet
  ev_binaryprint(&amp;b)
endif
return b
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_binaryprint" type="void">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="b" type="bundleref"/>
 </params>
<code>printf &quot;\nDependent Variable: %s\nMethod: %s\nDate: %s\n&quot;, b.depvar, b.method, b.estdate
printf &quot;Sample%s: %s\nIncluded observations: %d\n\n&quot;, b.adjusted ? &quot; (adjusted)&quot; : &quot;&quot;, b.sample, b.T
ev__line(78)
printf &quot;%-26s%13s%13s%14s%12s\n&quot;, &quot;Variable&quot;, &quot;Coefficient&quot;, &quot;Std. Error&quot;, &quot;z-Statistic&quot;, &quot;Prob.&quot;
ev__line(78)
loop i = 1..b.k
  printf &quot;%-26s%13.6f%13.6f%14.6f%12.4f\n&quot;, b.labels[i], b.coeff[i], b.stderr[i], b.tstat[i], b.pval[i]
endloop
ev__line(78)
printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f    %-24s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;McFadden R-squared&quot;, b.mcfadden, &quot;Mean dependent var&quot;, b.meany
printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f    %-24s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;S.D. dependent var&quot;, b.sdy, &quot;S.E. of regression&quot;, b.sigma
printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f    %-24s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Akaike info criterion&quot;, b.aic, &quot;Sum squared resid&quot;, b.ssr
printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f    %-24s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Schwarz criterion&quot;, b.sc, &quot;Log likelihood&quot;, b.lnl
printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f    %-24s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Hannan-Quinn criter.&quot;, b.hq, &quot;Restr. log likelihood&quot;, b.lnl0
printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f    %-24s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;LR statistic&quot;, b.LR, &quot;Avg. log likelihood&quot;, b.avglnl
printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Prob(LR statistic)&quot;, b.LRp
ev__line(78)
printf &quot;%-22s%14d    %-24s%14d\n&quot;, &quot;Obs with Dep=0&quot;, b.n0, &quot;Total obs&quot;, b.T
printf &quot;%-22s%14d\n&quot;, &quot;Obs with Dep=1&quot;, b.n1
ev__line(78)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_ardl" type="bundle">
 <params count="7">
  <param name="spec" type="string">
<description>Dependent variable and regressors, e.g. y x1 x2 [@ fixed]</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list">
<description>Series used (e.g. dataset)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="deplags" type="int" min="1" default="4">
<description>Maximum lags of the dependent variable</description>
  </param>
  <param name="reglags" type="int" min="0" default="4">
<description>Maximum lags of the regressors</description>
  </param>
  <param name="ic" type="string" optional="true">
<description>aic, sic or hq</description>
  </param>
  <param name="trend" type="string" optional="true">
<description>none, const or linear</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
 </params>
<code>string icr = exists(ic) ? tolower(ic) : &quot;aic&quot;
icr = icr == &quot;bic&quot; ? &quot;sic&quot; : icr
errorif(!instring(&quot; aic sic hq &quot;, &quot; &quot; ~ icr ~ &quot; &quot;), &quot;ic must be aic, sic or hq&quot;)
string tr = exists(trend) ? tolower(trend) : &quot;const&quot;
errorif(!instring(&quot; none const linear &quot;, &quot; &quot; ~ tr ~ &quot; &quot;), &quot;trend must be none, const or linear&quot;)
strings parts = strsplit(spec, &quot;@&quot;)
strings tok = strsplit(strstrip(parts[1]))
strings ftok = array(0)
if nelem(parts) &gt; 1
  ftok = strsplit(strstrip(parts[2]))
endif
scalar kx = nelem(tok) - 1
errorif(kx &lt; 1, &quot;ARDL needs at least one regressor&quot;)
# all candidate columns, over the current sample
set skip_missing off
series eva_y = ev_gen(tok[1], vars)
matrix Y = {eva_y}
matrix YL = {}
loop j = 1..deplags
  series eva_t = ev_gen(ev__lagx(tok[1], j, vars), vars)
  YL ~= {eva_t}
endloop
matrices XL = array(kx)
loop i = 1..kx
  matrix M = {}
  loop j = 0..reglags
    series eva_t = ev_gen(ev__lagx(tok[i+1], j, vars), vars)
    M ~= {eva_t}
  endloop
  XL[i] = M
endloop
matrix F = {}
strings flab = array(0)
loop i = 1..nelem(ftok)
  if tolower(ftok[i]) != &quot;c&quot;
    series eva_t = ev_gen(ftok[i], vars)
    F ~= {eva_t}
    flab += toupper(ftok[i])
  endif
endloop
series eva_o = obs
matrix tob = {eva_o}
matrix D = {}
if tr != &quot;none&quot;
  series eva_c = 1
  D ~= {eva_c}
endif
if tr == &quot;linear&quot;
  series eva_tt = obs - 1
  D ~= {eva_tt}
endif
# common sample: rows where every candidate column is available (as EViews)
matrix all = Y ~ YL ~ F
loop i = 1..kx
  all ~= XL[i]
endloop
matrix okr = sumr(!ok(all)) .= 0
Y = selifr(Y, okr)
YL = selifr(YL, okr)
loop i = 1..kx
  XL[i] = selifr(XL[i], okr)
endloop
if rows(F)
  F = selifr(F, okr)
endif
if rows(D)
  D = selifr(D, okr)
endif
tob = selifr(tob, okr)
scalar n = rows(Y)
# search over p = 1..deplags and q_i = 0..reglags
scalar nq = reglags + 1
scalar ncomb = deplags * nq^kx
scalar best = 1e300
matrix bestq = {}
scalar bestp = 1
matrix tab = {}
loop c = 0..ncomb - 1
  scalar r = c
  scalar p = 1 + (r % deplags)
  r = floor(r / deplags)
  matrix q = zeros(1, kx)
  loop i = 1..kx
    q[i] = r % nq
    r = floor(r / nq)
  endloop
  matrix W = YL[, 1:p] ~ F ~ D
  loop i = 1..kx
    matrix Mi = XL[i]
    W ~= Mi[, 1:q[i] + 1]
  endloop
  matrix e = Y - W * mols(Y, W)
  scalar v = ev__ic(e'e, n, cols(W), icr)
  tab |= p ~ q ~ v
  if v &lt; best
    best = v
    bestp = p
    bestq = q
  endif
endloop
# final model, EViews order: Y(-1..p), each X with its lags, fixed regressors, C, @TREND
matrix W = YL[, 1:bestp]
strings lab = array(0)
loop j = 1..bestp
  lab += sprintf(&quot;%s(-%d)&quot;, toupper(tok[1]), j)
endloop
loop i = 1..kx
  matrix Mi = XL[i]
  W ~= Mi[, 1:bestq[i] + 1]
  loop j = 0..bestq[i]
    lab += j == 0 ? toupper(tok[i+1]) : sprintf(&quot;%s(-%d)&quot;, toupper(tok[i+1]), j)
  endloop
endloop
W ~= F
loop i = 1..nelem(flab)
  lab += flab[i]
endloop
if tr != &quot;none&quot;
  W ~= D[, 1]
  lab += &quot;C&quot;
endif
if tr == &quot;linear&quot;
  W ~= D[, 2]
  lab += &quot;@TREND&quot;
endif
matrix bh = mols(Y, W, &amp;e)
scalar k = cols(W)
scalar s2 = e'e / (n - k)
matrix V = s2 * inv(W'W)
bundle b
b.kind = &quot;ardl&quot;
b.spec = spec
b.depvar = toupper(tok[1])
b.method = &quot;ARDL&quot;
b.labels = lab
b.p = bestp
b.q = bestq
b.ic = icr
b.trend = tr
b.kx = kx
b.ncomb = ncomb
b.models = tab
string sel = sprintf(&quot;ARDL(%d&quot;, bestp)
loop i = 1..kx
  sel ~= sprintf(&quot;, %d&quot;, bestq[i])
endloop
b.selected = sel ~ &quot;)&quot;
b.eqline = sprintf(&quot;Dependent lags: %d (Automatic selection)\nAutomatic-lag linear regressors (%d max. lags):&quot;, deplags, reglags)
loop i = 1..kx
  b.eqline = b.eqline ~ &quot; &quot; ~ toupper(tok[i+1])
endloop
b.eqline = b.eqline ~ sprintf(&quot;\nModel selection method: %s\nNumber of models evaluated: %d\nSelected Model: %s&quot;, icr == &quot;aic&quot; ? &quot;Akaike info criterion (AIC)&quot; : (icr == &quot;sic&quot; ? &quot;Schwarz criterion (SIC)&quot; : &quot;Hannan-Quinn criterion (HQ)&quot;), ncomb, b.selected)
b.coeff = bh
b.vcv = V
b.stderr = sqrt(diag(V))
b.T = n
b.k = k
b.y = Y
b.X = W
b.uhat = e
b.yhat = Y - e
b.tobs = tob
b.sample = sprintf(&quot;%s %s&quot;, obslabel(minc(tob)), obslabel(maxc(tob)))
b.adjusted = 1
b.covtype = &quot;ordinary&quot;
b.hascon = tr != &quot;none&quot;
matrix d = Y - meanc(Y)
b.ssr = e'e
b.rsq = 1 - b.ssr / (d'd)
b.adjrsq = 1 - (1 - b.rsq) * (n - 1) / (n - k)
b.sigma = sqrt(s2)
b.lnl = -n / 2 * (1 + log(2 * $pi) + log(b.ssr / n))
b.meany = meanc(Y)
b.sdy = sqrt(d'd / (n - 1))
b.aic = -2 * b.lnl / n + 2 * k / n
b.sc = -2 * b.lnl / n + k * log(n) / n
b.hq = -2 * b.lnl / n + 2 * k * log(log(n)) / n
b.dw = sumc((e[2:] - e[1:n-1]).^2) / b.ssr
scalar kc = k - (tr != &quot;none&quot;)
b.F = NA
if b.hascon &amp;&amp; k &gt; 1
  b.F = (b.rsq / (k - 1)) / ((1 - b.rsq) / (n - k))
endif
b.Fp = ok(b.F) ? pvalue(F, k - 1, n - k, b.F) : NA
b.tstat = bh ./ b.stderr
matrix pv = zeros(k, 1)
loop i = 1..k
  pv[i] = 2 * pvalue(t, n - k, abs(b.tstat[i]))
endloop
b.pval = pv
b.estdate = strftime($now[1], &quot;%m/%d/%y   Time: %H:%M&quot;)
ev__ardllr(&amp;b, XL, YL, F, D)
if !quiet
  ev_print(&amp;b)
endif
return b
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_ardlprint" type="void">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="b" type="bundleref"/>
 </params>
<code>ev_print(&amp;b)
printf &quot;\nLevels Equation (long-run coefficients)\n&quot;
ev__line(78)
printf &quot;%-26s%13s%13s%14s%12s\n&quot;, &quot;Variable&quot;, &quot;Coefficient&quot;, &quot;Std. Error&quot;, &quot;t-Statistic&quot;, &quot;Prob.&quot;
ev__line(78)
loop i = 1..rows(b.lr)
  scalar tt = b.lr[i] / b.lr_se[i]
  printf &quot;%-26s%13.6f%13.6f%14.6f%12.4f\n&quot;, b.lr_labels[i], b.lr[i], b.lr_se[i], tt, 2 * pvalue(t, b.T - b.k, abs(tt))
endloop
ev__line(78)
ev_boundsprint(&amp;b)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_boundsprint" type="void">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="b" type="bundleref"/>
 </params>
<code>printf &quot;\nF-Bounds Test           Null Hypothesis: No levels relationship\n&quot;
ev__line(78)
printf &quot;%-22s%12s    %10s%12s%12s\n&quot;, &quot;Test Statistic&quot;, &quot;Value&quot;, &quot;Signif.&quot;, &quot;I(0)&quot;, &quot;I(1)&quot;
ev__line(78)
printf &quot;%-22s%12.6f    %10s%12.2f%12.2f\n&quot;, &quot;F-statistic&quot;, b.bounds_F, &quot;10%&quot;, b.bounds_cv[1], b.bounds_cv[2]
printf &quot;%-22s%12d    %10s%12.2f%12.2f\n&quot;, &quot;k&quot;, b.bounds_k, &quot;5%&quot;, b.bounds_cv[3], b.bounds_cv[4]
printf &quot;%-22s%12s    %10s%12.2f%12.2f\n&quot;, &quot;&quot;, &quot;&quot;, &quot;1%&quot;, b.bounds_cv[5], b.bounds_cv[6]
printf &quot;Asymptotic critical values: Pesaran, Shin and Smith (2001), case III\n&quot;
ev__line(78)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_hettest" type="bundle">
 <params count="4">
  <param name="b" type="bundle">
<description>ev_ls result</description>
  </param>
  <param name="htype" type="string" optional="true">
<description>bpg, harvey, glejser, arch or white</description>
  </param>
  <param name="nlag" type="int" min="1" default="1">
<description>Lags for the ARCH test</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
 </params>
<code>errorif(!inbundle(b, &quot;X&quot;), &quot;hettest needs a least squares equation (ev_ls)&quot;)
string ty = exists(htype) ? tolower(htype) : &quot;bpg&quot;
errorif(!instring(&quot; bpg harvey glejser arch white &quot;, &quot; &quot; ~ ty ~ &quot; &quot;), &quot;type must be bpg, harvey, glejser, arch or white&quot;)
matrix e = b.uhat
scalar n = rows(e)
matrix Z = b.X
if !b.hascon
  Z = ones(n, 1) ~ Z
endif
matrix v = {}
if ty == &quot;bpg&quot;
  v = e.^2
elif ty == &quot;harvey&quot;
  v = log(e.^2)
elif ty == &quot;glejser&quot;
  v = abs(e)
elif ty == &quot;arch&quot;
  matrix e2 = e.^2
  v = e2[nlag + 1:n]
  matrix Z = ones(n - nlag, 1)
  loop j = 1..nlag
    Z ~= e2[nlag + 1 - j:n - j]
  endloop
else
  # White: levels, squares and cross products of the regressors
  matrix X = b.X
  matrix W = ones(n, 1)
  loop i = 1..cols(X)
    if sdc(X[, i]) &gt; 0
      W ~= X[, i]
    endif
  endloop
  scalar m0 = cols(W)
  loop i = 2..m0
    loop j = i..m0
      W ~= W[, i] .* W[, j]
    endloop
  endloop
  v = e.^2
  Z = W
endif
bundle a = ev__olsr(v, Z)
scalar m = cols(Z) - 1
scalar na = rows(v)
bundle r
r.type = ty
r.F = (a.rsq / m) / ((1 - a.rsq) / (na - m - 1))
r.Fp = pvalue(F, m, na - m - 1, r.F)
r.obsr2 = na * a.rsq
r.obsr2p = pvalue(c, m, r.obsr2)
r.df = m
if ty == &quot;bpg&quot;
  # scaled explained SS of e^2 / sigma^2 on Z
  scalar s2 = e'e / n
  matrix w = e.^2 / s2
  matrix d = w - meanc(w)
  bundle a2 = ev__olsr(w, Z)
  r.sess = (d'd - a2.ssr) / 2
  r.sessp = pvalue(c, m, r.sess)
elif ty == &quot;harvey&quot; || ty == &quot;glejser&quot;
  matrix d = v - meanc(v)
  r.sess = ty == &quot;harvey&quot; ? (d'd - a.ssr) / 4.9348 : NA    # Harvey: var(log chi2_1) = pi^2/2
  r.sessp = ok(r.sess) ? pvalue(c, m, r.sess) : NA
endif
if !quiet
  string tn = ty == &quot;bpg&quot; ? &quot;Breusch-Pagan-Godfrey&quot; : (ty == &quot;harvey&quot; ? &quot;Harvey&quot; : (ty == &quot;glejser&quot; ? &quot;Glejser&quot; : (ty == &quot;arch&quot; ? &quot;ARCH&quot; : &quot;White&quot;)))
  printf &quot;\nHeteroskedasticity Test: %s\n&quot;, tn
  ev__line(78)
  ev__teststat(&quot;F-statistic&quot;, r.F, sprintf(&quot;Prob. F(%d,%d)&quot;, m, na - m - 1), r.Fp)
  ev__teststat(&quot;Obs*R-squared&quot;, r.obsr2, sprintf(&quot;Prob. Chi-Square(%d)&quot;, m), r.obsr2p)
  if inbundle(r, &quot;sess&quot;) &amp;&amp; ok(r.sess)
    ev__teststat(&quot;Scaled explained SS&quot;, r.sess, sprintf(&quot;Prob. Chi-Square(%d)&quot;, m), r.sessp)
  endif
  ev__line(78)
endif
return r
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_reset" type="bundle">
 <params count="3">
  <param name="b" type="bundle">
<description>ev_ls result</description>
  </param>
  <param name="nfit" type="int" min="1" default="1">
<description>Number of fitted terms</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
 </params>
<code>errorif(!inbundle(b, &quot;X&quot;), &quot;RESET needs a least squares equation (ev_ls)&quot;)
matrix y = b.y
matrix X = b.X
matrix f = b.yhat
matrix Xa = X
loop j = 1..nfit
  Xa ~= f.^(j + 1)
endloop
bundle u = ev__olsr(y, Xa)
scalar n = rows(y)
scalar ku = cols(Xa)
bundle r
r.F = ((b.ssr - u.ssr) / nfit) / (u.ssr / (n - ku))
r.Fp = pvalue(F, nfit, n - ku, r.F)
r.LR = n * log(b.ssr / u.ssr)
r.LRp = pvalue(c, nfit, r.LR)
if nfit == 1
  matrix V = u.ssr / (n - ku) * inv(Xa'Xa)
  r.t = u.coeff[ku] / sqrt(V[ku, ku])
  r.tp = 2 * pvalue(t, n - ku, abs(r.t))
endif
if !quiet
  printf &quot;\nRamsey RESET Test\nOmitted Variables: Powers of fitted values from 2 to %d\n&quot;, nfit + 1
  ev__line(78)
  printf &quot;%-26s%12s    %-10s%14s\n&quot;, &quot;&quot;, &quot;Value&quot;, &quot;df&quot;, &quot;Probability&quot;
  if nfit == 1
    printf &quot;%-26s%12.6f    %-10d%14.4f\n&quot;, &quot;t-statistic&quot;, r.t, n - ku, r.tp
  endif
  printf &quot;%-26s%12.6f    %-10s%14.4f\n&quot;, &quot;F-statistic&quot;, r.F, sprintf(&quot;(%d, %d)&quot;, nfit, n - ku), r.Fp
  printf &quot;%-26s%12.6f    %-10d%14.4f\n&quot;, &quot;Likelihood ratio&quot;, r.LR, nfit, r.LRp
  ev__line(78)
endif
return r
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_chow" type="bundle">
 <params count="4">
  <param name="b" type="bundle">
<description>ev_ls result</description>
  </param>
  <param name="dates" type="string">
<description>Breakpoint date(s), e.g. 1990:1 2000:1</description>
  </param>
  <param name="forecast" type="bool" default="0">
<description>Chow forecast test (one date)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
 </params>
<code>errorif(!inbundle(b, &quot;X&quot;), &quot;The Chow test needs a least squares equation (ev_ls)&quot;)
matrix y = b.y
matrix X = b.X
matrix tob = b.tobs
scalar n = rows(y)
scalar k = cols(X)
strings dt = strsplit(dates)
matrix brk = {}
loop i = 1..nelem(dt)
  scalar o = obsnum(dt[i])
  errorif(!ok(o), &quot;Unknown date &quot; ~ dt[i])
  brk ~= o
endloop
bundle r
if forecast
  errorif(cols(brk) != 1, &quot;The forecast test takes one date&quot;)
  matrix m1 = tob .&lt; brk[1]
  scalar n1 = sumc(m1)
  scalar n2 = n - n1
  errorif(n1 &lt;= k || n2 &lt; 1, &quot;The breakpoint leaves too few observations&quot;)
  bundle a1 = ev__olsr(selifr(y, m1), selifr(X, m1))
  r.F = ((b.ssr - a1.ssr) / n2) / (a1.ssr / (n1 - k))
  r.Fdf1 = n2
  r.Fdf2 = n1 - k
  r.Fp = pvalue(F, n2, n1 - k, r.F)
  r.LR = n * log(b.ssr / a1.ssr)
  r.LRp = pvalue(c, n2, r.LR)
  if !quiet
    printf &quot;\nChow Forecast Test\nEquation: %s\nTest predictions for observations from %s to %s\n&quot;, b.spec, dt[1], obslabel(maxc(tob))
    ev__line(78)
    printf &quot;%-26s%12s    %-10s%14s\n&quot;, &quot;&quot;, &quot;Value&quot;, &quot;df&quot;, &quot;Probability&quot;
    printf &quot;%-26s%12.6f    %-10s%14.4f\n&quot;, &quot;F-statistic&quot;, r.F, sprintf(&quot;(%d, %d)&quot;, n2, n1 - k), r.Fp
    printf &quot;%-26s%12.6f    %-10d%14.4f\n&quot;, &quot;Likelihood ratio&quot;, r.LR, n2, r.LRp
    ev__line(78)
  endif
  return r
endif
# breakpoint test: separate regressions in each subsample
matrix cuts = brk ~ 1e10
scalar lo = -1e10
scalar ssru = 0
scalar lnlu = 0
loop i = 1..cols(cuts)
  matrix m = (tob .&gt;= lo) .* (tob .&lt; cuts[i])
  errorif(sumc(m) &lt;= k, &quot;A subsample has too few observations for the Chow test&quot;)
  bundle a = ev__olsr(selifr(y, m), selifr(X, m))
  ssru += a.ssr
  lo = cuts[i]
endloop
scalar ns = cols(cuts)
scalar q = (ns - 1) * k
r.F = ((b.ssr - ssru) / q) / (ssru / (n - ns * k))
r.Fdf1 = q
r.Fdf2 = n - ns * k
r.Fp = pvalue(F, q, n - ns * k, r.F)
r.LR = n * log(b.ssr / ssru)
r.LRp = pvalue(c, q, r.LR)
r.Wald = q * r.F
r.Waldp = pvalue(c, q, r.Wald)
if !quiet
  printf &quot;\nChow Breakpoint Test: %s\nNull Hypothesis: No breaks at specified breakpoints\n&quot;, dates
  printf &quot;Equation Sample: %s\n&quot;, b.sample
  ev__line(78)
  ev__teststat(&quot;F-statistic&quot;, r.F, sprintf(&quot;Prob. F(%d,%d)&quot;, q, n - ns * k), r.Fp)
  ev__teststat(&quot;Log likelihood ratio&quot;, r.LR, sprintf(&quot;Prob. Chi-Square(%d)&quot;, q), r.LRp)
  ev__teststat(&quot;Wald Statistic&quot;, r.Wald, sprintf(&quot;Prob. Chi-Square(%d)&quot;, q), r.Waldp)
  ev__line(78)
endif
return r
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_testadd" type="bundle">
 <params count="4">
  <param name="b" type="bundle">
<description>ev_ls result</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list">
<description>Series used (e.g. dataset)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="adds" type="string">
<description>Series to add, e.g. x2 log(z)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
 </params>
<code>errorif(!inbundle(b, &quot;X&quot;), &quot;testadd needs a least squares equation (ev_ls)&quot;)
strings tok = strsplit(adds)
matrix Z = {}
set skip_missing off
loop i = 1..nelem(tok)
  series eva_z = ev_gen(tok[i], vars)
  matrix zz = zeros(rows(b.tobs), 1)
  loop j = 1..rows(b.tobs)
    scalar t = b.tobs[j]
    zz[j] = eva_z[t]
  endloop
  errorif(sumc(!ok(zz)) &gt; 0, tok[i] ~ &quot; has missing values in the estimation sample&quot;)
  Z ~= zz
endloop
return ev__nested(b, b.X, b.X ~ Z, cols(Z), &quot;Omitted Variables&quot;, toupper(adds), quiet)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_testdrop" type="bundle">
 <params count="3">
  <param name="b" type="bundle">
<description>ev_ls result</description>
  </param>
  <param name="drops" type="string">
<description>Regressors to drop, e.g. x2 c</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
 </params>
<code>errorif(!inbundle(b, &quot;X&quot;), &quot;testdrop needs a least squares equation (ev_ls)&quot;)
strings tok = strsplit(drops)
matrix keep = ones(1, cols(b.X))
loop i = 1..nelem(tok)
  scalar f = 0
  loop j = 1..nelem(b.labels)
    if b.labels[j] == toupper(tok[i])
      keep[j] = 0
      f = 1
    endif
  endloop
  errorif(!f, tok[i] ~ &quot; is not a regressor of the equation&quot;)
endloop
matrix X = b.X
return ev__nested(b, selifc(X, keep), X, cols(X) - sumr(keep), &quot;Redundant Variables&quot;, toupper(drops), quiet)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_rls" type="bundle">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="b" type="bundle">
<description>ev_ls result</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
 </params>
<code># recursive residuals, CUSUM and CUSUM of squares with 5% bands, recursive coefficients
errorif(!inbundle(b, &quot;X&quot;), &quot;Recursive estimates need a least squares equation (ev_ls)&quot;)
matrix y = b.y
matrix X = b.X
scalar n = rows(y)
scalar k = cols(X)
scalar m = n - k
errorif(m &lt; 3, &quot;Too few observations for recursive estimates&quot;)
matrix w = zeros(m, 1)
matrix B = zeros(m, k)
matrix wse = zeros(m, 1)
loop t = k + 1..n
  matrix Xt = X[1:t-1,]
  matrix XX = inv(Xt'Xt)
  matrix bt = XX * Xt' * y[1:t-1]
  matrix x = X[t,]
  scalar f = 1 + qform(x, XX)
  w[t - k] = (y[t] - x * bt) / sqrt(f)
  matrix bt2 = mols(y[1:t], X[1:t,])
  B[t - k,] = bt2'
endloop
scalar s = sdc(w) * sqrt(m / (m - 1))
matrix cs = cum(w) / s
matrix tt = seq(1, m)'
matrix band = 0.948 * (sqrt(m) + 2 * tt / sqrt(m))
matrix w2 = w.^2
matrix cq = cum(w2) / sumc(w2)
# CUSUM of squares band: Kolmogorov-Smirnov approximation of Durbin's c0 (5%)
scalar c0 = 1.358 / sqrt(m / 2)
bundle r
r.tobs = b.tobs[k + 1:n]
r.rresid = w
r.cusum = cs
r.cusum_band = band
r.cusumsq = cq
r.cusumsq_lo = tt / m - c0
r.cusumsq_hi = tt / m + c0
r.coefs = B
r.labels = b.labels
r.hc = meanc(w) / (s / sqrt(m))          # Harvey-Collier t
r.hcp = 2 * pvalue(t, m - 1, abs(r.hc))
r.cusum_out = sumc(abs(cs) .&gt; band)
r.cusumsq_out = sumc((cq .&lt; r.cusumsq_lo) + (cq .&gt; r.cusumsq_hi))
if !quiet
  printf &quot;\nRecursive Estimates: %s\n&quot;, b.spec
  printf &quot;CUSUM: %d of %d points outside the 5%% band\n&quot;, r.cusum_out, m
  printf &quot;CUSUM of squares: %d of %d points outside the 5%% band\n&quot;, r.cusumsq_out, m
  printf &quot;Harvey-Collier t = %.6f  (Prob. %.4f)\n&quot;, r.hc, r.hcp
endif
return r
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_rlsplot" type="void">
 <params count="3">
  <param name="r" type="bundle">
<description>ev_rls result</description>
  </param>
  <param name="what" type="string" optional="true">
<description>c (CUSUM), q (CUSUM of squares) or r (recursive residuals)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="out" type="string" optional="true">
<description>Output file (default: display)</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code>string w = exists(what) ? tolower(what) : &quot;c&quot;
matrix M = {}
if w == &quot;q&quot;
  M = r.cusumsq ~ r.cusumsq_lo ~ r.cusumsq_hi
  cnameset(M, defarray(&quot;CUSUM of Squares&quot;, &quot;5% Significance&quot;, &quot;5% Significance&quot;))
elif w == &quot;r&quot;
  M = r.rresid ~ 2 * sdc(r.rresid) * ones(rows(r.rresid), 1) ~ -2 * sdc(r.rresid) * ones(rows(r.rresid), 1)
  cnameset(M, defarray(&quot;Recursive Residuals&quot;, &quot;+/- 2 S.E.&quot;, &quot;+/- 2 S.E.&quot;))
else
  M = r.cusum ~ r.cusum_band ~ -r.cusum_band
  cnameset(M, defarray(&quot;CUSUM&quot;, &quot;5% Significance&quot;, &quot;5% Significance&quot;))
endif
string o = exists(out) ? out : &quot;display&quot;
gnuplot 1 2 3 --matrix=M --with-lines --output=&quot;@o&quot;
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_pp" type="bundle">
 <params count="6">
  <param name="expr" type="string">
<description>Series or expression, e.g. log(gdp)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list">
<description>Series used (e.g. dataset)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="det" type="string" optional="true">
<description>c (constant), ct (constant and trend) or nc (none)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="bw" type="scalar" default="-1">
<description>Bandwidth: -1 Newey-West automatic, -2 Newey-West fixed rule, &gt;= 0 fixed</description>
  </param>
  <param name="dif" type="bool" default="0">
<description>Test the first difference</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
 </params>
<code>string d = exists(det) ? tolower(det) : &quot;c&quot;
errorif(!instring(&quot; c ct nc &quot;, &quot; &quot; ~ d ~ &quot; &quot;), &quot;det must be c, ct or nc&quot;)
set skip_missing off
# lags written into the expression, so that pre-sample data are used (as EViews)
series evp_0 = ev_gen(expr, vars)
series evp_1 = ev_gen(ev__lagx(expr, 1, vars), vars)
series evp_x = evp_0
series evp_l = evp_1
if dif
  series evp_2 = ev_gen(ev__lagx(expr, 2, vars), vars)
  evp_x = evp_0 - evp_1
  evp_l = evp_1 - evp_2
endif
series evp_d = evp_x - evp_l
series evp_tr = obs - 1
series evp_o = obs
list L = evp_d evp_l evp_tr evp_o
matrix D = {L}
D = selifr(D, sumr(!ok(D)) .= 0)
matrix dy = D[, 1]
matrix X = D[, 2]
if d != &quot;nc&quot;
  X ~= ones(rows(D), 1)
endif
if d == &quot;ct&quot;
  X ~= D[, 3]
endif
scalar T = rows(dy)
scalar k = cols(X)
matrix e = {}
matrix bh = mols(dy, X, &amp;e)
scalar s2 = e'e / (T - k)
matrix V = s2 * inv(X'X)
scalar se = sqrt(V[1, 1])
scalar tal = bh[1] / se
scalar g0 = e'e / T
scalar bwu = bw
string bwm = &quot;fixed&quot;
if bw == -1
  bwu = ev__nwbw(e)
  bwm = &quot;Newey-West automatic&quot;
elif bw == -2
  bwu = floor(4 * (T / 100)^(2 / 9))
  bwm = &quot;Newey-West fixed&quot;
endif
scalar l2 = ev__lrvar(e, bwu)
scalar zt = tal * sqrt(g0 / l2) - T * (l2 - g0) * se / (2 * sqrt(l2) * sqrt(s2))
scalar itv = d == &quot;nc&quot; ? 1 : (d == &quot;c&quot; ? 2 : 3)
bundle r
r.stat = zt
r.pval = urcpval(zt, T, 1, itv)
r.cv = {ev__urccv(T, itv, 0.01), ev__urccv(T, itv, 0.05), ev__urccv(T, itv, 0.10)}
r.bandwidth = bwu
r.bwmethod = bwm
r.T = T
r.resvar = g0
r.lrvar = l2
r.tdf = tal
r.coeff = bh
r.det = d
if !quiet
  printf &quot;\nNull Hypothesis: %s has a unit root\n&quot;, toupper(dif ? &quot;D(&quot; ~ expr ~ &quot;)&quot; : expr)
  printf &quot;Exogenous: %s\n&quot;, d == &quot;c&quot; ? &quot;Constant&quot; : (d == &quot;ct&quot; ? &quot;Constant, Linear Trend&quot; : &quot;None&quot;)
  printf &quot;Bandwidth: %.4g (%s) using Bartlett kernel\n\n&quot;, bwu, bwm
  printf &quot;%-40s%14s%10s\n&quot;, &quot;&quot;, &quot;Adj. t-Stat&quot;, &quot;Prob.*&quot;
  ev__line(78)
  printf &quot;%-40s%14.6f%10.4f\n&quot;, &quot;Phillips-Perron test statistic&quot;, zt, r.pval
  printf &quot;%-20s%-20s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Test critical values:&quot;, &quot;1% level&quot;, r.cv[1]
  printf &quot;%-20s%-20s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;&quot;, &quot;5% level&quot;, r.cv[2]
  printf &quot;%-20s%-20s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;&quot;, &quot;10% level&quot;, r.cv[3]
  ev__line(78)
  printf &quot;*MacKinnon (1996) one-sided p-values.\n\n&quot;
  printf &quot;%-40s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Residual variance (no correction)&quot;, g0
  printf &quot;%-40s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;HAC corrected variance (Bartlett kernel)&quot;, l2
endif
return r
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_cointeg" type="bundle">
 <params count="7">
  <param name="names" type="string">
<description>Series, e.g. y x1 x2 (the first is the dependent one)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list">
<description>Series used (e.g. dataset)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="method" type="string" optional="true">
<description>eg (Engle-Granger) or po (Phillips-Ouliaris)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="det" type="string" optional="true">
<description>c (constant), ct (constant and trend) or nc (none)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="lag" type="int" min="-1" default="-1">
<description>ADF lags for EG: -1 automatic (SIC)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="maxlag" type="int" min="-1" default="-1">
<description>Maximum lag for the automatic choice (-1: EViews rule)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
 </params>
<code>string meth = exists(method) ? tolower(method) : &quot;eg&quot;
errorif(meth != &quot;eg&quot; &amp;&amp; meth != &quot;po&quot;, &quot;method must be eg or po&quot;)
string d = exists(det) ? tolower(det) : &quot;c&quot;
strings tok = strsplit(names)
scalar m = nelem(tok)
errorif(m &lt; 2, &quot;Give at least two series&quot;)
set skip_missing off
matrix Y = {}
loop i = 1..m
  series evc_x = ev_gen(tok[i], vars)
  Y ~= {evc_x}
endloop
Y = selifr(Y, sumr(!ok(Y)) .= 0)
scalar T = rows(Y)
matrix X = Y[, 2:m]
if d != &quot;nc&quot;
  X ~= ones(T, 1)
endif
if d == &quot;ct&quot;
  X ~= seq(0, T - 1)'
endif
matrix u = {}
matrix bh = mols(Y[, 1], X, &amp;u)
scalar itv = d == &quot;nc&quot; ? 1 : (d == &quot;c&quot; ? 2 : 3)
bundle r
r.method = meth
r.coeff = bh
r.uhat = u
if meth == &quot;eg&quot;
  # ADF regression on the residuals without deterministic terms
  scalar pmax = maxlag &gt;= 0 ? maxlag : floor(4 * (T / 100)^(1 / 4))
  scalar bestp = lag
  if lag &lt; 0
    # choose the lag by SIC on a common sample
    scalar best = 1e300
    loop p = 0..pmax
      matrix du = u[2:T] - u[1:T-1]
      matrix Z = u[pmax+1:T-1]
      loop j = 1..p
        Z ~= du[pmax+1-j:T-1-j]
      endloop
      matrix ee = {}
      matrix bb = mols(du[pmax+1:T-1], Z, &amp;ee)
      scalar n = rows(ee)
      scalar sic = log(ee'ee / n) + cols(Z) * log(n) / n
      if sic &lt; best
        best = sic
        bestp = p
      endif
    endloop
  endif
  scalar p = bestp
  matrix du = u[2:T] - u[1:T-1]
  matrix Z = u[p+1:T-1]
  loop j = 1..p
    Z ~= du[p+1-j:T-1-j]
  endloop
  matrix ee = {}
  matrix bb = mols(du[p+1:T-1], Z, &amp;ee)
  scalar n = rows(ee)
  matrix V = (ee'ee / (n - cols(Z))) * inv(Z'Z)
  r.tau = bb[1] / sqrt(V[1, 1])
  scalar sg = p &gt; 0 ? sumc(bb[2:p+1]) : 0
  r.z = n * bb[1] / (1 - sg)
  r.lag = p
  r.n = n
else
  # Phillips-Ouliaris: PP-type correction of the residual autoregression
  matrix y1 = u[2:T]
  matrix y0 = u[1:T-1]
  scalar rho = (y0'y1) / (y0'y0)
  matrix e = y1 - rho * y0
  scalar n = rows(e)
  scalar bwu = ev__nwbw(e)
  scalar g0 = e'e / n
  scalar l2 = ev__lrvar(e, bwu)
  scalar lam = (l2 - g0) / 2
  scalar s2 = e'e / (n - 1)
  scalar se = sqrt(s2 / (y0'y0))
  scalar tr = (rho - 1) / se
  r.tau = tr * sqrt(g0 / l2) - lam * n * se / (sqrt(l2) * sqrt(s2))
  r.z = n * (rho - 1) - lam * n^2 / (y0'y0)
  r.bandwidth = bwu
  r.n = n
endif
r.taup = urcpval(r.tau, T, m, itv)        # sample size of the cointegrating regression (as gretl)
if !quiet
  printf &quot;\nNull hypothesis: Series are not cointegrated\nCointegrating equation deterministics: %s\n&quot;, d == &quot;c&quot; ? &quot;C&quot; : (d == &quot;ct&quot; ? &quot;C @TREND&quot; : &quot;none&quot;)
  if meth == &quot;eg&quot;
    printf &quot;Automatic lags specification based on Schwarz criterion\n&quot;
    printf &quot;Lags: %d\n&quot;, r.lag
  else
    printf &quot;Long-run variance estimate (Bartlett kernel, Newey-West bandwidth %.4g)\n&quot;, r.bandwidth
  endif
  printf &quot;\n%-26s%14s%14s%10s\n&quot;, &quot;Dependent&quot;, &quot;tau-statistic&quot;, &quot;z-statistic&quot;, &quot;Prob.*&quot;
  ev__line(78)
  printf &quot;%-26s%14.6f%14.6f%10.4f\n&quot;, toupper(tok[1]), r.tau, r.z, r.taup
  ev__line(78)
  printf &quot;*MacKinnon (1996) p-values (for the tau-statistic).\n&quot;
  printf &quot;Method: %s\n&quot;, meth == &quot;eg&quot; ? &quot;Engle-Granger&quot; : &quot;Phillips-Ouliaris&quot;
endif
return r
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_seasadj" type="series">
 <params count="3">
  <param name="x" type="series">
<description>Monthly or quarterly series</description>
  </param>
  <param name="kind" type="string" optional="true">
<description>m (multiplicative) or a (additive)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="factors" type="seriesref" optional="true">
<description>Output: seasonal factors</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code>errorif($pd != 4 &amp;&amp; $pd != 12, &quot;Seasonal adjustment needs quarterly or monthly data&quot;)
string k = exists(kind) ? tolower(kind) : &quot;m&quot;
errorif(k != &quot;m&quot; &amp;&amp; k != &quot;a&quot;, &quot;kind must be m or a&quot;)
errorif(k == &quot;m&quot; &amp;&amp; min(x) &lt;= 0, &quot;Multiplicative adjustment needs positive values&quot;)
scalar s = $pd
scalar h = s / 2
# centred 2 x s moving average
set skip_missing off
matrix v = {x}
matrix mv = 0.5 * mlag(v, h, NA) + 0.5 * mlag(v, -h, NA)
scalar jlo = 1 - h
loop j = jlo..h-1
  mv += mlag(v, j, NA)
endloop
series ma = mv / s
series ratio = k == &quot;m&quot; ? x / ma : x - ma
series per = $obsminor
matrix idx = zeros(s, 1)
loop j = 1..s
  series sel = per == j &amp;&amp; ok(ratio)
  idx[j] = sum(sel ? ratio : 0) / sum(sel)
endloop
# normalise: product 1 (multiplicative) or sum 0 (additive)
if k == &quot;m&quot;
  idx = idx / exp(meanc(log(idx)))
else
  idx = idx - meanc(idx)
endif
series sf = 0
loop j = 1..s
  sf = per == j ? idx[j] : sf
endloop
if exists(factors)
  factors = sf
endif
return k == &quot;m&quot; ? x / sf : x - sf
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_varroots" type="matrix">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="v" type="bundle">
<description>ev_varest result</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
 </params>
<code># roots of the characteristic polynomial = eigenvalues of the companion matrix
matrix A = v.sys.A
matrix ev = eigen(A)
matrix re = Re(ev)
matrix im = Im(ev)
matrix md = sqrt(re.^2 + im.^2)
# sort by modulus, largest first
matrix o = msortby(seq(1, rows(md))' ~ -md, 2)
matrix S = zeros(rows(md), 3)
loop i = 1..rows(md)
  scalar j = o[i, 1]
  S[i,] = re[j] ~ im[j] ~ md[j]
endloop
if !quiet
  printf &quot;\nRoots of Characteristic Polynomial\nEndogenous variables:&quot;
  loop i = 1..nelem(v.ylab)
    printf &quot; %s&quot;, v.ylab[i]
  endloop
  printf &quot;\nLag specification: %d %d\n\n&quot;, v.lags[1], v.lags[2]
  printf &quot;%-36s%14s\n&quot;, &quot;Root&quot;, &quot;Modulus&quot;
  ev__line(52)
  loop i = 1..rows(S)
    if abs(S[i, 2]) &lt; 1e-12
      printf &quot;%-36.6f%14.6f\n&quot;, S[i, 1], S[i, 3]
    else
      printf &quot;%-36s%14.6f\n&quot;, sprintf(&quot;%.6f %s %.6fi&quot;, S[i, 1], S[i, 2] &lt; 0 ? &quot;-&quot; : &quot;+&quot;, abs(S[i, 2])), S[i, 3]
    endif
  endloop
  ev__line(52)
  if maxc(S[, 3]) &lt; 1
    printf &quot;No root lies outside the unit circle.\nVAR satisfies the stability condition.\n&quot;
  else
    printf &quot;Warning: at least one root lies outside the unit circle.\nVAR does not satisfy the stability condition.\n&quot;
  endif
endif
return S
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_varlm" type="matrix">
 <params count="3">
  <param name="v" type="bundle">
<description>ev_varest result</description>
  </param>
  <param name="h" type="int" min="1" default="4">
<description>Number of lags to test</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
 </params>
<code># Breusch-Godfrey LM tests for residual serial correlation (Lutkepohl):
# LM = T (n - tr(inv(S_u) S_e)), chi-square(n^2 m); rows: lag j alone and lags 1..j
matrix U = v.sys.uhat
matrix X = v.sys.X
scalar T = rows(U)
scalar n = cols(U)
matrix Su = U'U / T
matrix R = {}
loop j = 1..h
  loop kind = 1..2
    matrix Z = X
    scalar m = 0
    loop l = 1..j
      if kind == 2 || l == j
        Z ~= mlag(U, l, 0)
        m++
      endif
    endloop
    matrix E = U - Z * mols(U, Z)
    matrix Se = E'E / T
    scalar lm = T * (n - tr(inv(Su) * Se))
    scalar df = n^2 * m
    R |= {j, kind, lm, df, pvalue(c, df, lm)}
  endloop
endloop
if !quiet
  printf &quot;\nVAR Residual Serial Correlation LM Tests\nSample: %s\nIncluded observations: %d\n&quot;, v.sample, T
  printf &quot;\nNull hypothesis: No serial correlation at lag h\n&quot;
  printf &quot;%6s%14s%8s%10s\n&quot;, &quot;Lag&quot;, &quot;LM-Stat&quot;, &quot;df&quot;, &quot;Prob.&quot;
  loop i = 1..rows(R)
    if R[i, 2] == 1
      printf &quot;%6d%14.6f%8d%10.4f\n&quot;, R[i, 1], R[i, 3], R[i, 4], R[i, 5]
    endif
  endloop
  printf &quot;\nNull hypothesis: No serial correlation at lags 1 to h\n&quot;
  printf &quot;%6s%14s%8s%10s\n&quot;, &quot;Lag&quot;, &quot;LM-Stat&quot;, &quot;df&quot;, &quot;Prob.&quot;
  loop i = 1..rows(R)
    if R[i, 2] == 2
      printf &quot;%6d%14.6f%8d%10.4f\n&quot;, R[i, 1], R[i, 3], R[i, 4], R[i, 5]
    endif
  endloop
  printf &quot;*LM statistic, chi-square distribution\n&quot;
endif
return R
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_varnorm" type="bundle">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="v" type="bundle">
<description>ev_varest result</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
 </params>
<code># Jarque-Bera normality tests on Cholesky-orthogonalised residuals (Lutkepohl)
matrix U = v.sys.uhat
scalar T = rows(U)
scalar n = cols(U)
matrix Uc = U .- meanc(U)
matrix S = Uc'Uc / T
matrix P = cholesky(S)
matrix W = Uc * inv(P')
matrix sk = meanc(W.^3)
matrix ku = meanc(W.^4)
matrix ls = T * sk.^2 / 6
matrix lk = T * (ku - 3).^2 / 24
bundle r
r.skew = sk'
r.kurt = ku'
r.skew_chi = ls'
r.kurt_chi = lk'
r.jb = ls' + lk'
r.skew_joint = sumr(ls)
r.kurt_joint = sumr(lk)
r.jb_joint = r.skew_joint + r.kurt_joint
r.skew_p = pvalue(c, n, r.skew_joint)
r.kurt_p = pvalue(c, n, r.kurt_joint)
r.jb_p = pvalue(c, 2 * n, r.jb_joint)
if !quiet
  printf &quot;\nVAR Residual Normality Tests\nOrthogonalization: Cholesky (Lutkepohl)\n&quot;
  printf &quot;Null Hypothesis: Residuals are multivariate normal\nIncluded observations: %d\n\n&quot;, T
  printf &quot;%-12s%14s%14s%8s%10s\n&quot;, &quot;Component&quot;, &quot;Skewness&quot;, &quot;Chi-sq&quot;, &quot;df&quot;, &quot;Prob.&quot;
  loop i = 1..n
    printf &quot;%-12d%14.6f%14.6f%8d%10.4f\n&quot;, i, sk[i], ls[i], 1, pvalue(c, 1, ls[i])
  endloop
  printf &quot;%-12s%14s%14.6f%8d%10.4f\n\n&quot;, &quot;Joint&quot;, &quot;&quot;, r.skew_joint, n, r.skew_p
  printf &quot;%-12s%14s%14s%8s%10s\n&quot;, &quot;Component&quot;, &quot;Kurtosis&quot;, &quot;Chi-sq&quot;, &quot;df&quot;, &quot;Prob.&quot;
  loop i = 1..n
    printf &quot;%-12d%14.6f%14.6f%8d%10.4f\n&quot;, i, ku[i], lk[i], 1, pvalue(c, 1, lk[i])
  endloop
  printf &quot;%-12s%14s%14.6f%8d%10.4f\n\n&quot;, &quot;Joint&quot;, &quot;&quot;, r.kurt_joint, n, r.kurt_p
  printf &quot;%-12s%14s%8s%10s\n&quot;, &quot;Component&quot;, &quot;Jarque-Bera&quot;, &quot;df&quot;, &quot;Prob.&quot;
  loop i = 1..n
    printf &quot;%-12d%14.6f%8d%10.4f\n&quot;, i, r.jb[i], 2, pvalue(c, 2, r.jb[i])
  endloop
  printf &quot;%-12s%14.6f%8d%10.4f\n&quot;, &quot;Joint&quot;, r.jb_joint, 2 * n, r.jb_p
endif
return r
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_varfcast" type="bundle">
 <params count="4">
  <param name="v" type="bundle">
<description>ev_varest result</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list">
<description>Series used (e.g. dataset)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="dynamic" type="bool" default="1">
<description>Dynamic (1) or static (0)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
 </params>
<code># forecasts of every endogenous variable over the current sample, with S.E.
scalar n = v.n
matrix lg = v.lags
scalar p = maxr(lg)
matrix C = v.coeff                     # k x n, rows as in v.clab
set skip_missing off
series evf_o = obs
matrix tob = {evf_o}
scalar T = rows(tob)
# actual values and actual lags (pre-sample data included)
matrix Ya = {}
matrices YL = array(p)
loop j = 1..p
  YL[j] = {}
endloop
loop i = 1..n
  series evf_y = ev_gen(v.ytok[i], vars)
  Ya ~= {evf_y}
  loop j = 1..p
    series evf_l = ev_gen(ev__lagx(v.ytok[i], j, vars), vars)
    matrix M = YL[j]
    YL[j] = M ~ {evf_l}
  endloop
endloop
matrix XE = {}
loop i = 1..nelem(v.xtok)
  if tolower(v.xtok[i]) != &quot;c&quot;
    series evf_x = ev_gen(v.xtok[i], vars)
    XE ~= {evf_x}
  endif
endloop
matrix F = zeros(T, n)
loop t = 1..T
  # regressor row in the order of v.clab: C, then each variable with its lags, then exogenous
  matrix row = {}
  if v.hasc
    row ~= 1
  endif
  loop i = 1..n
    loop jj = 1..cols(lg)
      scalar j = lg[jj]
      if dynamic &amp;&amp; t - j &gt;= 1
        row ~= F[t - j, i]
      else
        matrix M = YL[j]
        row ~= M[t, i]
      endif
    endloop
  endloop
  if cols(XE) &gt; 0
    row ~= XE[t,]
  endif
  F[t,] = row * C
endloop
# forecast standard errors from the MA representation (dynamic) or one step (static)
matrix A = v.sys.A
matrix Sg = v.sys.sigma
scalar np = rows(A)
matrix J = I(n) ~ zeros(n, np - n)
matrix SE = zeros(T, n)
matrix Mse = zeros(n, n)
matrix Ap = I(np)
loop h = 1..T
  matrix Phi = J * Ap * J'
  Mse += Phi * Sg * Phi'
  SE[h,] = sqrt(diag(dynamic ? Mse : Sg))'
  Ap = Ap * A
endloop
bundle r
r.fcast = F
r.se = SE
r.actual = Ya
r.tobs = tob
r.names = v.ylab
r.dynamic = dynamic
if !quiet
  printf &quot;\nVAR %s forecast, %s - %s\n&quot;, dynamic ? &quot;dynamic&quot; : &quot;static&quot;, obslabel(minc(tob)), obslabel(maxc(tob))
  printf &quot;%-12s&quot;, &quot;obs&quot;
  loop i = 1..n
    printf &quot;%16s%12s&quot;, v.ylab[i], &quot;S.E.&quot;
  endloop
  printf &quot;\n&quot;
  loop t = 1..T
    printf &quot;%-12s&quot;, obslabel(tob[t])
    loop i = 1..n
      printf &quot;%16.6f%12.6f&quot;, F[t, i], SE[t, i]
    endloop
    printf &quot;\n&quot;
  endloop
endif
return r
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_varfseries" type="series">
 <params count="3">
  <param name="r" type="bundle">
<description>ev_varfcast result</description>
  </param>
  <param name="i" type="int" min="1" default="1">
<description>Variable number</description>
  </param>
  <param name="se" type="bool" default="0">
<description>Return the S.E. instead of the forecast</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code>return ev__toseries(se ? r.se[, i] : r.fcast[, i], r.tobs)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_pagecol" type="matrix">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="x" type="series">
<description>Series of the source page</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code># [day number, value] of every observation, for ev_freqconv
set skip_missing off
series d = ev__epochdays()
return {d} ~ {x}
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_freqconv" type="series">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="S" type="matrix" const="true">
<description>ev_pagecol() of the source series</description>
  </param>
  <param name="method" type="string" optional="true">
<description>a s f l x n (high to low); r d i q t c (low to high)</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code># convert to the frequency of the current page, as EViews copy(c=...)
set skip_missing off
series d = ev__epochdays()
matrix D = {d}
scalar T = rows(D)
scalar ns = rows(S)
# length of a period: next start date (the last one: same spacing as before)
matrix Dn = D[2:T] | (2 * D[T] - D[T - 1])
matrix Sn = S[2:ns, 1] | (2 * S[ns, 1] - S[ns - 1, 1])
scalar tgt_len = meanc(Dn - D)
scalar src_len = meanc(Sn - S[, 1])
string m = exists(method) ? tolower(method) : (src_len &lt; tgt_len ? &quot;a&quot; : &quot;r&quot;)
series r = NA
if src_len &lt; tgt_len
  errorif(!instring(&quot; a s f l x n &quot;, &quot; &quot; ~ m ~ &quot; &quot;), &quot;high to low frequency: c=a, s, f, l, x or n&quot;)
  loop t = 1..T
    matrix in = (S[, 1] .&gt;= D[t]) .* (S[, 1] .&lt; Dn[t])
    if sumc(in) &gt; 0
      matrix v = selifr(S[, 2], in)
      if sumc(!ok(v)) == 0
        if m == &quot;a&quot;
          r[t] = meanc(v)
        elif m == &quot;s&quot;
          r[t] = sumc(v)
        elif m == &quot;f&quot;
          r[t] = v[1]
        elif m == &quot;l&quot;
          r[t] = v[rows(v)]
        elif m == &quot;x&quot;
          r[t] = maxc(v)
        else
          r[t] = minc(v)
        endif
      endif
    endif
  endloop
else
  errorif(!instring(&quot; r d i q t c &quot;, &quot; &quot; ~ m ~ &quot; &quot;), &quot;low to high frequency: c=r, d, i, q (quadratic match average), t (quadratic match sum) or c (cubic match last)&quot;)
  # the source period that contains each target date
  matrix j = zeros(T, 1)
  loop t = 1..T
    matrix in = (S[, 1] .&lt;= D[t]) .* (Sn .&gt; D[t])
    j[t] = sumc(in) &gt; 0 ? imaxc(in) : 0
  endloop
  if m == &quot;q&quot; || m == &quot;t&quot; || m == &quot;c&quot;
    # high-frequency periods per source period, and the position of each target in its period
    scalar mm = round(src_len / tgt_len)
    matrix pos = zeros(T, 1)
    loop t = 1..T
      if j[t] &gt; 0
        pos[t] = sumc(j[1:t] .= j[t])
      endif
    endloop
    # (a first source period cut by the page start is counted back from its end below)
    errorif(ns &lt; 3, &quot;Quadratic and cubic conversions need at least 3 source observations&quot;)
    matrix Y = S[, 2]
    if m == &quot;c&quot;
      # natural cubic spline through the last high-frequency position of each source period
      matrix xk = seq(1, ns)' * mm
      matrix h = xk[2:ns] - xk[1:ns-1]
      matrix A = zeros(ns, ns)
      matrix rhs = zeros(ns, 1)
      A[1, 1] = 1
      A[ns, ns] = 1
      loop i = 2..ns - 1
        A[i, i - 1] = h[i - 1]
        A[i, i] = 2 * (h[i - 1] + h[i])
        A[i, i + 1] = h[i]
        rhs[i] = 6 * ((Y[i + 1] - Y[i]) / h[i] - (Y[i] - Y[i - 1]) / h[i - 1])
      endloop
      matrix M2 = inv(A) * rhs
      loop t = 1..T
        if j[t] &gt; 0
          scalar k = j[t]
          scalar x = (k - 1) * mm + pos[t] + (mm - sumc(j .= k)) * (k == 1)
          scalar i = max(1, min(ns - 1, floor((x - xk[1]) / mm) + 1))
          if x &lt; xk[1]
            i = 1
          endif
          scalar hh = xk[i + 1] - xk[i]
          scalar a1 = (xk[i + 1] - x) / hh
          scalar b1 = (x - xk[i]) / hh
          r[t] = a1 * Y[i] + b1 * Y[i + 1] + ((a1^3 - a1) * M2[i] + (b1^3 - b1) * M2[i + 1]) * hh^2 / 6
        endif
      endloop
    else
      # quadratic through each source period and its neighbours, matching their averages (or sums)
      loop t = 1..T
        if j[t] &gt; 0
          scalar k = j[t]
          scalar k0 = k == 1 ? 1 : (k == ns ? ns - 2 : k - 1)
          k0 = max(1, k0)
          matrix Am = zeros(3, 3)
          matrix bv = zeros(3, 1)
          loop q = 1..3
            scalar pq = k0 + q - 1
            matrix sj = (pq - 1) * mm + seq(1, mm)'
            Am[q,] = {1, meanc(sj), meanc(sj.^2)}
            bv[q] = m == &quot;q&quot; ? Y[pq] : Y[pq] / mm
          endloop
          matrix cf = inv(Am) * bv
          scalar x = (k - 1) * mm + pos[t] + (mm - sumc(j .= k)) * (k == 1)
          r[t] = cf[1] + cf[2] * x + cf[3] * x^2
        endif
      endloop
    endif
  elif m == &quot;i&quot;
    # linear interpolation, matching the source value in the last period of each source period
    matrix xs = {}
    matrix ys = {}
    loop k = 1..ns
      matrix in = j .= k
      if sumc(in) &gt; 0
        scalar last = 0
        loop t = 1..T
          if in[t]
            last = t
          endif
        endloop
        xs |= last
        ys |= S[k, 2]
      endif
    endloop
    loop t = 1..T
      loop k = 1..rows(xs) - 1
        if t &gt;= xs[k] &amp;&amp; t &lt;= xs[k + 1]
          r[t] = ys[k] + (ys[k + 1] - ys[k]) * (t - xs[k]) / (xs[k + 1] - xs[k])
        endif
      endloop
    endloop
  else
    loop t = 1..T
      scalar k = j[t]
      if k &gt; 0
        scalar cnt = m == &quot;d&quot; ? sumc(j .= k) : 1
        r[t] = S[k, 2] / cnt
      endif
    endloop
  endif
endif
return r
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_left" type="string">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="s" type="string"/>
  <param name="n" type="int"/>
 </params>
<code>if n &lt;= 0
  return &quot;&quot;
endif
return substr(s, 1, min(n, strlen(s)))
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_right" type="string">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="s" type="string"/>
  <param name="n" type="int"/>
 </params>
<code>scalar L = strlen(s)
if n &lt;= 0 || L == 0
  return &quot;&quot;
endif
return substr(s, max(1, L - n + 1), L)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_mid" type="string">
 <params count="3">
  <param name="s" type="string"/>
  <param name="n1" type="int"/>
  <param name="n2" type="int" default="-1"/>
 </params>
<code>scalar L = strlen(s)
if n1 &gt; L || n2 == 0
  return &quot;&quot;
endif
scalar e = n2 &lt; 0 ? L : min(L, n1 + n2 - 1)
return substr(s, max(1, n1), e)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_instr" type="scalar">
 <params count="3">
  <param name="s" type="string"/>
  <param name="t" type="string"/>
  <param name="nth" type="int" min="1" default="1"/>
 </params>
<code># position of the nth occurrence of t in s (0 if not found), as EViews @instr
scalar base = 0
string rest = s
loop k = 1..nth
  if !instring(rest, t)
    return 0
  endif
  scalar p = strlen(rest) - strlen(strstr(rest, t)) + 1
  if k == nth
    return base + p
  endif
  if p &gt;= strlen(rest)
    return 0
  endif
  base += p
  rest = substr(rest, p + 1, strlen(rest))
endloop
return 0
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_word" type="string">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="s" type="string"/>
  <param name="n" type="int"/>
 </params>
<code>strings w = strsplit(s)
if n &lt; 1 || n &gt; nelem(w)
  return &quot;&quot;
endif
return w[n]
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_dateval" type="scalar">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="s" type="string"/>
  <param name="fmt" type="string" optional="true">
<description>EViews format, e.g. YYYY-MM-DD or MM/DD/YYYY</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code># EViews date number (days since 1 Jan 1 AD, starting at 0)
string f = exists(fmt) ? fmt : (instring(s, &quot;/&quot;) ? &quot;MM/DD/YYYY&quot; : &quot;YYYY-MM-DD&quot;)
f = strsub(strsub(strsub(toupper(f), &quot;YYYY&quot;, &quot;%Y&quot;), &quot;MM&quot;, &quot;%m&quot;), &quot;DD&quot;, &quot;%d&quot;)
scalar sec = strptime(s, f)
errorif(!ok(sec), &quot;Cannot read the date &quot; ~ s)
return round(sec / 86400) + 719162         # strptime reads local time: round to the day
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_datestr" type="string">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="d" type="scalar">
<description>EViews date number</description>
  </param>
  <param name="fmt" type="string" optional="true">
<description>EViews format, default YYYY-MM-DD</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code>string f = exists(fmt) ? fmt : &quot;YYYY-MM-DD&quot;
f = strsub(strsub(strsub(toupper(f), &quot;YYYY&quot;, &quot;%Y&quot;), &quot;MM&quot;, &quot;%m&quot;), &quot;DD&quot;, &quot;%d&quot;)
return strftime((d - 719162) * 86400 + 43200, f)   # noon UTC: the same day in any time zone
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_date" type="series">
<code># EViews @date: date number of each observation
series r = ev__epochdays()
return r - 1
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_table" type="bundle">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="r" type="int" min="1" default="1"/>
  <param name="c" type="int" min="1" default="1"/>
 </params>
<code>bundle t
t.kind = &quot;table&quot;
t.rows = r
t.cols = c
strings cells = array(r * c)
loop i = 1..r * c
  cells[i] = &quot;&quot;
endloop
t.cells = cells
t.width = 10 * ones(1, c)
return t
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_tset" type="void">
 <params count="4">
  <param name="t" type="bundleref"/>
  <param name="i" type="int" min="1"/>
  <param name="j" type="int" min="1"/>
  <param name="v" type="string"/>
 </params>
<code>ev__tgrow(&amp;t, i, j)
strings cl = t.cells
cl[(i - 1) * t.cols + j] = v
t.cells = cl
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_tsetnum" type="void">
 <params count="4">
  <param name="t" type="bundleref"/>
  <param name="i" type="int" min="1"/>
  <param name="j" type="int" min="1"/>
  <param name="v" type="scalar"/>
 </params>
<code>ev_tset(&amp;t, i, j, ok(v) ? sprintf(&quot;%.8g&quot;, v) : &quot;NA&quot;)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_tget" type="string">
 <params count="3">
  <param name="t" type="bundle"/>
  <param name="i" type="int"/>
  <param name="j" type="int"/>
 </params>
<code>if i &gt; t.rows || j &gt; t.cols
  return &quot;&quot;
endif
return t.cells[(i - 1) * t.cols + j]
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_twidth" type="void">
 <params count="3">
  <param name="t" type="bundleref"/>
  <param name="j" type="int" min="1"/>
  <param name="w" type="int" min="1"/>
 </params>
<code>ev__tgrow(&amp;t, 1, j)
matrix ww = t.width
ww[j] = w
t.width = ww
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_ttext" type="string">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="t" type="bundle"/>
  <param name="fmt" type="string" optional="true">
<description>txt, csv or html</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code>string f = exists(fmt) ? tolower(fmt) : &quot;txt&quot;
string out = &quot;&quot;
string nl = sprintf(&quot;\n&quot;)             # string literals do not expand \n
if f == &quot;html&quot;
  out = &quot;&lt;table&gt;&quot; ~ nl
endif
loop i = 1..t.rows
  string line = &quot;&quot;
  loop j = 1..t.cols
    string v = t.cells[(i - 1) * t.cols + j]
    if f == &quot;csv&quot;
      line ~= (j &gt; 1 ? &quot;,&quot; : &quot;&quot;) ~ (instring(v, &quot;,&quot;) || instring(v, &quot;\&quot;&quot;) ? &quot;\&quot;&quot; ~ strsub(v, &quot;\&quot;&quot;, &quot;\&quot;\&quot;&quot;) ~ &quot;\&quot;&quot; : v)
    elif f == &quot;html&quot;
      line ~= &quot;&lt;td&gt;&quot; ~ v ~ &quot;&lt;/td&gt;&quot;
    else
      string fm = sprintf(&quot;%%%ds&quot;, t.width[j])
      line ~= sprintf(fm, v)
    endif
  endloop
  out ~= f == &quot;html&quot; ? &quot;&lt;tr&gt;&quot; ~ line ~ &quot;&lt;/tr&gt;&quot; ~ nl : line ~ nl
endloop
if f == &quot;html&quot;
  out ~= &quot;&lt;/table&gt;&quot; ~ nl
endif
return out
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_tprint" type="void">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="t" type="bundle"/>
 </params>
<code>printf &quot;%s&quot;, ev_ttext(t, &quot;txt&quot;)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_tsave" type="void">
 <params count="3">
  <param name="t" type="bundle"/>
  <param name="fname" type="string"/>
  <param name="fmt" type="string" optional="true">
<description>txt, csv or html</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code>string f = exists(fmt) ? tolower(fmt) : &quot;csv&quot;
string txt = ev_ttext(t, f)
outfile &quot;@fname&quot; --quiet
  printf &quot;%s&quot;, txt
end outfile
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_mlreg" type="bundle">
 <params count="6">
  <param name="spec" type="string">
<description>Equation, e.g. y c x</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list">
<description>Series used (e.g. dataset)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="method" type="string">
<description>ologit, oprobit, tobit, poisson, negbin or qreg</description>
  </param>
  <param name="p1" type="scalar" default="NA">
<description>tobit: left limit (default 0); qreg: quantile (default 0.5)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="p2" type="scalar" default="NA">
<description>tobit: right limit (default none)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
 </params>
<code>string m = tolower(method)
errorif(!instring(&quot; ologit oprobit tobit poisson negbin qreg &quot;, &quot; &quot; ~ m ~ &quot; &quot;), &quot;unknown method &quot; ~ method)
strings tok = strsplit(spec)
series evm_y = ev_gen(tok[1], vars)
list X = null
strings lab = array(0)
scalar hascon = 0
loop i = 2..nelem(tok)
  if tolower(tok[i]) == &quot;c&quot;
    list X += const
    lab += &quot;C&quot;
    hascon = 1
  else
    string v = sprintf(&quot;evm_x%d&quot;, i)
    series @v = ev_gen(tok[i], vars)
    list X += @v
    lab += toupper(tok[i])
  endif
endloop
errorif((m == &quot;ologit&quot; || m == &quot;oprobit&quot;) &amp;&amp; hascon, &quot;Ordered models have no constant (the limit points take its place): drop c&quot;)
scalar n0 = $nobs
scalar tau = ok(p1) ? p1 : 0.5
if m == &quot;ologit&quot;
  logit evm_y X --quiet
elif m == &quot;oprobit&quot;
  probit evm_y X --quiet
elif m == &quot;tobit&quot;
  scalar ll = ok(p1) ? p1 : 0
  if ok(p2)
    tobit evm_y X --llimit=ll --rlimit=p2 --quiet
  else
    tobit evm_y X --llimit=ll --quiet
  endif
elif m == &quot;poisson&quot;
  poisson evm_y X --quiet
elif m == &quot;negbin&quot;
  negbin evm_y X --quiet
else
  quantreg tau evm_y X --quiet
endif
bundle b
b.kind = &quot;mlreg&quot;
b.method = m
b.spec = spec
b.depvar = toupper(tok[1])
matrix c = $coeff
matrix se = $stderr
matrix V = $vcv
scalar k = rows(c)
scalar kx = nelem(X)
# extra parameters after the regressors: limit points, NB dispersion
loop i = kx + 1..k
  if m == &quot;ologit&quot; || m == &quot;oprobit&quot;
    lab += sprintf(&quot;LIMIT_%d:C(%d)&quot;, i - kx, i)
  elif m == &quot;negbin&quot;
    lab += sprintf(&quot;ALPHA:C(%d)&quot;, i)
  else
    lab += sprintf(&quot;C(%d)&quot;, i)
  endif
endloop
if m == &quot;tobit&quot;
  # EViews reports the scale with the coefficients
  lab += sprintf(&quot;SCALE:C(%d)&quot;, k + 1)
  c |= $sigma
  se |= NA
  k++
endif
b.labels = lab
b.coeff = c
b.stderr = se
b.vcv = V
b.k = k
b.T = $T
b.adjusted = $T &lt; n0
catch scalar lnl = $lnl
if $error
  lnl = NA
endif
b.lnl = lnl
b.tstat = c ./ se
b.zstat = m != &quot;qreg&quot;
matrix pv = zeros(k, 1)
loop i = 1..k
  pv[i] = b.zstat ? 2 * cnorm(-abs(b.tstat[i])) : 2 * pvalue(t, $T - k, abs(b.tstat[i]))
endloop
b.pval = pv
series evm_o = obs
catch series evm_f = $yhat
if $error
  series evm_f = NA
endif
list L = evm_y evm_o
matrix D = {L}
b.y = D[, 1]
b.tobs = D[, 2]
set skip_missing off
matrix F = {evm_f}
b.yhat = ev__atrows(F, b.tobs)
b.uhat = b.y - b.yhat
b.sample = sprintf(&quot;%s %s&quot;, obslabel(minc(b.tobs)), obslabel(maxc(b.tobs)))
scalar n = b.T
b.meany = meanc(b.y)
b.sdy = sdc(b.y) * sqrt(n / (n - 1))
if ok(lnl)
  b.aic = -2 * lnl / n + 2 * k / n
  b.sc = -2 * lnl / n + k * log(n) / n
  b.hq = -2 * lnl / n + 2 * k * log(log(n)) / n
  b.avglnl = lnl / n
endif
if m == &quot;qreg&quot;
  # pseudo R-squared (Koenker-Machado): 1 - V(tau) / V(tau | constant only)
  b.tau = tau
  matrix u = b.uhat
  scalar Vt = sumc(u .* (tau - (u .&lt; 0)))
  scalar q = quantile(b.y, tau)
  matrix u0 = b.y - q
  scalar V0 = sumc(u0 .* (tau - (u0 .&lt; 0)))
  b.pseudo_r2 = 1 - Vt / V0
  b.adj_pseudo_r2 = 1 - (1 - b.pseudo_r2) * (n - 1) / (n - k)
  b.qdep = q
endif
if m == &quot;ologit&quot; || m == &quot;oprobit&quot;
  b.ncat = rows(values(b.y))
endif
b.estdate = strftime($now[1], &quot;%m/%d/%y   Time: %H:%M&quot;)
if !quiet
  ev_mlprint(&amp;b)
endif
return b
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_mlprint" type="void">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="b" type="bundleref"/>
 </params>
<code>string title = b.method == &quot;ologit&quot; ? &quot;ML - Ordered Logit (Newton-Raphson)&quot; : (b.method == &quot;oprobit&quot; ? &quot;ML - Ordered Probit (Newton-Raphson)&quot; : (b.method == &quot;tobit&quot; ? &quot;ML - Censored Normal (TOBIT) (Newton-Raphson)&quot; : (b.method == &quot;poisson&quot; ? &quot;ML/QML - Poisson Count (Newton-Raphson)&quot; : (b.method == &quot;negbin&quot; ? &quot;ML - Negative Binomial Count (Newton-Raphson)&quot; : &quot;Quantile Regression&quot;))))
printf &quot;\nDependent Variable: %s\nMethod: %s\nDate: %s\n&quot;, b.depvar, title, b.estdate
printf &quot;Sample%s: %s\nIncluded observations: %d\n&quot;, b.adjusted ? &quot; (adjusted)&quot; : &quot;&quot;, b.sample, b.T
if b.method == &quot;qreg&quot;
  printf &quot;Quantile: %g\n&quot;, b.tau
endif
printf &quot;\n&quot;
ev__line(78)
printf &quot;%-26s%13s%13s%14s%12s\n&quot;, &quot;Variable&quot;, &quot;Coefficient&quot;, &quot;Std. Error&quot;, b.zstat ? &quot;z-Statistic&quot; : &quot;t-Statistic&quot;, &quot;Prob.&quot;
ev__line(78)
loop i = 1..b.k
  if ok(b.stderr[i])
    printf &quot;%-26s%13.6f%13.6f%14.6f%12.4f\n&quot;, b.labels[i], b.coeff[i], b.stderr[i], b.tstat[i], b.pval[i]
  else
    printf &quot;%-26s%13.6f\n&quot;, b.labels[i], b.coeff[i]
  endif
endloop
ev__line(78)
if b.method == &quot;qreg&quot;
  printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f    %-24s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Pseudo R-squared&quot;, b.pseudo_r2, &quot;Mean dependent var&quot;, b.meany
  printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f    %-24s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Adjusted R-squared&quot;, b.adj_pseudo_r2, &quot;S.D. dependent var&quot;, b.sdy
  printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Quantile dependent var&quot;, b.qdep
else
  printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f    %-24s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Mean dependent var&quot;, b.meany, &quot;S.D. dependent var&quot;, b.sdy
  printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f    %-24s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Akaike info criterion&quot;, b.aic, &quot;Schwarz criterion&quot;, b.sc
  printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f    %-24s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Log likelihood&quot;, b.lnl, &quot;Hannan-Quinn criter.&quot;, b.hq
  printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Avg. log likelihood&quot;, b.avglnl
endif
ev__line(78)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_wls" type="bundle">
 <params count="5">
  <param name="spec" type="string">
<description>Equation, e.g. y c x</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list">
<description>Series used (e.g. dataset)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="wexpr" type="string">
<description>Weight series or expression</description>
  </param>
  <param name="wtype" type="string" optional="true">
<description>istdev (default), ivar, stdev or var</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
 </params>
<code>string wt = exists(wtype) ? tolower(wtype) : &quot;istdev&quot;
errorif(!instring(&quot; istdev ivar stdev var &quot;, &quot; &quot; ~ wt ~ &quot; &quot;), &quot;wtype must be istdev, ivar, stdev or var&quot;)
strings tok = strsplit(spec)
series evw_y = ev_gen(tok[1], vars)
series evw_s = ev_gen(wexpr, vars)
# gretl wls minimises sum(w * u^2): EViews weights multiply the residuals
series evw_w = wt == &quot;istdev&quot; ? 1 / evw_s^2 : (wt == &quot;ivar&quot; ? 1 / evw_s : (wt == &quot;stdev&quot; ? evw_s^2 : evw_s))
list X = null
strings lab = array(0)
scalar hascon = 0
loop i = 2..nelem(tok)
  if tolower(tok[i]) == &quot;c&quot;
    list X += const
    lab += &quot;C&quot;
    hascon = 1
  else
    string v = sprintf(&quot;evw_x%d&quot;, i)
    series @v = ev_gen(tok[i], vars)
    list X += @v
    lab += toupper(tok[i])
  endif
endloop
scalar n0 = $nobs
wls evw_w evw_y X --quiet
bundle b
b.spec = spec
b.method = &quot;Least Squares&quot;
b.eqline = sprintf(&quot;Weighting series: %s\nWeight type: %s&quot;, toupper(wexpr), wt == &quot;istdev&quot; ? &quot;Inverse standard deviation&quot; : (wt == &quot;ivar&quot; ? &quot;Inverse variance&quot; : (wt == &quot;stdev&quot; ? &quot;Standard deviation&quot; : &quot;Variance&quot;)))
b.depvar = toupper(tok[1])
b.labels = lab
b.covtype = &quot;ordinary&quot;
b.coeff = $coeff
b.stderr = $stderr
b.vcv = $vcv
b.T = $T
b.k = $ncoeff
b.rsq = $rsq
b.adjrsq = 1 - (1 - $rsq) * ($T - 1) / ($T - $ncoeff)
b.sigma = $sigma
b.ssr = $ess
b.lnl = $lnl
b.dw = $dw
b.hascon = hascon
b.adjusted = $T &lt; n0
b.estdate = strftime($now[1], &quot;%m/%d/%y   Time: %H:%M&quot;)
series evw_u = $uhat
series evw_f = $yhat
smpl ok(evw_u) --restrict
b.y = {evw_y}
b.X = {X}
b.uhat = {evw_u}
b.yhat = {evw_f}
series evw_o = obs
b.tobs = {evw_o}
b.sample = sprintf(&quot;%s %s&quot;, obslabel($t1), obslabel($t2))
scalar n = b.T
scalar k = b.k
matrix d = b.y - meanc(b.y)
b.meany = meanc(b.y)
b.sdy = sqrt(d'd / (n - 1))
b.aic = -2 * b.lnl / n + 2 * k / n
b.sc = -2 * b.lnl / n + k * log(n) / n
b.hq = -2 * b.lnl / n + 2 * k * log(log(n)) / n
b.F = NA
b.Fp = NA
if hascon &amp;&amp; k &gt; 1
  b.F = (b.rsq / (k - 1)) / ((1 - b.rsq) / (n - k))
  b.Fp = pvalue(F, k - 1, n - k, b.F)
endif
b.tstat = b.coeff ./ b.stderr
matrix p = zeros(k, 1)
loop i = 1..k
  p[i] = 2 * pvalue(t, n - k, abs(b.tstat[i]))
endloop
b.pval = p
if !quiet
  ev_print(&amp;b)
endif
return b
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_cointreg" type="bundle">
 <params count="7">
  <param name="spec" type="string">
<description>Cointegrating equation: y x1 x2 (a constant is added)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list">
<description>Series used (e.g. dataset)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="method" type="string" optional="true">
<description>dols (default) or fmols</description>
  </param>
  <param name="nlead" type="int" min="0" default="1">
<description>DOLS leads of the differenced regressors</description>
  </param>
  <param name="nlag" type="int" min="0" default="1">
<description>DOLS lags of the differenced regressors</description>
  </param>
  <param name="trend" type="string" optional="true">
<description>const (default), linear or none</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
 </params>
<code>string m = exists(method) ? tolower(method) : &quot;dols&quot;
errorif(m != &quot;dols&quot; &amp;&amp; m != &quot;fmols&quot;, &quot;method must be dols or fmols&quot;)
string tr = exists(trend) ? tolower(trend) : &quot;const&quot;
strings tok = strsplit(spec)
scalar kx = nelem(tok) - 1
errorif(kx &lt; 1, &quot;Give the dependent variable and at least one regressor&quot;)
set skip_missing off
series evc_y = ev_gen(tok[1], vars)
matrix Y = {evc_y}
matrix X = {}
matrix DX = {}
loop i = 1..kx
  series evc_x = ev_gen(tok[i+1], vars)
  series evc_l = ev_gen(ev__lagx(tok[i+1], 1, vars), vars)
  X ~= {evc_x}
  DX ~= {evc_x} - {evc_l}
endloop
series evc_o = obs
matrix tob = {evc_o}
scalar T0 = rows(Y)
matrix Dt = {}
if tr != &quot;none&quot;
  Dt ~= ones(T0, 1)
endif
if tr == &quot;linear&quot;
  Dt ~= seq(0, T0 - 1)'
endif
strings lab = array(0)
loop i = 1..kx
  lab += toupper(tok[i+1])
endloop
if tr != &quot;none&quot;
  lab += &quot;C&quot;
endif
if tr == &quot;linear&quot;
  lab += &quot;@TREND&quot;
endif
bundle b
if m == &quot;dols&quot;
  # regressors in levels, deterministic terms, leads and lags of the differences
  matrix W = X ~ Dt
  scalar jlo = -nlead
  loop j = jlo..nlag
    W ~= mlag(DX, j, NA)
  endloop
  matrix okr = sumr(!ok(Y ~ W)) .= 0
  matrix y = selifr(Y, okr)
  matrix Z = selifr(W, okr)
  tob = selifr(tob, okr)
  matrix e = {}
  matrix bh = mols(y, Z, &amp;e)
  scalar n = rows(y)
  scalar kk = cols(Z)
  scalar s2 = e'e / (n - kk)
  # EViews default: OLS covariance rescaled by the long-run residual variance
  scalar bw = ev__nwbw(e)
  scalar lr = ev__lrcov(e, bw, 0)
  matrix V = (lr / s2) * s2 * inv(Z'Z)
  scalar kp = kx + cols(Dt)
  b.coeff = bh[1:kp]
  b.vcv = V[1:kp, 1:kp]
  b.uhat = e
  b.ssr = e'e
  b.lrvar = lr
  b.bandwidth = bw
  b.eqline = sprintf(&quot;Method: Dynamic Least Squares (DOLS)\nCointegrating equation deterministics: %s\n&quot; ~ &quot;Fixed leads and lags specification (lead=%d, lag=%d)\nLong-run variance estimate (Bartlett kernel, Newey-West bandwidth = %.4f)&quot;, tr == &quot;const&quot; ? &quot;C&quot; : (tr == &quot;linear&quot; ? &quot;C @TREND&quot; : &quot;none&quot;), nlead, nlag, bw)
  b.T = n
else
  # Phillips-Hansen fully modified OLS
  matrix okr = sumr(!ok(Y ~ X ~ DX)) .= 0
  matrix y = selifr(Y, okr)
  matrix Xs = selifr(X, okr)
  matrix dX = selifr(DX, okr)
  matrix Dd = {}
  if rows(Dt)
    Dd = selifr(Dt, okr)
  endif
  tob = selifr(tob, okr)
  scalar n = rows(y)
  matrix Z = Xs ~ Dd
  matrix u1 = {}
  matrix b0 = mols(y, Z, &amp;u1)
  matrix U = u1 ~ dX
  scalar bw = ev__nwbw(u1)
  matrix Om = ev__lrcov(U, bw, 0)
  matrix La = ev__lrcov(U, bw, 1)
  matrix O12 = Om[1, 2:]
  matrix O22 = Om[2:, 2:]
  matrix ys = y - dX * inv(O22) * O12'
  matrix l12 = La[2:, 1] - La[2:, 2:] * inv(O22) * O12'
  matrix adjm = n * (l12 | zeros(cols(Dd), 1))
  matrix ZZi = inv(Z'Z)
  matrix bh = ZZi * (Z'ys - adjm)
  scalar w12 = Om[1, 1] - O12 * inv(O22) * O12'
  b.coeff = bh
  b.vcv = w12 * ZZi
  matrix e = y - Z * bh
  b.uhat = e
  b.ssr = e'e
  b.lrvar = w12
  b.bandwidth = bw
  b.eqline = sprintf(&quot;Method: Fully Modified Least Squares (FMOLS)\nCointegrating equation deterministics: %s\n&quot; ~ &quot;Long-run covariance estimate (Bartlett kernel, Newey-West bandwidth = %.4f)&quot;, tr == &quot;const&quot; ? &quot;C&quot; : (tr == &quot;linear&quot; ? &quot;C @TREND&quot; : &quot;none&quot;), bw)
  b.T = n
endif
b.kind = &quot;cointreg&quot;
b.spec = spec
b.depvar = toupper(tok[1])
b.method = m == &quot;dols&quot; ? &quot;Dynamic Least Squares (DOLS)&quot; : &quot;Fully Modified Least Squares (FMOLS)&quot;
b.labels = lab
b.k = rows(b.coeff)
b.stderr = sqrt(diag(b.vcv))
b.tstat = b.coeff ./ b.stderr
matrix pv = zeros(b.k, 1)
loop i = 1..b.k
  pv[i] = 2 * pvalue(t, b.T - b.k, abs(b.tstat[i]))
endloop
b.pval = pv
b.tobs = tob
b.sample = sprintf(&quot;%s %s&quot;, obslabel(minc(tob)), obslabel(maxc(tob)))
b.adjusted = 1
b.estdate = strftime($now[1], &quot;%m/%d/%y   Time: %H:%M&quot;)
b.meany = meanc(y)
b.sdy = sdc(y) * sqrt(n / (n - 1))
if !quiet
  printf &quot;\nDependent Variable: %s\nMethod: %s\nDate: %s\n&quot;, b.depvar, b.method, b.estdate
  printf &quot;Sample (adjusted): %s\nIncluded observations: %d after adjustments\n%s\n\n&quot;, b.sample, b.T, b.eqline
  ev__line(78)
  printf &quot;%-26s%13s%13s%14s%12s\n&quot;, &quot;Variable&quot;, &quot;Coefficient&quot;, &quot;Std. Error&quot;, &quot;t-Statistic&quot;, &quot;Prob.&quot;
  ev__line(78)
  loop i = 1..b.k
    printf &quot;%-26s%13.6f%13.6f%14.6f%12.4f\n&quot;, b.labels[i], b.coeff[i], b.stderr[i], b.tstat[i], b.pval[i]
  endloop
  ev__line(78)
  printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f    %-24s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Mean dependent var&quot;, b.meany, &quot;S.D. dependent var&quot;, b.sdy
  printf &quot;%-22s%14.6f    %-24s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Sum squared resid&quot;, b.ssr, &quot;Long-run variance&quot;, b.lrvar
  ev__line(78)
endif
return b
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_dpanel" type="bundle">
 <params count="7">
  <param name="y" type="string">
<description>Dependent variable</description>
  </param>
  <param name="xs" type="string" optional="true">
<description>Other regressors, e.g. x1 x2</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list">
<description>Series used (e.g. dataset)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="p" type="int" min="1" default="1">
<description>Lags of the dependent variable</description>
  </param>
  <param name="twostep" type="bool" default="0">
<description>Two-step GMM</description>
  </param>
  <param name="timedum" type="bool" default="0">
<description>Period dummies</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
 </params>
<code>errorif($datatype != 3, &quot;Dynamic panel GMM needs a panel page&quot;)
series evd_y = ev_gen(y, vars)
list X = null
strings lab = array(0)
loop j = 1..p
  lab += sprintf(&quot;%s(-%d)&quot;, toupper(y), j)
endloop
if exists(xs) &amp;&amp; strstrip(xs) != &quot;&quot;
  strings tok = strsplit(xs)
  loop i = 1..nelem(tok)
    string v = sprintf(&quot;evd_x%d&quot;, i)
    series @v = ev_gen(tok[i], vars)
    list X += @v
    lab += toupper(tok[i])
  endloop
endif
if nelem(X) == 0
  list X = null
endif
if twostep &amp;&amp; timedum
  dpanel p ; evd_y X --two-step --time-dummies --quiet
elif twostep
  dpanel p ; evd_y X --two-step --quiet
elif timedum
  dpanel p ; evd_y X --time-dummies --quiet
else
  dpanel p ; evd_y X --quiet
endif
bundle b
b.kind = &quot;dpanel&quot;
b.depvar = &quot;D(&quot; ~ toupper(y) ~ &quot;)&quot;
b.method = sprintf(&quot;Panel Generalized Method of Moments (Arellano-Bond, %s)&quot;, twostep ? &quot;2-step&quot; : &quot;1-step&quot;)
scalar k = nelem(lab)
b.coeff = $coeff[1:k]
b.stderr = $stderr[1:k]
b.vcv = $vcv[1:k, 1:k]
b.labels = lab
b.k = k
b.T = $T
b.tstat = b.coeff ./ b.stderr
b.pval = 2 * cnorm(-abs(b.tstat))
catch b.sargan = $sargan
if !quiet
  printf &quot;\nDependent Variable: %s\nMethod: %s\nTransformation: First Differences\n&quot;, b.depvar, b.method
  printf &quot;Total panel observations: %d\n\n&quot;, b.T
  ev__line(78)
  printf &quot;%-26s%13s%13s%14s%12s\n&quot;, &quot;Variable&quot;, &quot;Coefficient&quot;, &quot;Std. Error&quot;, &quot;z-Statistic&quot;, &quot;Prob.&quot;
  ev__line(78)
  loop i = 1..k
    printf &quot;%-26s%13.6f%13.6f%14.6f%12.4f\n&quot;, b.labels[i], b.coeff[i], b.stderr[i], b.tstat[i], b.pval[i]
  endloop
  ev__line(78)
endif
return b
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_coefprint" type="void">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="b" type="bundleref"/>
 </params>
<code># generic coefficient table (cointegrating regressions, dynamic panels)
printf &quot;\nDependent Variable: %s\nMethod: %s\n&quot;, b.depvar, b.method
if inbundle(b, &quot;sample&quot;)
  printf &quot;Sample: %s\n&quot;, b.sample
endif
printf &quot;Included observations: %d\n\n&quot;, b.T
ev__line(78)
printf &quot;%-26s%13s%13s%14s%12s\n&quot;, &quot;Variable&quot;, &quot;Coefficient&quot;, &quot;Std. Error&quot;, &quot;t-Statistic&quot;, &quot;Prob.&quot;
ev__line(78)
loop i = 1..b.k
  printf &quot;%-26s%13.6f%13.6f%14.6f%12.4f\n&quot;, b.labels[i], b.coeff[i], b.stderr[i], b.tstat[i], b.pval[i]
endloop
ev__line(78)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_rescorr" type="matrix">
 <params count="4">
  <param name="b" type="bundle">
<description>Equation with residuals (uhat)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="k" type="int" min="1" default="12">
<description>Lags</description>
  </param>
  <param name="squared" type="bool" default="0">
<description>Correlogram of squared residuals</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
 </params>
<code># AC, PAC, Ljung-Box Q and its p-value for lags 1..k (EViews eq.correlogram / correlsq)
matrix u = b.uhat
if squared
  u = u.^2
endif
u = u - meanc(u)
scalar T = rows(u)
matrix ac = zeros(k, 1)
loop j = 1..k
  ac[j] = (u[j+1:T]'u[1:T-j]) / (u'u)
endloop
# partial autocorrelations by Durbin-Levinson
matrix pac = zeros(k, 1)
matrix phi = zeros(k, k)
loop j = 1..k
  if j == 1
    phi[1, 1] = ac[1]
  else
    scalar num = ac[j]
    scalar den = 1
    loop i = 1..j-1
      num -= phi[j-1, i] * ac[j-i]
      den -= phi[j-1, i] * ac[i]
    endloop
    phi[j, j] = num / den
    loop i = 1..j-1
      phi[j, i] = phi[j-1, i] - phi[j, j] * phi[j-1, j-i]
    endloop
  endif
  pac[j] = phi[j, j]
endloop
matrix Q = cum(T * (T + 2) * ac.^2 ./ (T - seq(1, k)'))
scalar narma = inbundle(b, &quot;narma&quot;) ? b.narma : 0
matrix pv = zeros(k, 1)
loop j = 1..k
  pv[j] = j &gt; narma ? pvalue(c, j - narma, Q[j]) : NA
endloop
matrix R = ac ~ pac ~ Q ~ pv
cnameset(R, defarray(&quot;AC&quot;, &quot;PAC&quot;, &quot;Q-Stat&quot;, &quot;Prob&quot;))
if !quiet
  printf &quot;\nCorrelogram of %s\nIncluded observations: %d\n\n&quot;, squared ? &quot;Residuals Squared&quot; : &quot;Residuals&quot;, T
  printf &quot;%6s%12s%12s%12s%10s\n&quot;, &quot;&quot;, &quot;AC&quot;, &quot;PAC&quot;, &quot;Q-Stat&quot;, &quot;Prob&quot;
  loop j = 1..k
    printf &quot;%6d%12.4f%12.4f%12.4f%10.4f\n&quot;, j, ac[j], pac[j], Q[j], pv[j]
  endloop
endif
return R
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_ubreak" type="bundle">
 <params count="3">
  <param name="b" type="bundle">
<description>ev_ls result</description>
  </param>
  <param name="trim" type="scalar" default="0.15">
<description>Trimming fraction (EViews default 15%)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
 </params>
<code># Quandt-Andrews unknown breakpoint test: Chow F at every date in the trimmed sample
errorif(!inbundle(b, &quot;X&quot;), &quot;The Quandt-Andrews test needs a least squares equation (ev_ls)&quot;)
matrix y = b.y
matrix X = b.X
scalar n = rows(y)
scalar k = cols(X)
scalar t1 = ceil(trim * n)
scalar t2 = floor((1 - trim) * n)
matrix Fs = {}
matrix at = {}
loop t = t1 + 1..t2
  matrix m1 = seq(1, n)' .&lt; t
  bundle a1 = ev__olsr(selifr(y, m1), selifr(X, m1))
  bundle a2 = ev__olsr(selifr(y, !m1), selifr(X, !m1))
  scalar ssru = a1.ssr + a2.ssr
  Fs |= ((b.ssr - ssru) / k) / (ssru / (n - 2 * k))
  at |= b.tobs[t]
endloop
bundle r
r.F = Fs
r.tobs = at
scalar im = imaxc(Fs)
r.maxF = Fs[im]
r.maxWald = k * Fs[im]
r.break = obslabel(at[im])
r.expF = log(meanc(exp(Fs / 2)))
r.aveF = meanc(Fs)
# Andrews (1993) asymptotic p-value of the sup-Wald statistic (gretl qlrpval)
r.maxWaldp = qlrpval(r.maxWald, k, trim, 1 - trim)
if !quiet
  printf &quot;\nQuandt-Andrews unknown breakpoint test\nNull Hypothesis: No breakpoints within %g%% trimmed data\n&quot;, 100 * trim
  printf &quot;Varying regressors: all equation variables\nEquation Sample: %s\nTest Sample: %s %s\nNumber of breaks compared: %d\n\n&quot;, b.sample, obslabel(at[1]), obslabel(at[rows(at)]), rows(at)
  printf &quot;%-40s%14s%10s\n&quot;, &quot;Statistic&quot;, &quot;Value&quot;, &quot;Prob.&quot;
  ev__line(64)
  printf &quot;%-40s%14.6f%10.4f\n&quot;, sprintf(&quot;Maximum Wald F-statistic (%s)&quot;, r.break), r.maxF, r.maxWaldp
  printf &quot;%-40s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Exp Wald F-statistic&quot;, r.expF
  printf &quot;%-40s%14.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Ave Wald F-statistic&quot;, r.aveF
  ev__line(64)
  printf &quot;Note: probability from Andrews (1993) via Hansen's approximation (gretl qlrpval)\n&quot;
endif
return r
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_vif" type="matrix">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="b" type="bundle">
<description>ev_ls result</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
 </params>
<code># coefficient variance (uncentered) and centered variance inflation factors
errorif(!inbundle(b, &quot;X&quot;), &quot;VIFs need a least squares equation (ev_ls)&quot;)
matrix X = b.X
matrix V = b.vcv
scalar k = cols(X)
matrix R = zeros(k, 3)
loop j = 1..k
  R[j, 1] = V[j, j]
  matrix xj = X[, j]
  matrix oth = {}
  if j == 1
    oth = X[, 2:k]
  elif j == k
    oth = X[, 1:k-1]
  else
    oth = X[, 1:j-1] ~ X[, j+1:k]
  endif
  matrix e = xj - oth * mols(xj, oth)
  R[j, 2] = (xj'xj) / (e'e)                 # uncentered VIF
  matrix d = xj - meanc(xj)
  R[j, 3] = sdc(xj) &gt; 0 ? (d'd) / (e'e) : NA # centered VIF (NA for the constant)
endloop
if !quiet
  printf &quot;\nVariance Inflation Factors\nIncluded observations: %d\n\n&quot;, b.T
  printf &quot;%-20s%16s%16s%16s\n&quot;, &quot;Variable&quot;, &quot;Coefficient&quot;, &quot;Uncentered&quot;, &quot;Centered&quot;
  printf &quot;%-20s%16s%16s%16s\n&quot;, &quot;&quot;, &quot;Variance&quot;, &quot;VIF&quot;, &quot;VIF&quot;
  ev__line(68)
  loop j = 1..k
    if ok(R[j, 3])
      printf &quot;%-20s%16.6g%16.6f%16.6f\n&quot;, b.labels[j], R[j, 1], R[j, 2], R[j, 3]
    else
      printf &quot;%-20s%16.6g%16.6f%16s\n&quot;, b.labels[j], R[j, 1], R[j, 2], &quot;NA&quot;
    endif
  endloop
endif
return R
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_paneltests" type="bundle">
 <params count="3">
  <param name="spec" type="string">
<description>Equation, e.g. y c x</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list">
<description>Series used (e.g. dataset)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
 </params>
<code>bundle fe = ev_panel(spec, vars, &quot;fixed&quot;, 0, 1)
bundle re = ev_panel(spec, vars, &quot;random&quot;, 0, 1)
bundle po = ev_panel(spec, vars, &quot;none&quot;, 0, 1)
# slopes only (no constant)
matrix keep = zeros(1, fe.k)
loop i = 1..fe.k
  keep[i] = fe.xlab[i] != &quot;C&quot;
endloop
matrix d = selifr(fe.coeff - re.coeff, keep')
matrix Vd = selifc(selifr(fe.vcv - re.vcv, keep'), keep)
bundle r
r.hausman = qform(d', inv(Vd))
r.hdf = rows(d)
r.hp = pvalue(c, r.hdf, r.hausman)
scalar N = fe.ncross
scalar q = N - 1
r.F = ((po.ssr - fe.ssr) / q) / (fe.ssr / fe.df)
r.Fdf1 = q
r.Fdf2 = fe.df
r.Fp = pvalue(F, q, fe.df, r.F)
r.chi2 = -2 * (po.lnl - fe.lnl)
r.chi2p = pvalue(c, q, r.chi2)
if !quiet
  printf &quot;\nCorrelated Random Effects - Hausman Test\nTest cross-section random effects\n\n&quot;
  printf &quot;%-26s%18s%10s%10s\n&quot;, &quot;Test Summary&quot;, &quot;Chi-Sq. Statistic&quot;, &quot;Chi-Sq. d.f.&quot;, &quot;Prob.&quot;
  ev__line(68)
  printf &quot;%-26s%18.6f%10d%10.4f\n&quot;, &quot;Cross-section random&quot;, r.hausman, r.hdf, r.hp
  ev__line(68)
  printf &quot;\nRedundant Fixed Effects Tests\nTest cross-section fixed effects\n\n&quot;
  printf &quot;%-26s%14s%14s%10s\n&quot;, &quot;Effects Test&quot;, &quot;Statistic&quot;, &quot;d.f.&quot;, &quot;Prob.&quot;
  ev__line(68)
  printf &quot;%-26s%14.6f%14s%10.4f\n&quot;, &quot;Cross-section F&quot;, r.F, sprintf(&quot;(%d,%d)&quot;, q, fe.df), r.Fp
  printf &quot;%-26s%14.6f%14d%10.4f\n&quot;, &quot;Cross-section Chi-square&quot;, r.chi2, q, r.chi2p
  ev__line(68)
endif
return r
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_cause" type="matrix">
 <params count="4">
  <param name="names" type="string">
<description>Series, e.g. y x z</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list">
<description>Series used (e.g. dataset)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="p" type="int" min="1" default="2">
<description>Lags</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
 </params>
<code>strings tok = strsplit(names)
scalar m = nelem(tok)
set skip_missing off
matrix Y = {}
matrices L = array(m)
loop i = 1..m
  series evg_x = ev_gen(tok[i], vars)
  Y ~= {evg_x}
  matrix M = {}
  loop j = 1..p
    series evg_l = ev_gen(ev__lagx(tok[i], j, vars), vars)
    M ~= {evg_l}
  endloop
  L[i] = M
endloop
matrix R = {}
if !quiet
  printf &quot;\nPairwise Granger Causality Tests\nLags: %d\n\n&quot;, p
  printf &quot;%-44s%8s%14s%10s\n&quot;, &quot;Null Hypothesis:&quot;, &quot;Obs&quot;, &quot;F-Statistic&quot;, &quot;Prob.&quot;
  ev__line(76)
endif
loop a = 1..m
  loop cc = 1..m
    if a != cc
      # does tok[c] Granger-cause tok[a]?
      matrix yv = Y[, a]
      matrix Xr = ones(rows(yv), 1) ~ L[a]
      matrix Xu = Xr ~ L[cc]
      matrix okr = sumr(!ok(yv ~ Xu)) .= 0
      bundle r0 = ev__olsr(selifr(yv, okr), selifr(Xr, okr))
      bundle r1 = ev__olsr(selifr(yv, okr), selifr(Xu, okr))
      scalar n = sumc(okr)
      scalar Fst = ((r0.ssr - r1.ssr) / p) / (r1.ssr / (n - cols(Xu)))
      scalar pv = pvalue(F, p, n - cols(Xu), Fst)
      R |= {cc, a, n, Fst, pv}
      if !quiet
        printf &quot;%-44s%8d%14.5f%10.4f\n&quot;, sprintf(&quot; %s does not Granger Cause %s&quot;, toupper(tok[cc]), toupper(tok[a])), n, Fst, pv
      endif
    endif
  endloop
endloop
return R
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_varwhite" type="bundle">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="v" type="bundle">
<description>ev_varest result</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
 </params>
<code># joint White test without cross terms (Lutkepohl/Kelejian system LM)
matrix U = v.sys.uhat
matrix X = v.sys.X
scalar T = rows(U)
scalar n = cols(U)
matrix Z = ones(T, 1)
loop j = 1..cols(X)
  if sdc(X[, j]) &gt; 0
    Z ~= X[, j] ~ X[, j].^2
  endif
endloop
matrix P = {}
loop i = 1..n
  loop j = i..n
    P ~= U[, i] .* U[, j]
  endloop
endloop
scalar m = cols(P)
matrix Pc = P .- meanc(P)
matrix E = P - Z * mols(P, Z)
scalar q = cols(Z) - 1
bundle r
r.chi2 = T * (m - tr(inv(Pc'Pc / T) * (E'E / T)))
r.df = m * q
r.p = pvalue(c, r.df, r.chi2)
if !quiet
  printf &quot;\nVAR Residual Heteroskedasticity Tests (Levels and Squares)\nIncluded observations: %d\n\n&quot;, T
  printf &quot;Joint test:\n%14s%8s%10s\n&quot;, &quot;Chi-sq&quot;, &quot;df&quot;, &quot;Prob.&quot;
  printf &quot;%14.6f%8d%10.4f\n&quot;, r.chi2, r.df, r.p
endif
return r
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_varimpulse" type="bundle">
 <params count="7">
  <param name="v" type="bundle">
<description>ev_varest result</description>
  </param>
  <param name="h" type="int" min="1" default="10">
<description>Horizon</description>
  </param>
  <param name="kind" type="string" optional="true">
<description>chol (default) or gen (generalized)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="accum" type="bool" default="0">
<description>Accumulated responses</description>
  </param>
  <param name="reps" type="int" min="0" default="200">
<description>Bootstrap repetitions for the bands (0: none)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="level" type="scalar" default="0.95">
<description>Band coverage</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
 </params>
<code>string k = exists(kind) ? tolower(kind) : &quot;chol&quot;
errorif(k != &quot;chol&quot; &amp;&amp; k != &quot;gen&quot;, &quot;kind must be chol or gen&quot;)
scalar n = v.n
matrix A = v.sys.A
matrix S = v.sys.sigma
bundle r
r.irf = ev__irfs(A, S, n, h, k, accum)
if reps &gt; 0
  # residual bootstrap: rebuild the data with resampled residuals, re-estimate by OLS
  matrix U = v.sys.uhat
  matrix X = v.sys.X
  matrix Y = v.sys.Y
  matrix B = v.coeff
  scalar T = rows(U)
  scalar p = maxr(v.lags)
  matrix lg = v.lags
  matrix draws = zeros(reps, h * n * n)
  loop b = 1..reps
    matrix Ub = U[mrandgen(i, 1, T, T, 1),]
    matrix Yb = Y
    matrix Xb = X
    loop t = 1..T
      # rebuild the lagged regressors from the simulated values
      matrix row = X[t,]
      scalar col = v.hasc
      loop i = 1..n
        loop jj = 1..cols(lg)
          scalar j = lg[jj]
          col++
          if t - j &gt;= 1
            row[col] = Yb[t - j, i]
          endif
        endloop
      endloop
      Xb[t,] = row
      Yb[t,] = row * B + Ub[t,]
    endloop
    matrix Bb = mols(Yb, Xb)
    matrix Eb = Yb - Xb * Bb
    # companion matrix of the bootstrap estimates
    matrix Ab = zeros(n * p, n * p)
    loop i = 1..n
      scalar col = v.hasc
      loop ii = 1..n
        loop jj = 1..cols(lg)
          scalar j = lg[jj]
          col++
          Ab[i, (j - 1) * n + ii] = Bb[col, i]
        endloop
      endloop
    endloop
    if p &gt; 1
      Ab[n + 1:n * p, 1:n * (p - 1)] = I(n * (p - 1))
    endif
    draws[b,] = vec(ev__irfs(Ab, Eb'Eb / T, n, h, k, accum))'
  endloop
  scalar a = (1 - level) / 2
  r.lo = mshape(quantile(draws, a)', h, n * n)
  r.hi = mshape(quantile(draws, 1 - a)', h, n * n)
  r.reps = reps
endif
r.kind = k
r.accum = accum
if !quiet
  printf &quot;\n%s%s impulse responses, horizon %d%s\n&quot;, accum ? &quot;Accumulated &quot; : &quot;&quot;, k == &quot;gen&quot; ? &quot;Generalized&quot; : &quot;Cholesky (one S.D.)&quot;, h, reps &gt; 0 ? sprintf(&quot;, %d bootstrap draws&quot;, reps) : &quot;&quot;
  loop s = 1..n
    printf &quot;\nResponse to %s:\n%6s&quot;, v.ylab[s], &quot;Period&quot;
    loop t = 1..n
      printf &quot;%16s&quot;, v.ylab[t]
    endloop
    printf &quot;\n&quot;
    loop t = 1..h
      printf &quot;%6d&quot;, t
      loop i = 1..n
        printf &quot;%16.6f&quot;, r.irf[t, (s - 1) * n + i]
      endloop
      printf &quot;\n&quot;
    endloop
  endloop
endif
return r
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_var2eqs" type="bundles">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="v" type="bundle">
<description>ev_varest result</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list">
<description>Series used (e.g. dataset)</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code># each VAR equation as a least-squares equation bundle, for ev_modelsolve (var.makemodel)
bundles out = array(0)
scalar n = v.n
matrix lg = v.lags
loop i = 1..n
  string spec = v.ytok[i]
  if v.hasc
    spec ~= &quot; c&quot;
  endif
  loop ii = 1..n
    loop jj = 1..cols(lg)
      spec ~= &quot; &quot; ~ ev__lagx(v.ytok[ii], lg[jj], vars)
    endloop
  endloop
  loop x = 1..nelem(v.xtok)
    if tolower(v.xtok[x]) != &quot;c&quot;
      spec ~= &quot; &quot; ~ v.xtok[x]
    endif
  endloop
  bundle e = defbundle()
  e.kind = &quot;ls&quot;
  e.spec = spec
  e.coeff = v.coeff[, i]
  e.sigma = sqrt(v.sys.sigma[i, i])
  out += e
endloop
return out
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_vecrestrict" type="bundle">
 <params count="4">
  <param name="v" type="bundle">
<description>ev_vecm result</description>
  </param>
  <param name="restr" type="string">
<description>e.g. B(1,1)=1, B(1,2)=-1</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list">
<description>Series used (e.g. dataset)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
 </params>
<code># linear restrictions on vec(beta); EViews B(i,j) = gretl beta[j, i]
matrix beta = v.beta
scalar nb = rows(beta)
scalar r = cols(beta)
# restrictions are separated by commas outside B(i,j)
strings parts = strsplit(regsub(regsub(restr, &quot;\s&quot;, &quot;&quot;), &quot;,(?![0-9]+\))&quot;, &quot;;&quot;), &quot;;&quot;)
matrix R = {}
matrix q = {}
loop i = 1..nelem(parts)
  string pt = parts[i]
  errorif(!instring(pt, &quot;=&quot;), &quot;Each restriction needs '=': &quot; ~ pt)
  strings lrs = strsplit(pt, &quot;=&quot;)
  matrix row = zeros(1, nb * r)
  string t = regsub(toupper(lrs[1]), &quot;-&quot;, &quot;+-&quot;)
  strings terms = strsplit(t, &quot;+&quot;)
  loop jj = 1..nelem(terms)
    string term = terms[jj]
    if term != &quot;&quot;
      errorif(instring(term, &quot;A(&quot;), &quot;Restrictions on the adjustment coefficients A() are not supported&quot;)
      string sc = regsub(term, &quot;\*?B\(.*&quot;, &quot;&quot;)
      scalar coef = sc == &quot;&quot; ? 1 : (sc == &quot;-&quot; ? -1 : atof(sc))
      scalar ri = atof(regsub(term, &quot;.*B\(([0-9]+),.*&quot;, &quot;\1&quot;))
      scalar cj = atof(regsub(term, &quot;.*B\([0-9]+,([0-9]+)\).*&quot;, &quot;\1&quot;))
      row[(ri - 1) * nb + cj] = row[(ri - 1) * nb + cj] + coef
    endif
  endloop
  R |= row
  q |= atof(lrs[2])
endloop
bundle w = ev_vecm(v.spec, vars, v.case, v.rank, 1, null, R, q)
w.restr = restr
if !quiet
  printf &quot;\nCointegration Restrictions: %s\n&quot;, restr
  printf &quot;Restricted cointegrating vector(s) (rows = variables):\n&quot;
  matrix br = w.beta
  print br
  if inbundle(w, &quot;lr_restr&quot;)
    printf &quot;LR test for binding restrictions: Chi-square(%d) = %g, Prob. = %.4f\n&quot;, rows(q) - r * r, w.lr_restr, w.lr_restr_p
  endif
endif
return w
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_ngperron" type="bundle">
 <params count="5">
  <param name="expr" type="string">
<description>Series or expression</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list">
<description>Series used (e.g. dataset)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="trend" type="bool" default="0">
<description>Include a linear trend</description>
  </param>
  <param name="maxlag" type="int" min="-1" default="-1">
<description>Maximum lag (-1: EViews rule)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
 </params>
<code># ERS point-optimal P_T and Ng-Perron MZa, MZt, MSB, MPT (AR spectral, GLS-detrended, SIC lags)
set skip_missing off
series evn_x = ev_gen(expr, vars)
matrix y = {evn_x}
y = selifr(y, ok(y))
scalar T = rows(y)
scalar cb = 0
matrix yd = ev__glsdetrend(y, trend, &amp;cb)
scalar pmax = maxlag &gt;= 0 ? maxlag : floor(12 * (T / 100)^(1 / 4))
scalar kopt = 0
scalar f0 = ev__arspec(yd, pmax, &amp;kopt)
matrix yl = yd[1:T-1]
scalar s1 = yl'yl / T^2
scalar yT = yd[T]
bundle r
r.MZa = (yT^2 / T - f0) / (2 * s1)
r.MSB = sqrt(s1 / f0)
r.MZt = r.MZa * r.MSB
r.MPT = trend ? (cb^2 * s1 + (1 - cb) * yT^2 / T) / f0 : (cb^2 * s1 - cb * yT^2 / T) / f0
# ERS point optimal: SSR of the quasi-differenced regressions at a-bar and at 1
scalar abar = 1 + cb / T
matrix Z = ones(T, 1)
if trend
  Z ~= seq(1, T)'
endif
matrix yq = y[1] | (y[2:T] - abar * y[1:T-1])
matrix Zq = Z[1,] | (Z[2:T,] - abar * Z[1:T-1,])
matrix ea = yq - Zq * mols(yq, Zq)
matrix y1 = y[1] | (y[2:T] - y[1:T-1])
matrix Z1 = Z[1,] | (Z[2:T,] - Z[1:T-1,])
matrix e1 = y1 - Z1 * mols(y1, Z1)
r.PT = (ea'ea - abar * e1'e1) / f0
r.f0 = f0
r.lag = kopt
r.T = T
# asymptotic critical values (1%, 5%, 10%): Ng and Perron (2001) Table 1; ERS (1996) Table 1
if trend
  r.cv = {-23.8, -3.42, 0.143, 4.03; -17.3, -2.91, 0.168, 5.48; -14.2, -2.62, 0.185, 6.67}
  r.cvpt = {4.26, 5.64, 6.79}
else
  r.cv = {-13.8, -2.58, 0.174, 1.78; -8.1, -1.98, 0.233, 3.17; -5.7, -1.62, 0.275, 4.45}
  r.cvpt = {1.99, 3.26, 4.48}
endif
if !quiet
  printf &quot;\nNull Hypothesis: %s has a unit root\nExogenous: %s\n&quot;, toupper(expr), trend ? &quot;Constant, Linear Trend&quot; : &quot;Constant&quot;
  printf &quot;Lag length: %d (Spectral GLS-detrended AR based on SIC, maxlag=%d)\nSample size: %d\n\n&quot;, kopt, pmax, T
  printf &quot;%-34s%10s%10s%10s%10s\n&quot;, &quot;&quot;, &quot;MZa&quot;, &quot;MZb&quot;, &quot;MSB&quot;, &quot;MPT&quot;
  ev__line(74)
  printf &quot;%-34s%10.4f%10.4f%10.4f%10.4f\n&quot;, &quot;Ng-Perron test statistics&quot;, r.MZa, r.MZt, r.MSB, r.MPT
  strings lv = defarray(&quot;1%&quot;, &quot;5%&quot;, &quot;10%&quot;)
  loop i = 1..3
    printf &quot;%-34s%10.3f%10.3f%10.3f%10.3f\n&quot;, sprintf(&quot;Asymptotic critical values*: %s&quot;, lv[i]), r.cv[i, 1], r.cv[i, 2], r.cv[i, 3], r.cv[i, 4]
  endloop
  ev__line(74)
  printf &quot;*Ng-Perron (2001, Table 1)\n\nElliott-Rothenberg-Stock point-optimal P-statistic: %.4f\n&quot;, r.PT
  printf &quot;Asymptotic critical values (ERS 1996): 1%% %.2f  5%% %.2f  10%% %.2f\n&quot;, r.cvpt[1], r.cvpt[2], r.cvpt[3]
  printf &quot;(MZb above is MZt)\n&quot;
endif
return r
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_zivot" type="bundle">
 <params count="6">
  <param name="expr" type="string">
<description>Series or expression</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list">
<description>Series used (e.g. dataset)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="model" type="string" optional="true">
<description>a (intercept break), b (trend break) or c (both)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="lag" type="int" min="-1" default="-1">
<description>ADF lags (-1: chosen by SIC without break)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="trim" type="scalar" default="0.15"/>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
 </params>
<code># Zivot-Andrews (1992) unit root test with one endogenous break: minimum t over break dates
string md = exists(model) ? tolower(model) : &quot;a&quot;
errorif(md != &quot;a&quot; &amp;&amp; md != &quot;b&quot; &amp;&amp; md != &quot;c&quot;, &quot;model must be a, b or c&quot;)
set skip_missing off
series evz_x = ev_gen(expr, vars)
series evz_o = obs
matrix D = {evz_x} ~ {evz_o}
D = selifr(D, ok(D[, 1]))
matrix y = D[, 1]
matrix tob = D[, 2]
scalar T = rows(y)
matrix dy = y[2:T] - y[1:T-1]
# lag order: SIC on the ADF regression without a break
scalar pmax = floor(12 * (T / 100)^(1 / 4))
scalar p = lag
if lag &lt; 0
  scalar best = 1e300
  loop k = 0..pmax
    matrix Z = ones(T - 1 - pmax, 1) ~ seq(pmax + 2, T)' ~ y[pmax + 1:T - 1]
    loop j = 1..k
      Z ~= dy[pmax + 1 - j:T - 1 - j]
    endloop
    matrix e = {}
    matrix b = mols(dy[pmax + 1:T - 1], Z, &amp;e)
    scalar n = rows(e)
    scalar sic = log(e'e / n) + cols(Z) * log(n) / n
    if sic &lt; best
      best = sic
      p = k
    endif
  endloop
endif
scalar t1 = ceil(trim * T)
scalar t2 = floor((1 - trim) * T)
scalar tmin = 1e300
scalar tb = NA
loop bk = t1..t2
  matrix tt = seq(p + 2, T)'
  matrix Z = ones(rows(tt), 1) ~ tt ~ y[p + 1:T - 1]
  if md == &quot;a&quot; || md == &quot;c&quot;
    Z ~= tt .&gt; bk                        # DU: intercept shift
  endif
  if md == &quot;b&quot; || md == &quot;c&quot;
    Z ~= (tt .&gt; bk) .* (tt - bk)         # DT: trend shift
  endif
  loop j = 1..p
    Z ~= dy[p + 1 - j:T - 1 - j]
  endloop
  matrix e = {}
  matrix b = mols(dy[p + 1:T - 1], Z, &amp;e)
  matrix V = (e'e / (rows(e) - cols(Z))) * inv(Z'Z)
  scalar tv = b[3] / sqrt(V[3, 3])
  if tv &lt; tmin
    tmin = tv
    tb = bk
  endif
endloop
bundle r
r.stat = tmin
r.break = obslabel(tob[tb + 1])
r.lag = p
r.model = md
# Zivot and Andrews (1992), Tables 2-4: 1%, 5%, 10%
r.cv = md == &quot;a&quot; ? {-5.34, -4.80, -4.58} : (md == &quot;b&quot; ? {-4.93, -4.42, -4.11} : {-5.57, -5.08, -4.82})
if !quiet
  printf &quot;\nZivot-Andrews Unit Root Test\nNull Hypothesis: %s has a unit root with a structural break in the %s\n&quot;, toupper(expr), md == &quot;a&quot; ? &quot;intercept&quot; : (md == &quot;b&quot; ? &quot;trend&quot; : &quot;intercept and trend&quot;)
  printf &quot;Chosen lag length: %d\nChosen break point: %s\n\n&quot;, p, r.break
  printf &quot;%-30s%12s\n&quot;, &quot;&quot;, &quot;t-Statistic&quot;
  printf &quot;%-30s%12.6f\n&quot;, &quot;Zivot-Andrews test statistic&quot;, r.stat
  printf &quot;%-30s%12.2f\n%-30s%12.2f\n%-30s%12.2f\n&quot;, &quot;1% critical value:&quot;, r.cv[1], &quot;5% critical value:&quot;, r.cv[2], &quot;10% critical value:&quot;, r.cv[3]
endif
return r
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_panelur" type="bundle">
 <params count="5">
  <param name="x" type="series">
<description>Series of a panel page</description>
  </param>
  <param name="test" type="string" optional="true">
<description>fisher (ADF, default), fisherpp or hadri</description>
  </param>
  <param name="trend" type="bool" default="0"/>
  <param name="lag" type="int" min="0" default="1">
<description>ADF lag for the Fisher test</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
 </params>
<code># Maddala-Wu / Choi Fisher-type tests and Hadri's stationarity test
errorif($datatype != 3, &quot;Panel unit root tests need a panel page&quot;)
string ts = exists(test) ? tolower(test) : &quot;fisher&quot;
set skip_missing off
matrix M = ev_unstack(x)
scalar N = cols(M)
matrix pv = zeros(N, 1)
matrix stv = zeros(N, 1)
bundle r
if ts == &quot;hadri&quot;
  matrix LMi = zeros(N, 1)
  scalar ssum = 0
  scalar nobs = 0
  scalar lmh = 0
  matrix s2i = zeros(N, 1)
  matrix etas = zeros(N, 1)
  loop i = 1..N
    matrix yi = M[, i]
    yi = selifr(yi, ok(yi))
    scalar T = rows(yi)
    matrix Z = ones(T, 1)
    if trend
      Z ~= seq(1, T)'
    endif
    matrix e = yi - Z * mols(yi, Z)
    matrix S = cum(e)
    etas[i] = (S'S) / T^2
    s2i[i] = e'e / T
  endloop
  scalar s2 = meanc(s2i)
  scalar xi = trend ? 1 / 15 : 1 / 6
  scalar ze = trend ? sqrt(11 / 6300) : sqrt(1 / 45)
  scalar LMh = meanc(etas / s2)              # homoskedastic
  scalar LMhet = meanc(etas ./ s2i)          # heteroskedasticity consistent
  r.Z = sqrt(N) * (LMh - xi) / ze
  r.Zhet = sqrt(N) * (LMhet - xi) / ze
  r.p = 1 - cnorm(r.Z)
  r.phet = 1 - cnorm(r.Zhet)
  if !quiet
    printf &quot;\nHadri Panel Unit Root Test\nNull Hypothesis: Stationarity\nExogenous variables: %s\n\n&quot;, trend ? &quot;Individual effects, individual linear trends&quot; : &quot;Individual effects&quot;
    printf &quot;%-34s%14s%10s\n&quot;, &quot;Method&quot;, &quot;Statistic&quot;, &quot;Prob.**&quot;
    printf &quot;%-34s%14.6f%10.4f\n&quot;, &quot;Hadri Z-stat&quot;, r.Z, r.p
    printf &quot;%-34s%14.6f%10.4f\n&quot;, &quot;Heteroscedastic Consistent Z-stat&quot;, r.Zhet, r.phet
  endif
  return r
endif
errorif(ts != &quot;fisher&quot; &amp;&amp; ts != &quot;fisherpp&quot;, &quot;test must be fisher, fisherpp or hadri&quot;)
scalar itv = trend ? 3 : 2
loop i = 1..N
  matrix yi = M[, i]
  yi = selifr(yi, ok(yi))
  scalar T = rows(yi)
  matrix dy = yi[2:T] - yi[1:T-1]
  scalar st = NA
  if ts == &quot;fisher&quot;
    matrix Z = ones(T - 1 - lag, 1)
    if trend
      Z ~= seq(lag + 2, T)'
    endif
    Z ~= yi[lag + 1:T - 1]
    loop j = 1..lag
      Z ~= dy[lag + 1 - j:T - 1 - j]
    endloop
    matrix e = {}
    matrix b = mols(dy[lag + 1:T - 1], Z, &amp;e)
    matrix V = (e'e / (rows(e) - cols(Z))) * inv(Z'Z)
    scalar kk = trend ? 3 : 2
    st = b[kk] / sqrt(V[kk, kk])
    stv[i] = st
    pv[i] = urcpval(st, rows(e), 1, itv)
  else
    matrix Z = ones(T - 1, 1)
    if trend
      Z ~= seq(2, T)'
    endif
    Z ~= yi[1:T - 1]
    matrix e = {}
    matrix b = mols(dy, Z, &amp;e)
    scalar kk = cols(Z)
    scalar s2 = e'e / (rows(e) - kk)
    matrix ZZi = inv(Z'Z)
    scalar se = sqrt(s2 * ZZi[kk, kk])
    scalar g0 = e'e / rows(e)
    scalar l2 = ev__lrvar(e, ev__nwbw(e))
    st = (b[kk] / se) * sqrt(g0 / l2) - rows(e) * (l2 - g0) * se / (2 * sqrt(l2) * sqrt(s2))
    pv[i] = urcpval(st, rows(e), 1, itv)
  endif
endloop
r.pvals = pv
r.stats = stv
r.fisher = -2 * sumc(log(pv))
r.fisherp = pvalue(c, 2 * N, r.fisher)
r.choi = sumc(invcdf(z, pv)) / sqrt(N)
r.choip = cnorm(r.choi)
if !quiet
  printf &quot;\n%s Fisher Panel Unit Root Test\nNull Hypothesis: Unit root (individual unit root process)\nCross-sections: %d\n\n&quot;, ts == &quot;fisher&quot; ? &quot;ADF -&quot; : &quot;PP -&quot;, N
  printf &quot;%-34s%14s%10s\n&quot;, &quot;Method&quot;, &quot;Statistic&quot;, &quot;Prob.**&quot;
  printf &quot;%-34s%14.6f%10.4f\n&quot;, ts == &quot;fisher&quot; ? &quot;ADF - Fisher Chi-square&quot; : &quot;PP - Fisher Chi-square&quot;, r.fisher, r.fisherp
  printf &quot;%-34s%14.6f%10.4f\n&quot;, ts == &quot;fisher&quot; ? &quot;ADF - Choi Z-stat&quot; : &quot;PP - Choi Z-stat&quot;, r.choi, r.choip
  printf &quot;** Probabilities for Fisher tests use the asymptotic Chi-square distribution;\n   the Choi test assumes asymptotic normality.\n&quot;
endif
return r
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_cf" type="series">
 <params count="3">
  <param name="x" type="series">
<description>Series</description>
  </param>
  <param name="low" type="int" min="2" default="6">
<description>Lower period</description>
  </param>
  <param name="high" type="int" min="2" default="32">
<description>Upper period</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code># Christiano-Fitzgerald asymmetric full-sample filter (random-walk assumption, drift removed)
set skip_missing off
matrix y = {x}
errorif(sumc(!ok(y)) &gt; 0, &quot;The series has missing values in the sample&quot;)
scalar T = rows(y)
# remove the drift
scalar d = (y[T] - y[1]) / (T - 1)
y = y - d * seq(0, T - 1)'
scalar a = 2 * $pi / high
scalar bb = 2 * $pi / low
matrix B = zeros(T, 1)                     # B[j+1] = B_j
B[1] = (bb - a) / $pi
loop j = 1..T - 1
  B[j + 1] = (sin(j * bb) - sin(j * a)) / ($pi * j)
endloop
matrix cy = zeros(T, 1)
loop t = 1..T
  scalar v = B[1] * y[t]
  # forward: y[t+1] .. y[T-1], then y[T] with B-tilde(T-t) = -B0/2 - sum B
  scalar sf = 0
  if T - t - 1 &gt;= 1
    loop j = 1..T - t - 1
      v += B[j + 1] * y[t + j]
      sf += B[j + 1]
    endloop
  endif
  v += (-B[1] / 2 - sf) * y[T]
  # backward: y[t-1] .. y[2], then y[1] with B-tilde(t-1)
  scalar sb = 0
  if t - 2 &gt;= 1
    loop j = 1..t - 2
      v += B[j + 1] * y[t - j]
      sb += B[j + 1]
    endloop
  endif
  v += (-B[1] / 2 - sb) * y[1]
  cy[t] = v
endloop
series out = cy
return out
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_smooth" type="series">
 <params count="6">
  <param name="x" type="series">
<description>Series</description>
  </param>
  <param name="method" type="string" optional="true">
<description>s (single), d (double), n (Holt-Winters no seasonal), a (additive) or m (multiplicative)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="pa" type="scalar" default="NA">
<description>alpha</description>
  </param>
  <param name="pb" type="scalar" default="NA">
<description>beta</description>
  </param>
  <param name="pg" type="scalar" default="NA">
<description>gamma</description>
  </param>
  <param name="res" type="bundleref" optional="true">
<description>Output: parameters, SSR, RMSE</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code># exponential smoothing; parameters not given are estimated by minimising the sum of squared one-step errors
string m = exists(method) ? tolower(method) : &quot;s&quot;
errorif(!instring(&quot; s d n a m &quot;, &quot; &quot; ~ m ~ &quot; &quot;), &quot;method must be s, d, n, a or m&quot;)
set skip_missing off
matrix y = {x}
errorif(sumc(!ok(y)) &gt; 0, &quot;The series has missing values in the sample&quot;)
scalar s = $pd
errorif((m == &quot;a&quot; || m == &quot;m&quot;) &amp;&amp; s &lt; 2, &quot;Seasonal Holt-Winters needs seasonal data&quot;)
errorif(m == &quot;m&quot; &amp;&amp; minc(y) &lt;= 0, &quot;Multiplicative seasonals need positive data&quot;)
matrix fix = {pa, pb, pg}
scalar np = m == &quot;s&quot; || m == &quot;d&quot; ? 1 : (m == &quot;n&quot; ? 2 : 3)
matrix th = zeros(np, 1)                 # logit scale
matrix th0 = th
scalar nfree = 0
loop i = 1..np
  nfree += !ok(fix[i])
endloop
if nfree &gt; 0
  set max_verbose off
  scalar ssr = BFGSmin(&amp;th, &quot;ev__smooth_ssr(th, y, m, s, fix)&quot;)
endif
matrix f = ev__smooth_run(th, y, m, s, fix)
if exists(res)
  matrix par = 1 ./ (1 + exp(-th))
  loop i = 1..np
    if ok(fix[i])
      par[i] = fix[i]
    endif
  endloop
  res.params = par
  res.ssr = sumc((y - f[, 1]).^2)
  res.rmse = sqrt(res.ssr / rows(y))
endif
return f[, 2]
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_ipolate" type="series">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="x" type="series">
<description>Series with missing values</description>
  </param>
  <param name="kind" type="string" optional="true">
<description>lin (default) or log</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code># fills interior missing values by linear (or log-linear) interpolation, as EViews ipolate
string k = exists(kind) ? tolower(kind) : &quot;lin&quot;
set skip_missing off
matrix y = {x}
if k == &quot;log&quot;
  errorif(minc(selifr(y, ok(y))) &lt;= 0, &quot;Log interpolation needs positive values&quot;)
  y = log(y)
endif
scalar T = rows(y)
matrix r = y
scalar last = 0
loop t = 1..T
  if ok(y[t])
    if last &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; t - last &gt; 1
      loop j = last + 1..t - 1
        r[j] = y[last] + (y[t] - y[last]) * (j - last) / (t - last)
      endloop
    endif
    last = t
  endif
endloop
if k == &quot;log&quot;
  r = exp(r)
endif
series out = r
return out
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_pcomp" type="bundle">
 <params count="4">
  <param name="names" type="string">
<description>Series, e.g. x1 x2 x3</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list">
<description>Series used (e.g. dataset)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="cov" type="bool" default="0">
<description>Use the covariance (default: correlation) matrix</description>
  </param>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool" default="0"/>
 </params>
<code>strings tok = strsplit(names)
scalar m = nelem(tok)
set skip_missing off
matrix X = {}
series evp_o = obs
loop i = 1..m
  series evp_x = ev_gen(tok[i], vars)
  X ~= {evp_x}
endloop
matrix okr = sumr(!ok(X)) .= 0
X = selifr(X, okr)
matrix tob = selifr({evp_o}, okr)
scalar T = rows(X)
matrix Xc = X .- meanc(X)
matrix S = Xc'Xc / (T - 1)
if !cov
  matrix d = sqrt(diag(S))
  S = S ./ (d * d')
  Xc = Xc ./ d'
endif
matrix EV = {}
matrix lam = eigensym(S, &amp;EV)
# eigensym returns ascending order: reverse
lam = mreverse(lam)
EV = mreverse(EV')'
# sign convention: largest loading of each vector positive
loop j = 1..m
  if EV[imaxc(abs(EV[, j])), j] &lt; 0
    EV[, j] = -EV[, j]
  endif
endloop
bundle r
r.eigval = lam
r.prop = lam / sumc(lam)
r.cumprop = cum(r.prop)
r.eigvec = EV
r.scores = Xc * EV
r.tobs = tob
r.names = tok
if !quiet
  printf &quot;\nPrincipal Components Analysis\nComputed using: %s\nIncluded observations: %d\n\n&quot;, cov ? &quot;Covariance&quot; : &quot;Ordinary correlations&quot;, T
  printf &quot;%-10s%14s%14s%14s\n&quot;, &quot;Number&quot;, &quot;Value&quot;, &quot;Proportion&quot;, &quot;Cumulative&quot;
  loop j = 1..m
    printf &quot;%-10d%14.6f%14.4f%14.4f\n&quot;, j, lam[j], r.prop[j], r.cumprop[j]
  endloop
  printf &quot;\nEigenvectors (loadings):\n%-12s&quot;, &quot;Variable&quot;
  loop j = 1..m
    printf &quot;%12s&quot;, sprintf(&quot;PC %d&quot;, j)
  endloop
  printf &quot;\n&quot;
  loop i = 1..m
    printf &quot;%-12s&quot;, toupper(tok[i])
    loop j = 1..m
      printf &quot;%12.6f&quot;, EV[i, j]
    endloop
    printf &quot;\n&quot;
  endloop
endif
return r
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_pcscore" type="series">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="r" type="bundle">
<description>ev_pcomp result</description>
  </param>
  <param name="j" type="int" min="1" default="1">
<description>Component</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code>return ev__toseries(r.scores[, j], r.tobs)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_kdplot" type="void">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="x" type="series">
<description>Series</description>
  </param>
  <param name="out" type="string" optional="true">
<description>Output file (default: display)</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code># kernel density estimate (Epanechnikov in EViews; gretl's default Gaussian kernel here)
matrix K = kdensity(x)
cnameset(K, defarray(&quot;x&quot;, &quot;Kernel density&quot;))
string o = exists(out) ? out : &quot;display&quot;
gnuplot 2 1 --matrix=K --with-lines --output=&quot;@o&quot;
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_dateadd" type="scalar">
 <params count="3">
  <param name="d" type="scalar">
<description>EViews date number</description>
  </param>
  <param name="n" type="scalar"/>
  <param name="unit" type="string" optional="true">
<description>dd, ww, mm, qq or yy</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code>string u = exists(unit) ? tolower(unit) : &quot;dd&quot;
if u == &quot;dd&quot;
  return d + n
elif u == &quot;ww&quot;
  return d + 7 * n
endif
matrix ymd = ev__ymd(d)
scalar months = u == &quot;mm&quot; ? n : (u == &quot;qq&quot; ? 3 * n : (u == &quot;yy&quot; ? 12 * n : NA))
errorif(!ok(months), &quot;unit must be dd, ww, mm, qq or yy&quot;)
scalar tot = ymd[1] * 12 + ymd[2] - 1 + months
scalar y = floor(tot / 12)
scalar m = tot - 12 * y + 1
scalar dd = ymd[3]
# clamp the day to the length of the target month
scalar ml = monthlen(m, y, 7)
return epochday(y, m, min(dd, ml)) - 1
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_datediff" type="scalar">
 <params count="3">
  <param name="d1" type="scalar">
<description>EViews date number</description>
  </param>
  <param name="d2" type="scalar"/>
  <param name="unit" type="string" optional="true">
<description>dd, ww, mm, qq or yy</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code># d1 - d2 in whole units
string u = exists(unit) ? tolower(unit) : &quot;dd&quot;
if u == &quot;dd&quot;
  return d1 - d2
elif u == &quot;ww&quot;
  return floor((d1 - d2) / 7)
endif
matrix a = ev__ymd(d1)
matrix b = ev__ymd(d2)
scalar months = (a[1] - b[1]) * 12 + a[2] - b[2]
if u == &quot;mm&quot;
  return months
elif u == &quot;qq&quot;
  return floor(months / 3)
elif u == &quot;yy&quot;
  return a[1] - b[1]
endif
errorif(1, &quot;unit must be dd, ww, mm, qq or yy&quot;)
return NA
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_makedate" type="scalar">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="v" type="scalar"/>
  <param name="fmt" type="string">
<description>yyyy, yyyymm, yyyymmdd, yyyy.mm or mm.dd</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code>string f = tolower(fmt)
if f == &quot;yyyy&quot;
  return epochday(v, 1, 1) - 1
elif f == &quot;yyyymm&quot;
  return epochday(floor(v / 100), v % 100, 1) - 1
elif f == &quot;yyyymmdd&quot;
  return epochday(floor(v / 10000), floor(v / 100) % 100, v % 100) - 1
elif f == &quot;yyyy.mm&quot;
  return epochday(floor(v), round(100 * (v - floor(v))), 1) - 1
endif
errorif(1, &quot;format must be yyyy, yyyymm, yyyymmdd or yyyy.mm&quot;)
return NA
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_wfind" type="scalar">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="s" type="string">
<description>Word list</description>
  </param>
  <param name="w" type="string">
<description>Word</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code># position of a word in a space-separated list (0 if absent), case-insensitive
strings t = strsplit(s)
loop i = 1..nelem(t)
  if toupper(t[i]) == toupper(w)
    return i
  endif
endloop
return 0
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_wdrop" type="string">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="s" type="string">
<description>Word list</description>
  </param>
  <param name="drop" type="string">
<description>Words to drop</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code>strings t = strsplit(s)
string out = &quot;&quot;
loop i = 1..nelem(t)
  if !ev_wfind(drop, t[i])
    out ~= (out == &quot;&quot; ? &quot;&quot; : &quot; &quot;) ~ t[i]
  endif
endloop
return out
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_wkeep" type="string">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="s" type="string">
<description>Word list</description>
  </param>
  <param name="keep" type="string">
<description>Words to keep</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code>strings t = strsplit(s)
string out = &quot;&quot;
loop i = 1..nelem(t)
  if ev_wfind(keep, t[i])
    out ~= (out == &quot;&quot; ? &quot;&quot; : &quot; &quot;) ~ t[i]
  endif
endloop
return out
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_wunique" type="string">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="s" type="string">
<description>Word list</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code>strings t = strsplit(s)
string out = &quot;&quot;
loop i = 1..nelem(t)
  if !ev_wfind(out, t[i])
    out ~= (out == &quot;&quot; ? &quot;&quot; : &quot; &quot;) ~ t[i]
  endif
endloop
return out
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_wreplace" type="string">
 <params count="3">
  <param name="s" type="string">
<description>Word list</description>
  </param>
  <param name="src" type="string">
<description>Word</description>
  </param>
  <param name="dst" type="string">
<description>Replacement</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code>strings t = strsplit(s)
string out = &quot;&quot;
loop i = 1..nelem(t)
  string w = toupper(t[i]) == toupper(src) ? dst : t[i]
  out ~= (out == &quot;&quot; ? &quot;&quot; : &quot; &quot;) ~ w
endloop
return out
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_wsort" type="string">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="s" type="string">
<description>Word list</description>
  </param>
  <param name="desc" type="bool" default="0"/>
 </params>
<code>strings t = strsplit(s)
scalar n = nelem(t)
# insertion sort, case-insensitive
loop i = 2..n
  string key = t[i]
  scalar j = i - 1
  loop while j &gt;= 1
    scalar cmpv = strncmp(toupper(t[j]), toupper(key))
    if (desc &amp;&amp; cmpv &lt; 0) || (!desc &amp;&amp; cmpv &gt; 0)
      t[j + 1] = t[j]
      j--
    else
      break
    endif
  endloop
  t[j + 1] = key
endloop
string out = &quot;&quot;
loop i = 1..n
  out ~= (out == &quot;&quot; ? &quot;&quot; : &quot; &quot;) ~ t[i]
endloop
return out
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_covp" type="scalar">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="x" type="series"/>
  <param name="y" type="series"/>
 </params>
<code># EViews @cov: population covariance (divides by n)
smpl ok(x) &amp;&amp; ok(y) --restrict
return cov(x, y) * ($nobs - 1) / $nobs
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_cumprod" type="series">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="x" type="series"/>
 </params>
<code>set skip_missing off
matrix v = {x}
matrix r = v
loop t = 2..rows(v)
  r[t] = r[t - 1] * v[t]
endloop
series out = r
return out
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_cummax" type="series">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="x" type="series"/>
  <param name="mn" type="bool" default="0">
<description>Cumulative minimum instead</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code>set skip_missing off
matrix v = {x}
matrix r = v
loop t = 2..rows(v)
  if ok(r[t - 1]) &amp;&amp; ok(v[t])
    r[t] = mn ? min(r[t - 1], v[t]) : max(r[t - 1], v[t])
  elif ok(r[t - 1])
    r[t] = r[t - 1]
  endif
endloop
series out = r
return out
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_ifirst" type="scalar">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="x" type="series"/>
 </params>
<code># observation number of the first non-missing value (EViews @ifirst)
set skip_missing off
matrix v = {x}
loop t = 1..rows(v)
  if ok(v[t])
    return $t1 + t - 1
  endif
endloop
return NA
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_ilast" type="scalar">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="x" type="series"/>
 </params>
<code>set skip_missing off
matrix v = {x}
scalar n = rows(v)
loop i = 1..n                 # hansl loops only count upwards
  scalar t = n - i + 1
  if ok(v[t])
    return $t1 + t - 1
  endif
endloop
return NA
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev_ls_gui" type="bundle" pkg-role="gui-main">
 <params count="5">
  <param name="spec" type="string">
<description>Equation (EViews syntax)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="spec2" type="string" optional="true">
<description>  ...continued (optional)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="spec3" type="string" optional="true">
<description>  ...continued (optional)</description>
  </param>
  <param name="vars" type="list">
<description>Series used in the equation</description>
  </param>
  <param name="cov" type="int" min="1" max="3" default="1">
<description>Coefficient covariance</description>
<labels count="3">
"Ordinary" "White" "HAC (Newey-West)" </labels>
  </param>
 </params>
<code># optional parts may arrive empty or as the literal text &quot;null&quot;
string s = spec
if exists(spec2) &amp;&amp; strstrip(spec2) != &quot;&quot; &amp;&amp; strstrip(spec2) != &quot;null&quot;
  s ~= &quot; &quot; ~ spec2
endif
if exists(spec3) &amp;&amp; strstrip(spec3) != &quot;&quot; &amp;&amp; strstrip(spec3) != &quot;null&quot;
  s ~= &quot; &quot; ~ spec3
endif
strings cv = defarray(&quot;ordinary&quot;, &quot;white&quot;, &quot;hac&quot;)
bundle b = ev_ls(s, vars, cv[cov])    # prints the table into the result window
return b
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__expand_diff" type="string" private="1">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="s" type="string"/>
 </params>
<code># d(Y), d(Y(-k)), dlog(Y), dlog(Y(-k)), d(log(Y)), d(log(Y(-k))) written with
# explicit lags, so that the first observation of the sample uses pre-sample
# data, as EViews does (gretl's diff/ldiff of a lagged series would give NA)
string e = s
string N = &quot;([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)&quot;
loop k = 0..24
  string lk = k ? sprintf(&quot;\(\s*-\s*%d\s*\)&quot;, k) : &quot;&quot;
  string a = k ? sprintf(&quot;(-%d)&quot;, k) : &quot;&quot;
  string b2 = sprintf(&quot;(-%d)&quot;, k + 1)
  e = regsub(e, &quot;(?i)(?&lt;![A-Za-z0-9_.])dlog\(\s*&quot; ~ N ~ &quot;\s*&quot; ~ lk ~ &quot;\s*\)&quot;, &quot;(log(\1&quot; ~ a ~ &quot;)-log(\1&quot; ~ b2 ~ &quot;))&quot;)
  e = regsub(e, &quot;(?i)(?&lt;![A-Za-z0-9_.])d\(\s*log\(\s*&quot; ~ N ~ &quot;\s*&quot; ~ lk ~ &quot;\s*\)\s*\)&quot;, &quot;(log(\1&quot; ~ a ~ &quot;)-log(\1&quot; ~ b2 ~ &quot;))&quot;)
  e = regsub(e, &quot;(?i)(?&lt;![A-Za-z0-9_.])d\(\s*&quot; ~ N ~ &quot;\s*&quot; ~ lk ~ &quot;\s*\)&quot;, &quot;(\1&quot; ~ a ~ &quot;-\1&quot; ~ b2 ~ &quot;)&quot;)
endloop
return e
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__translate" type="string" private="1">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="s" type="string"/>
 </params>
<code># Rewrite an EViews expression into hansl syntax.
string AT = &quot;@&quot;
string e = ev__expand_diff(s)
# EViews function names -&gt; hansl / package equivalents
e = regsub(e, &quot;(?i)\bdlog\(&quot;, &quot;ldiff(&quot;)
e = regsub(e, &quot;(?i)\bd\(&quot;, &quot;diff(&quot;)
e = regsub(e, &quot;(?i)\blog\(&quot;, &quot;log(&quot;)
e = regsub(e, &quot;(?i)\bexp\(&quot;, &quot;exp(&quot;)
e = regsub(e, &quot;(?i)\babs\(&quot;, &quot;abs(&quot;)
e = regsub(e, &quot;(?i)\bsqr\(&quot;, &quot;sqrt(&quot;)
# EViews at-functions
e = regsub(e, &quot;(?i)&quot; ~ AT ~ &quot;trend(\(\))?&quot;, &quot;(obs-1)&quot;)
e = regsub(e, &quot;(?i)&quot; ~ AT ~ &quot;seas\(&quot;, &quot;ev_seas(&quot;)
e = regsub(e, &quot;(?i)&quot; ~ AT ~ &quot;pchy\(&quot;, &quot;ev_pchy(&quot;)
e = regsub(e, &quot;(?i)&quot; ~ AT ~ &quot;pcy\(&quot;, &quot;ev_pcy(&quot;)
e = regsub(e, &quot;(?i)&quot; ~ AT ~ &quot;pch\(&quot;, &quot;ev_pch(&quot;)
e = regsub(e, &quot;(?i)&quot; ~ AT ~ &quot;pc\(&quot;, &quot;ev_pc(&quot;)
e = regsub(e, &quot;(?i)&quot; ~ AT ~ &quot;movav\(&quot;, &quot;ev_movav(&quot;)
e = regsub(e, &quot;(?i)&quot; ~ AT ~ &quot;movsum\(&quot;, &quot;ev_movsum(&quot;)
e = regsub(e, &quot;(?i)&quot; ~ AT ~ &quot;cumsum\(&quot;, &quot;cum(&quot;)
e = regsub(e, &quot;(?i)&quot; ~ AT ~ &quot;mean\(&quot;, &quot;ev_mean(&quot;)
e = regsub(e, &quot;(?i)&quot; ~ AT ~ &quot;stdev\(&quot;, &quot;ev_stdev(&quot;)
e = regsub(e, &quot;(?i)&quot; ~ AT ~ &quot;abs\(&quot;, &quot;abs(&quot;)
e = regsub(e, &quot;(?i)&quot; ~ AT ~ &quot;log\(&quot;, &quot;log(&quot;)
errorif(instring(e, AT), sprintf(&quot;Unsupported EViews function in '%s'&quot;, s))
return e
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__fit" type="scalar" private="1">
 <params count="4">
  <param name="y" type="matrix" const="true"/>
  <param name="Z" type="matrix" const="true"/>
  <param name="ssr" type="scalarref"/>
  <param name="df" type="scalarref"/>
 </params>
<code># Least squares via generalized inverse (safe if Z is rank-deficient).
# Returns centered R-squared; fills SSR and rank(Z).
matrix e = y - Z * (ginv(Z'Z) * (Z'y))
ssr = e'e
df = rank(Z)
matrix d = y - meanc(y)
return 1 - ssr / (d'd)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__line" type="void" private="1">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="n" type="int" min="1" default="78"/>
 </params>
<code>string s = &quot;&quot;
loop n
  s ~= &quot;=&quot;
endloop
printf &quot;%s\n&quot;, s
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__prep" type="string" private="1">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="expr" type="string"/>
  <param name="vars" type="list"/>
 </params>
<code># EViews expression -&gt; hansl expression in which dataset series are vars.NAME
string evx_e = ev__translate(expr)
strings evx_nms = varnames(vars)
strings evx_ids = strsplit(regsub(evx_e, &quot;[^A-Za-z0-9_]+&quot;, &quot; &quot;))
# Refer to each series as vars.NAME rather than copying it: a copy made
# inside a function holds only in-sample values, while vars.NAME(-k)
# can reach pre-sample observations, as gretl and EViews do for lags.
strings evx_done = array(0)
loop evx_j = 1..nelem(evx_ids)
  string evx_id = evx_ids[evx_j]
  if rows(instrings(evx_nms, evx_id)) &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; rows(instrings(evx_done, evx_id)) == 0
    evx_e = regsub(evx_e, &quot;(?&lt;![A-Za-z0-9_.])&quot; ~ evx_id ~ &quot;(?![A-Za-z0-9_])&quot;, &quot;vars.&quot; ~ evx_id)
    evx_done += evx_id
  endif
endloop
return evx_e
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__gen2" type="series" private="1">
 <params count="4">
  <param name="expr" type="string"/>
  <param name="vars" type="list"/>
  <param name="base" type="string"/>
  <param name="dlt" type="series"/>
 </params>
<code># like ev_gen, but the dataset series called base is shifted by dlt
# (forecast minus actual; zero before the sample), lags included
string evx_e = ev__prep(expr, vars)
evx_e = regsub(evx_e, &quot;vars\.&quot; ~ base ~ &quot;(\(-?[0-9]+\))?(?![A-Za-z0-9_])&quot;, &quot;(vars.&quot; ~ base ~ &quot;\1 + misszero(dlt\1))&quot;)
series evx_out = @evx_e
return evx_out
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__toseries" type="series" private="1">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="v" type="matrix" const="true"/>
  <param name="tobs" type="matrix" const="true"/>
 </params>
<code>series s = NA
loop i = 1..rows(v)
  scalar t = tobs[i]
  s[t] = v[i]
endloop
return s
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__stats" type="void" private="1">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="b" type="bundleref"/>
 </params>
<code># common EViews statistics from b.y, b.uhat, b.k, b.lnl (and b.T)
scalar n = rows(b.uhat)
scalar k = b.k
matrix u = b.uhat
matrix d = b.y - meanc(b.y)
b.T = n
b.ssr = u'u
b.rsq = 1 - b.ssr / (d'd)
b.adjrsq = 1 - (1 - b.rsq) * (n - 1) / (n - k)
b.meany = meanc(b.y)
b.sdy = sqrt(d'd / (n - 1))
scalar kk = inbundle(b, &quot;sigmasq&quot;) ? k + 1 : k
b.aic = -2 * b.lnl / n + 2 * kk / n
b.sc = -2 * b.lnl / n + kk * log(n) / n
b.hq = -2 * b.lnl / n + 2 * kk * log(log(n)) / n
matrix du = u[2:n] - u[1:n-1]
b.dw = (du'du) / (u'u)
b.tstat = b.coeff ./ b.stderr
matrix p = zeros(k, 1)
loop i = 1..k
  p[i] = 2 * pvalue(t, n - k, abs(b.tstat[i]))
endloop
b.pval = p
if !inbundle(b, &quot;F&quot;)
  b.F = NA
  b.Fp = NA
endif
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__depform" type="scalar" private="1">
 <params count="3">
  <param name="dep" type="string"/>
  <param name="base" type="stringref"/>
  <param name="vars" type="list"/>
 </params>
<code># form of the dependent variable: 0 = Y, 1 = log(Y), 2 = d(Y), 3 = dlog(Y)
# or d(log(Y)); -1 = other. base receives the series name Y.
strings pats = defarray(&quot;^\s*([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)\s*$&quot;, &quot;^\s*log\(\s*([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)\s*\)\s*$&quot;, &quot;^\s*d\(\s*([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)\s*\)\s*$&quot;, &quot;^\s*dlog\(\s*([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)\s*\)\s*$&quot;, &quot;^\s*d\(\s*log\(\s*([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)\s*\)\s*\)\s*$&quot;)
matrix forms = {0, 1, 2, 3, 3}
loop i = 1..nelem(pats)
  string m = regsub(dep, &quot;(?i)&quot; ~ pats[i], &quot;\1&quot;)
  if m != dep || i == 1 &amp;&amp; regsub(dep, &quot;(?i)&quot; ~ pats[1], &quot;&quot;) == &quot;&quot;
    if rows(instrings(varnames(vars), m)) &gt; 0
      base = m
      return forms[i]
    endif
  endif
endloop
base = &quot;&quot;
return -1
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__toseries_s" type="series" private="1">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="v" type="matrix" const="true"/>
  <param name="tobs" type="matrix" const="true"/>
 </params>
<code>return ev__toseries(v, tobs)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__fc_finish" type="bundle" private="1">
 <params count="15">
  <param name="b" type="bundle"/>
  <param name="dep" type="string"/>
  <param name="base" type="string"/>
  <param name="form" type="scalar"/>
  <param name="dynamic" type="bool"/>
  <param name="level" type="bool"/>
  <param name="y" type="matrix"/>
  <param name="yf" type="matrix"/>
  <param name="se" type="matrix"/>
  <param name="Ylev" type="matrix"/>
  <param name="yfl" type="matrix"/>
  <param name="sel" type="matrix"/>
  <param name="tobs" type="matrix"/>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool"/>
  <param name="approx_se" type="bool"/>
 </params>
<code>bundle f
f.depvar = b.depvar
f.base = toupper(base)
f.form = form
f.dynamic = dynamic
f.level = level &amp;&amp; form &gt; 0
f.yf = yf
f.se = se
f.actual = y
f.yfl = yfl
f.sel = sel
f.actual_level = Ylev
f.tobs = tobs
f.sample = sprintf(&quot;%s %s&quot;, obslabel($t1), obslabel($t2))
f.se_note = approx_se ? &quot;S.E. of a dynamic forecast from an explicit equation uses the one-step formula&quot; : &quot;&quot;
# evaluation statistics for the series reported
matrix a = f.level ? Ylev : y
matrix p = f.level ? yfl : yf
matrix m = ok(a) .* ok(p)
f.nobs = sum(m)
if f.nobs &gt; 0
  a = selifr(a, m)
  p = selifr(p, m)
  matrix e = p - a
  scalar mse = meanc(e.^2)
  f.rmse = sqrt(mse)
  f.mae = meanc(abs(e))
  f.mape = 100 * meanc(abs(e ./ a))
  f.theil = f.rmse / (sqrt(meanc(a.^2)) + sqrt(meanc(p.^2)))
  scalar sa = sqrt(meanc((a - meanc(a)).^2))
  scalar sp = sqrt(meanc((p - meanc(p)).^2))
  scalar r = (sa &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; sp &gt; 0) ? meanc((a - meanc(a)) .* (p - meanc(p))) / (sa * sp) : 0
  f.bias_prop = (meanc(p) - meanc(a))^2 / mse
  f.var_prop = (sp - sa)^2 / mse
  f.cov_prop = 2 * (1 - r) * sp * sa / mse
endif
if !quiet
  ev_fprint(&amp;f)
endif
return f
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__fc_arma" type="bundle" private="1">
 <params count="7">
  <param name="b" type="bundle"/>
  <param name="vars" type="list"/>
  <param name="dynamic" type="bool"/>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool"/>
  <param name="level" type="bool"/>
  <param name="form" type="scalar"/>
  <param name="base" type="string"/>
 </params>
<code># regression with ARMA errors: y = X beta + u,  phi(L) u = theta(L) e
string dep = strsplit(b.spec)[1]
series eva_y = ev_gen(dep, vars)
matrix y = {eva_y}
series eva_o = obs
matrix tobs = {eva_o}
scalar T = rows(y)
matrix Xf = b.hasc ? ones(T, 1) : {}
loop i = 1..nelem(b.xtok)
  series eva_x = ev_gen(b.xtok[i], vars)
  Xf ~= {eva_x}
endloop
matrix xb = cols(Xf) &gt; 0 ? Xf * b.beta : zeros(T, 1)
scalar s0 = tobs[1]
scalar N = max(tobs[T], maxc(b.tobs))
matrix U = mshape(NA, N, 1)        # u = y - X beta, by observation number
matrix E = mshape(NA, N, 1)        # innovations
U[b.tobs] = b.ureg
E[b.tobs] = b.uhat
scalar pmax = cols(b.pl) ? maxr(b.pl) : 0
scalar qmax = cols(b.ql) ? maxr(b.ql) : 0
errorif(s0 - max(pmax, qmax) &lt; minc(b.tobs) || s0 &gt; maxc(b.tobs) + 1, &quot;ARMA forecasts must start inside the estimation sample or right after it&quot;)
# for static forecasts actual u and e inside the forecast sample are needed
matrix uact = y - xb
matrix yf = mshape(NA, T, 1)
loop t = 1..T
  scalar s = tobs[t]
  scalar uh = 0
  loop i = 1..cols(b.pl)
    scalar L = b.pl[i]
    scalar uu = (s - L &lt; s0 || !dynamic) ? U[s - L] : yf[t - L] - xb[t - L]
    if s - L &gt;= s0 &amp;&amp; !dynamic
      uu = uact[t - L]
    endif
    uh += b.phi[i] * uu
  endloop
  loop i = 1..cols(b.ql)
    scalar L = b.ql[i]
    scalar ee = s - L &lt; s0 ? E[s - L] : (dynamic ? 0 : E[s - L])
    uh += b.theta[i] * ee
  endloop
  yf[t] = xb[t] + uh
  if !dynamic
    # one-step innovation at s, used by later static steps
    E[s] = uact[t] - uh
    U[s] = uact[t]
  endif
endloop
# psi weights of the ARMA error process
matrix psi = zeros(T, 1)
psi[1] = 1
loop j = 2..T
  scalar v = 0
  loop i = 1..cols(b.ql)
    if b.ql[i] == j - 1
      v += b.theta[i]
    endif
  endloop
  loop i = 1..cols(b.pl)
    if j - b.pl[i] &gt;= 1
      v += b.phi[i] * psi[j - b.pl[i]]
    endif
  endloop
  psi[j] = v
endloop
matrix psiC = cum(psi)
scalar s2 = b.sigmasq
matrix se = mshape(NA, T, 1)
matrix Ylev = mshape(NA, T, 1)
matrix Yprev = mshape(NA, T, 1)
matrix yfl = mshape(NA, T, 1)
matrix sel = mshape(NA, T, 1)
if form &gt;= 0
  string e1 = &quot;vars.&quot; ~ base
  string e2 = &quot;vars.&quot; ~ base ~ &quot;(-1)&quot;
  series evf_L = @e1
  series evf_Lp = @e2
  Ylev = {evf_L}
  Yprev = {evf_Lp}
endif
loop t = 1..T
  scalar h = dynamic ? t : 1
  se[t] = sqrt(s2 * sumc(psi[1:h].^2))
  if form &gt;= 0 &amp;&amp; ok(yf[t])
    scalar prev = (t &gt; 1 &amp;&amp; dynamic &amp;&amp; ok(yfl[t-1])) ? yfl[t-1] : Yprev[t]
    if form == 0
      yfl[t] = yf[t]
      sel[t] = se[t]
    elif form == 1
      yfl[t] = exp(yf[t])
      sel[t] = yfl[t] * se[t]
    elif form == 2
      yfl[t] = prev + yf[t]
      sel[t] = dynamic ? sqrt(s2 * sumc(psiC[1:h].^2)) : se[t]
    else
      yfl[t] = prev * exp(yf[t])
      sel[t] = yfl[t] * (dynamic ? sqrt(s2 * sumc(psiC[1:h].^2)) : se[t])
    endif
  endif
endloop
return ev__fc_finish(b, dep, base, form, dynamic, level, y, yf, se, Ylev, yfl, sel, tobs, quiet, 0)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__roots" type="string" private="1">
 <params count="3">
  <param name="coefs" type="matrix"/>
  <param name="lagv" type="matrix"/>
  <param name="sgn" type="scalar"/>
 </params>
<code># inverted roots of 1 - sgn*sum(coef_i L^lag_i), formatted like EViews
if cols(lagv) == 0
  return &quot;&quot;
endif
scalar p = maxr(lagv)
matrix a = zeros(1, p + 1)
a[1] = 1
loop i = 1..cols(lagv)
  a[lagv[i] + 1] = -sgn * coefs[i]
endloop
matrix r = polroots(a)
matrix rr = iscomplex(r) ? Re(r) : r[,1]
matrix ri = iscomplex(r) ? Im(r) : (cols(r) &gt; 1 ? r[,2] : zeros(rows(r), 1))
string out = &quot;&quot;
loop i = 1..rows(rr)
  scalar xr = rr[i]
  scalar xi = ri[i]
  scalar m2 = xr^2 + xi^2
  scalar ire = xr / m2
  scalar iim = -xi / m2
  if abs(iim) &lt; 1e-8
    out ~= sprintf(&quot;%10.2f&quot;, ire)
  else
    out ~= sprintf(&quot;%10s&quot;, sprintf(&quot;%.2f%s%.2fi&quot;, ire, iim &gt;= 0 ? &quot;+&quot; : &quot;-&quot;, abs(iim)))
  endif
endloop
return out
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__nwlag" type="scalar" private="1">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="T" type="scalar"/>
  <param name="lag" type="int"/>
 </params>
<code>return lag &gt; 0 ? lag : floor(4 * (T / 100)^(2 / 9))
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__gmmS" type="matrix" private="1">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="U" type="matrix" const="true"/>
  <param name="lag" type="int"/>
 </params>
<code># long-run covariance of moment contributions U (T x q): White (lag &lt; 0)
# or Bartlett / Newey-West HAC (lag 0 = automatic)
matrix S = U'U
if lag &gt;= 0
  scalar T = rows(U)
  scalar L = ev__nwlag(T, lag)
  loop j = 1..L
    matrix G = U[j+1:T, ]' * U[1:T-j, ]
    S += (1 - j / (L + 1)) * (G + G')
  endloop
endif
return S
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__nlres" type="matrix" private="1">
 <params count="6">
  <param name="rhx" type="strings"/>
  <param name="Y" type="matrix" const="true"/>
  <param name="mask" type="matrix" const="true"/>
  <param name="vars" type="list"/>
  <param name="cu" type="matrix" const="true"/>
  <param name="c" type="matrix" const="true"/>
 </params>
<code># stacked residuals y_i - f_i(c) over the rows in mask
set skip_missing off       # keep rows with missing values when making matrices
loop j = 1..cols(cu)
  string pn = sprintf(&quot;evq_c%d&quot;, cu[j])
  scalar @pn = c[j]
endloop
matrix r = {}
loop i = 1..nelem(rhx)
  string e = rhx[i]
  series evq_f = @e
  r |= selifr(Y[, i] - {evq_f}, mask)
endloop
return r
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__psi" type="matrix" private="1">
 <params count="3">
  <param name="sys" type="bundle"/>
  <param name="n" type="int"/>
  <param name="h" type="int"/>
 </params>
<code># MA matrices Psi_0 .. Psi_{h-1} side by side (n x n*h), from the companion form
matrix A = sys.A
matrix P = I(rows(A))
matrix out = {}
loop j = 1..h
  out ~= P[1:n, 1:n]
  P = A * P
endloop
return out
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__fill" type="matrix" private="1">
 <params count="3">
  <param name="P" type="matrix"/>
  <param name="idx" type="matrix" const="true"/>
  <param name="vals" type="matrix" const="true"/>
 </params>
<code># P with the elements at positions idx (column-major) set to vals
scalar nr = rows(P)
loop i = 1..rows(idx)
  scalar r = (idx[i] - 1) % nr + 1
  scalar c = int((idx[i] - 1) / nr) + 1
  P[r, c] = vals[i]
endloop
return P
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__pick" type="matrix" private="1">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="P" type="matrix" const="true"/>
  <param name="idx" type="matrix" const="true"/>
 </params>
<code>matrix out = zeros(rows(idx), 1)
scalar nr = rows(P)
loop i = 1..rows(idx)
  scalar r = (idx[i] - 1) % nr + 1
  scalar c = int((idx[i] - 1) / nr) + 1
  out[i] = P[r, c]
endloop
return out
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__svar_ll" type="scalar" private="1">
 <params count="5">
  <param name="th" type="matrix"/>
  <param name="Ap" type="matrix" const="true"/>
  <param name="Bp" type="matrix" const="true"/>
  <param name="S" type="matrix" const="true"/>
  <param name="T" type="scalar"/>
 </params>
<code>matrix A = Ap
matrix B = Bp
scalar na = sum(!ok(vec(Ap)))
matrix ia = selifr(seq(1, rows(vec(Ap)))', !ok(vec(Ap)))
matrix ib = selifr(seq(1, rows(vec(Bp)))', !ok(vec(Bp)))
if na
  A = ev__fill(A, ia, th[1:na])
endif
if rows(ib)
  B = ev__fill(B, ib, th[na+1:na+rows(ib)])
endif
scalar n = rows(A)
scalar dA = det(A)
scalar dB = det(B)
if abs(dA) &lt; 1e-12 || abs(dB) &lt; 1e-12
  return -1e10
endif
return -T * n / 2 * log(2 * $pi) + T * log(abs(dA)) - T * log(abs(dB)) - T / 2 * tr(A' * inv(B * B') * A * S)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__svar_grad" type="matrix" private="1">
 <params count="5">
  <param name="th" type="matrix"/>
  <param name="Ap" type="matrix" const="true"/>
  <param name="Bp" type="matrix" const="true"/>
  <param name="S" type="matrix" const="true"/>
  <param name="T" type="scalar"/>
 </params>
<code># numerical gradient of the log likelihood (used for the Hessian)
matrix g = zeros(rows(th), 1)
loop i = 1..rows(th)
  scalar h = 1e-5 * (1 + abs(th[i]))
  matrix t1 = th
  matrix t2 = th
  t1[i] += h
  t2[i] -= h
  g[i] = (ev__svar_ll(t1, Ap, Bp, S, T) - ev__svar_ll(t2, Ap, Bp, S, T)) / (2 * h)
endloop
return g
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__genm" type="series" private="1">
 <params count="6">
  <param name="expr" type="string"/>
  <param name="vars" type="list"/>
  <param name="bases" type="strings"/>
  <param name="D" type="matrix" const="true"/>
  <param name="ovr" type="strings" optional="true"/>
  <param name="suf" type="string" optional="true"/>
 </params>
<code># evaluate expr with each series bases[k] shifted by D[,k] (lags included);
# series named in ovr are replaced by their scenario versions name + suf
string e = ev__prep(expr, vars)
if exists(ovr)
  loop k = 1..nelem(ovr)
    e = regsub(e, &quot;vars\.&quot; ~ ovr[k] ~ &quot;(?![A-Za-z0-9_])&quot;, &quot;vars.&quot; ~ ovr[k] ~ suf)
  endloop
endif
loop k = 1..nelem(bases)
  string dn = sprintf(&quot;evm_d%d&quot;, k)
  series @dn = D[, k]
  e = regsub(e, &quot;vars\.&quot; ~ bases[k] ~ &quot;(\(-?[0-9]+\))?(?![A-Za-z0-9_])&quot;, &quot;(vars.&quot; ~ bases[k] ~ &quot;\1 + misszero(&quot; ~ dn ~ &quot;\1))&quot;)
endloop
series evm_out = @e
return evm_out
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__mg" type="matrix" private="1">
 <params count="7">
  <param name="C" type="bundle"/>
  <param name="vars" type="list"/>
  <param name="t" type="scalar"/>
  <param name="x" type="matrix"/>
  <param name="D" type="matrix"/>
  <param name="Sol" type="matrix" const="true"/>
  <param name="AF" type="matrix" const="true"/>
 </params>
<code># one evaluation of every model equation in period t, given the levels x of
# the endogenous variables in t; returns the implied levels
scalar m = C.m
loop k = 1..m
  D[t, k] = ok(C.L[t, k]) ? x[k] - C.L[t, k] : 0
endloop
scalar st = C.tobs[t]
matrix g = mshape(NA, 1, m)
loop k = 1..m
  scalar v = NA
  if k &lt;= C.ne &amp;&amp; C.rhs[k] == &quot;&quot;
    bundle b = C.eqs[k]
    matrix XX = C.XX[k]
    matrix xr = XX[t,]
    matrix u = C.uses[k]
    strings tok = strsplit(b.spec)
    loop i = 1..cols(xr)
      if u[i]
        series evm_c = ev__genm(tok[i+1], vars, C.bases, D, C.ovr, C.suf)
        xr[i] = evm_c[st]
      endif
    endloop
    v = xr * b.coeff
  else
    series evm_c = ev__genm(C.rhs[k], vars, C.bases, D, C.ovr, C.suf)
    v = evm_c[st]
  endif
  v += AF[t, k]          # add factor and/or stochastic shock
  scalar prev = (C.dynamic &amp;&amp; t &gt; 1) ? Sol[t - 1, k] : C.Lp[t, k]
  scalar f = C.forms[k]
  g[k] = f == 0 ? v : (f == 1 ? exp(v) : (f == 2 ? prev + v : prev * exp(v)))
endloop
return g
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__msolve" type="matrix" private="1">
 <params count="6">
  <param name="C" type="bundle"/>
  <param name="vars" type="list"/>
  <param name="AF" type="matrix" const="true"/>
  <param name="Sol" type="matrix"/>
  <param name="maxit" type="scalarref"/>
  <param name="unconverged" type="scalarref"/>
 </params>
<code># period-by-period damped Newton solution of x = G(x)
scalar T = rows(Sol)
scalar m = C.m
matrix L = C.L
matrix D = zeros(T, m)
maxit = 0
unconverged = 0
loop t = 1..T
  if !C.dynamic
    D = zeros(T, m)
  endif
  matrix x = Sol[t,]
  scalar conv = 0
  loop it = 1..100
    matrix g = ev__mg(C, vars, t, x, D, Sol, AF)
    matrix F = x - g
    if sum(!ok(F))
      break
    endif
    if maxr(abs(F) ./ (1 + abs(x))) &lt; 1e-8      # EViews default convergence
      conv = 1
      maxit = max(maxit, it)
      break
    endif
    matrix J = I(m)
    loop k = 1..m
      matrix xh = x
      scalar h = 1e-6 * (1 + abs(x[k]))
      xh[k] += h
      matrix gh = ev__mg(C, vars, t, xh, D, Sol, AF)
      J[, k] = J[, k] - ((gh - g) / h)'
    endloop
    matrix dx = (inv(J) * F')'
    scalar nF = maxr(abs(F) ./ (1 + abs(x)))
    scalar lam = 1
    loop 30
      matrix xt = x - lam * dx
      matrix gt = ev__mg(C, vars, t, xt, D, Sol, AF)
      matrix Ft = xt - gt
      if sum(!ok(Ft)) == 0
        if maxr(abs(Ft) ./ (1 + abs(xt))) &lt; nF
          break
        endif
      endif
      lam = lam / 2
    endloop
    x = xt
  endloop
  unconverged += !conv
  Sol[t,] = x
  loop k = 1..m
    D[t, k] = ok(L[t, k]) ? x[k] - L[t, k] : 0
  endloop
endloop
return Sol
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__garchh" type="matrix" private="1">
 <params count="10">
  <param name="th" type="matrix" const="true"/>
  <param name="y" type="matrix" const="true"/>
  <param name="XM" type="matrix" const="true"/>
  <param name="eg" type="scalar"/>
  <param name="nm" type="scalar"/>
  <param name="na" type="scalar"/>
  <param name="nt" type="scalar"/>
  <param name="ng" type="scalar"/>
  <param name="mt" type="scalar"/>
  <param name="h0" type="scalar"/>
 </params>
<code># conditional variance recursion of the ARCH family (EViews form);
# th = [lambda (ARCH-M only), mean coefficients, omega, alpha, gamma, beta]
# returns [log-likelihood_t, residual_t, h_t]
scalar T = rows(y)
scalar off = mt &gt; 0
scalar lam = 0
if mt &gt; 0
  lam = th[1]
endif
matrix mu = zeros(T, 1)
if nm &gt; 0
  mu = XM * th[off + 1:off + nm]
endif
scalar p0 = off + nm
scalar w = th[p0 + 1]
matrix e = zeros(T, 1)
matrix h = zeros(T, 1)
matrix ll = zeros(T, 1)
scalar lh0 = log(h0)
scalar az0 = sqrt(2 / $pi)
loop t = 1..T
  scalar ht = w
  loop i = 1..na
    scalar a = th[p0 + 1 + i]
    scalar s = t - i
    if eg
      ht += s &gt;= 1 ? a * abs(e[s]) / sqrt(h[s]) : a * az0
    else
      ht += s &gt;= 1 ? a * e[s]^2 : a * h0
    endif
  endloop
  loop k = 1..nt
    scalar g = th[p0 + 1 + na + k]
    scalar s = t - k
    if eg
      ht += s &gt;= 1 ? g * e[s] / sqrt(h[s]) : 0
    else
      ht += s &gt;= 1 ? g * e[s]^2 * (e[s] &lt; 0) : g * h0 / 2
    endif
  endloop
  loop j = 1..ng
    scalar bb = th[p0 + 1 + na + nt + j]
    scalar s = t - j
    if eg
      ht += s &gt;= 1 ? bb * log(h[s]) : bb * lh0
    else
      ht += s &gt;= 1 ? bb * h[s] : bb * h0
    endif
  endloop
  scalar hv = eg ? exp(ht) : ht
  if !ok(hv) || hv &lt;= 0
    return mshape(NA, T, 3)
  endif
  h[t] = hv
  scalar gm = 0
  if mt == 1
    gm = hv
  elif mt == 2
    gm = sqrt(hv)
  elif mt == 3
    gm = log(hv)
  endif
  e[t] = y[t] - mu[t] - lam * gm
  ll[t] = -0.5 * (log(2 * $pi) + log(hv) + e[t]^2 / hv)
endloop
return ll ~ e ~ h
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__garchobj" type="scalar" private="1">
 <params count="10">
  <param name="th" type="matrix" const="true"/>
  <param name="y" type="matrix" const="true"/>
  <param name="XM" type="matrix" const="true"/>
  <param name="eg" type="scalar"/>
  <param name="nm" type="scalar"/>
  <param name="na" type="scalar"/>
  <param name="nt" type="scalar"/>
  <param name="ng" type="scalar"/>
  <param name="mt" type="scalar"/>
  <param name="h0" type="scalar"/>
 </params>
<code>matrix r = ev__garchh(th, y, XM, eg, nm, na, nt, ng, mt, h0)
scalar s = sumc(r[, 1])
return ok(s) ? s : -1e100
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__lagx" type="string" private="1">
 <params count="3">
  <param name="e" type="string"/>
  <param name="j" type="int"/>
  <param name="vars" type="list"/>
 </params>
<code># lag every series of an expression by j: log(y) -&gt; log(y(-j)), as EViews writes it
errorif(instring(e, &quot;(-&quot;), &quot;ARDL variables cannot contain explicit lags: &quot; ~ e)
if j == 0
  return e
endif
strings nm = varnames(vars)
string r = e
loop i = 1..nelem(nm)
  r = regsub(r, &quot;(?i)(?&lt;![A-Za-z0-9_.])&quot; ~ nm[i] ~ &quot;(?![A-Za-z0-9_(])&quot;, nm[i] ~ sprintf(&quot;(-%d)&quot;, j))
endloop
return r
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__ic" type="scalar" private="1">
 <params count="4">
  <param name="ssr" type="scalar"/>
  <param name="n" type="scalar"/>
  <param name="k" type="scalar"/>
  <param name="ic" type="string"/>
 </params>
<code>scalar l = -n / 2 * (1 + log(2 * $pi) + log(ssr / n))
if ic == &quot;sic&quot; || ic == &quot;bic&quot;
  return -2 * l / n + k * log(n) / n
elif ic == &quot;hq&quot;
  return -2 * l / n + 2 * k * log(log(n)) / n
endif
return -2 * l / n + 2 * k / n
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__ardllr" type="void" private="1">
 <params count="5">
  <param name="b" type="bundleref"/>
  <param name="XL" type="matrices"/>
  <param name="YL" type="matrix" const="true"/>
  <param name="F" type="matrix" const="true"/>
  <param name="D" type="matrix" const="true"/>
 </params>
<code># long-run coefficients (delta method) and the Pesaran-Shin-Smith bounds F test
scalar p = b.p
scalar kx = b.kx
matrix c = b.coeff
matrix V = b.vcv
scalar k = rows(c)
scalar sphi = sumc(c[1:p])
scalar den = 1 - sphi
matrix lr = {}
matrix G = {}                       # Jacobian of the long-run coefficients
strings lrl = array(0)
scalar pos = p
loop i = 1..kx
  scalar qi = b.q[i]
  matrix g = zeros(1, k)
  scalar sb = sumc(c[pos + 1:pos + qi + 1])
  g[1:p] = sb / den^2
  g[pos + 1:pos + qi + 1] = 1 / den
  lr |= sb / den
  G |= g
  strings lt = b.labels
  lrl += lt[pos + 1]
  pos += qi + 1
endloop
if b.trend != &quot;none&quot;
  scalar ic = 0
  loop j = 1..nelem(b.labels)
    if b.labels[j] == &quot;C&quot;
      ic = j
    endif
  endloop
  matrix g = zeros(1, k)
  g[1:p] = c[ic] / den^2
  g[ic] = 1 / den
  lr |= c[ic] / den
  G |= g
  lrl += &quot;C&quot;
endif
b.lr = lr
b.lr_se = sqrt(diag(G * V * G'))
b.lr_labels = lrl
# conditional ECM: dY on Y(-1), X(-1), lagged dY, dX(t..t-q+1), deterministic terms
matrix y = b.y
matrix Yl1 = YL[, 1]
matrix dy = y - Yl1
matrix R = Yl1
loop i = 1..kx
  matrix Mi = XL[i]
  R ~= Mi[, 2]
endloop
errorif(cols(XL[1]) &lt; 2, &quot;The bounds test needs at least one lag of the regressors in the data&quot;)
matrix W = R
loop j = 1..p - 1
  W ~= YL[, j] - YL[, j + 1]
endloop
loop i = 1..kx
  matrix Mi = XL[i]
  scalar qi = b.q[i]
  loop j = 0..max(qi - 1, 0)
    W ~= Mi[, j + 1] - Mi[, j + 2]
  endloop
endloop
W ~= F ~ D
matrix eu = dy - W * mols(dy, W)
scalar m = kx + 1
matrix Wr = W[, m + 1:cols(W)]
matrix er = dy - Wr * mols(dy, Wr)
scalar n = rows(dy)
b.bounds_F = ((er'er - eu'eu) / m) / (eu'eu / (n - cols(W)))
b.bounds_k = kx
# asymptotic critical values, Pesaran, Shin and Smith (2001), Table CI(iii):
# unrestricted intercept, no trend; rows k = 1..5; columns I(0)/I(1) at 10%, 5%, 1%
matrix cv = {4.04, 4.78, 4.94, 5.73, 6.84, 7.84; 3.17, 4.14, 3.79, 4.85, 5.15, 6.36; 2.72, 3.77, 3.23, 4.35, 4.29, 5.61; 2.45, 3.52, 2.86, 4.01, 3.74, 5.06; 2.26, 3.35, 2.62, 3.79, 3.41, 4.68}
b.bounds_cv = mshape(NA, 1, 6)
if b.trend == &quot;const&quot; &amp;&amp; kx &lt;= 5
  b.bounds_cv = cv[kx,]
endif
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__olsr" type="bundle" private="1">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="y" type="matrix" const="true"/>
  <param name="X" type="matrix" const="true"/>
 </params>
<code>matrix e = {}
matrix bh = mols(y, X, &amp;e)
scalar n = rows(y)
matrix d = y - meanc(y)
scalar ssr = e'e
return _(coeff = bh, uhat = e, ssr = ssr, rsq = 1 - ssr / (d'd), n = n, k = cols(X), lnl = -n / 2 * (1 + log(2 * $pi) + log(ssr / n)))
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__teststat" type="void" private="1">
 <params count="4">
  <param name="name" type="string"/>
  <param name="v" type="scalar"/>
  <param name="dist" type="string"/>
  <param name="p" type="scalar"/>
 </params>
<code>printf &quot;%-26s%12.6f    %-22s%10.4f\n&quot;, name, v, dist, p
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__nested" type="bundle" private="1">
 <params count="7">
  <param name="b" type="bundle"/>
  <param name="Xr" type="matrix" const="true"/>
  <param name="Xu" type="matrix" const="true"/>
  <param name="q" type="scalar"/>
  <param name="title" type="string"/>
  <param name="names" type="string"/>
  <param name="quiet" type="bool"/>
 </params>
<code>matrix y = b.y
bundle r0 = ev__olsr(y, Xr)
bundle r1 = ev__olsr(y, Xu)
scalar n = rows(y)
scalar ku = cols(Xu)
bundle r
r.F = ((r0.ssr - r1.ssr) / q) / (r1.ssr / (n - ku))
r.Fp = pvalue(F, q, n - ku, r.F)
r.LR = n * log(r0.ssr / r1.ssr)
r.LRp = pvalue(c, q, r.LR)
if !quiet
  printf &quot;\n%s Test\nEquation: %s\nSpecification: %s\n%s: %s\n&quot;, title, b.spec, b.spec, title == &quot;Omitted Variables&quot; ? &quot;Omitted Variables&quot; : &quot;Redundant Variables&quot;, names
  ev__line(78)
  printf &quot;%-26s%12s    %-10s%14s\n&quot;, &quot;&quot;, &quot;Value&quot;, &quot;df&quot;, &quot;Probability&quot;
  printf &quot;%-26s%12.6f    %-10s%14.4f\n&quot;, &quot;F-statistic&quot;, r.F, sprintf(&quot;(%d, %d)&quot;, q, n - ku), r.Fp
  printf &quot;%-26s%12.6f    %-10d%14.4f\n&quot;, &quot;Likelihood ratio&quot;, r.LR, q, r.LRp
  ev__line(78)
endif
return r
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__nwbw" type="scalar" private="1">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="u" type="matrix" const="true"/>
 </params>
<code># Newey-West (1994) automatic bandwidth for the Bartlett kernel (EViews default)
scalar T = rows(u)
scalar n = floor(4 * (T / 100)^(2 / 9))
scalar s0 = u'u / T
scalar s1 = 0
loop j = 1..n
  scalar g = u[j+1:T]'u[1:T-j] / T
  s0 += 2 * g
  s1 += 2 * j * g
endloop
return 1.1447 * ((s1 / s0)^2)^(1 / 3) * T^(1 / 3)
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__lrvar" type="scalar" private="1">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="u" type="matrix" const="true"/>
  <param name="bw" type="scalar"/>
 </params>
<code># Bartlett-kernel long-run variance with bandwidth bw (weights 1 - j/(bw+1))
scalar T = rows(u)
scalar l2 = u'u / T
scalar jmax = floor(bw)
loop j = 1..jmax
  if j &lt; T
    l2 += 2 * (1 - j / (bw + 1)) * (u[j+1:T]'u[1:T-j] / T)
  endif
endloop
return l2
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__urccv" type="scalar" private="1">
 <params count="3">
  <param name="T" type="scalar"/>
  <param name="itv" type="scalar"/>
  <param name="p" type="scalar"/>
 </params>
<code># MacKinnon critical value for level p: invert urcpval by bisection
scalar lo = -10
scalar hi = 3
loop 60
  scalar mid = (lo + hi) / 2
  if urcpval(mid, T, 1, itv) &gt; p
    hi = mid
  else
    lo = mid
  endif
endloop
return (lo + hi) / 2
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__epochdays" type="series" private="1">
<code># calendar day number (days since 1 Jan 1 AD, day 1) of each observation's start
errorif($datatype != 2, &quot;Frequency conversion needs dated time-series pages&quot;)
series d = $obsdate
series y = floor(d / 10000)
series m = floor(d / 100) - 100 * y
series dd = d - 10000 * y - 100 * m
series r = NA
loop t = 1..$nobs
  r[t] = epochday(y[t], m[t], dd[t])
endloop
return r
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__tgrow" type="void" private="1">
 <params count="3">
  <param name="t" type="bundleref"/>
  <param name="i" type="int"/>
  <param name="j" type="int"/>
 </params>
<code># tables grow when a cell outside them is set (as EViews)
if i &gt; t.rows || j &gt; t.cols
  scalar r = max(i, t.rows)
  scalar c = max(j, t.cols)
  strings nc = array(r * c)
  loop a = 1..r
    loop b = 1..c
      nc[(a - 1) * c + b] = &quot;&quot;
      if a &lt;= t.rows &amp;&amp; b &lt;= t.cols
        nc[(a - 1) * c + b] = t.cells[(a - 1) * t.cols + b]
      endif
    endloop
  endloop
  matrix w = 10 * ones(1, c)
  w[1:t.cols] = t.width
  t.cells = nc
  t.width = w
  t.rows = r
  t.cols = c
endif
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__atrows" type="matrix" private="1">
 <params count="2">
  <param name="F" type="matrix" const="true"/>
  <param name="tobs" type="matrix" const="true"/>
 </params>
<code># rows tobs (observation numbers) of a full-sample column, relative to the sample start
scalar o1 = $t1
matrix r = zeros(rows(tobs), 1)
loop i = 1..rows(tobs)
  scalar t = tobs[i] - o1 + 1
  r[i] = t &gt;= 1 &amp;&amp; t &lt;= rows(F) ? F[t] : NA
endloop
return r
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__lrcov" type="matrix" private="1">
 <params count="3">
  <param name="U" type="matrix" const="true"/>
  <param name="bw" type="scalar"/>
  <param name="onesided" type="bool"/>
 </params>
<code># Bartlett-kernel long-run covariance (onesided: sum over j &gt;= 0 only)
scalar T = rows(U)
matrix S = U'U / T
matrix O = S
scalar jmax = floor(bw)
loop j = 1..jmax
  if j &lt; T
    matrix G = U[j+1:T,]' * U[1:T-j,] / T     # Gamma(j) = E u_t u_{t-j}'
    scalar w = 1 - j / (bw + 1)
    if onesided
      O += w * G'
    else
      O += w * (G + G')
    endif
  endif
endloop
return O
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__irfs" type="matrix" private="1">
 <params count="6">
  <param name="A" type="matrix" const="true"/>
  <param name="S" type="matrix" const="true"/>
  <param name="n" type="scalar"/>
  <param name="h" type="scalar"/>
  <param name="kind" type="string"/>
  <param name="accum" type="bool"/>
 </params>
<code># responses (h x n^2; column (s-1)*n+t: variable t to shock s)
scalar np = rows(A)
matrix J = I(n) ~ zeros(n, np - n)
matrix P = kind == &quot;gen&quot; ? S ./ sqrt(diag(S)') : cholesky(S)
matrix R = zeros(h, n * n)
matrix Ap = I(np)
loop t = 1..h
  matrix Phi = J * Ap * J'
  matrix M = Phi * P
  R[t,] = vec(M)'
  Ap = Ap * A
endloop
if accum
  R = cum(R)
endif
return R
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__glsdetrend" type="matrix" private="1">
 <params count="3">
  <param name="y" type="matrix" const="true"/>
  <param name="trend" type="bool"/>
  <param name="cbar" type="scalarref"/>
 </params>
<code># ERS quasi-differencing with c-bar = -7 (constant) or -13.5 (trend)
scalar T = rows(y)
cbar = trend ? -13.5 : -7
scalar a = 1 + cbar / T
matrix Z = ones(T, 1)
if trend
  Z ~= seq(1, T)'
endif
matrix yq = y[1] | (y[2:T] - a * y[1:T-1])
matrix Zq = Z[1,] | (Z[2:T,] - a * Z[1:T-1,])
matrix b = mols(yq, Zq)
return y - Z * b
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__arspec" type="scalar" private="1">
 <params count="3">
  <param name="yd" type="matrix" const="true"/>
  <param name="maxlag" type="int"/>
  <param name="kopt" type="scalarref"/>
 </params>
<code># AR spectral density at frequency zero of GLS-detrended data, lag chosen by SIC
scalar T = rows(yd)
matrix dy = yd[2:T] - yd[1:T-1]
scalar best = 1e300
scalar f0 = NA
loop k = 0..maxlag
  matrix Z = yd[maxlag + 1:T - 1]
  loop j = 1..k
    Z ~= dy[maxlag + 1 - j:T - 1 - j]
  endloop
  matrix e = {}
  matrix b = mols(dy[maxlag + 1:T - 1], Z, &amp;e)
  scalar n = rows(e)
  scalar s2 = e'e / n
  scalar sic = log(s2) + cols(Z) * log(n) / n
  if sic &lt; best
    best = sic
    kopt = k
    scalar sb = 0
    if k &gt; 0
      sb = sumc(b[2:k+1])
    endif
    f0 = s2 / (1 - sb)^2
  endif
endloop
return f0
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__smooth_ssr" type="scalar" private="1">
 <params count="5">
  <param name="th" type="matrix" const="true"/>
  <param name="y" type="matrix" const="true"/>
  <param name="m" type="string"/>
  <param name="s" type="scalar"/>
  <param name="fix" type="matrix" const="true"/>
 </params>
<code>matrix f = ev__smooth_run(th, y, m, s, fix)
scalar r = sumc((y - f[, 1]).^2)
return ok(r) ? r : 1e300
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__smooth_run" type="matrix" private="1">
 <params count="5">
  <param name="th" type="matrix" const="true"/>
  <param name="y" type="matrix" const="true"/>
  <param name="m" type="string"/>
  <param name="s" type="scalar"/>
  <param name="fix" type="matrix" const="true"/>
 </params>
<code># returns [one-step forecast, smoothed series]
matrix par = 1 ./ (1 + exp(-th))
loop i = 1..rows(par)
  if ok(fix[i])
    par[i] = fix[i]
  endif
endloop
scalar T = rows(y)
matrix F = zeros(T, 2)
if m == &quot;s&quot;
  scalar a = par[1]
  scalar S = meanc(y[1:ceil((T + 1) / 2)])
  loop t = 1..T
    F[t, 1] = S
    S = a * y[t] + (1 - a) * S
    F[t, 2] = S
  endloop
elif m == &quot;d&quot;
  scalar a = par[1]
  scalar S = y[1]
  scalar D = y[1]
  loop t = 1..T
    F[t, 1] = 2 * S - D + a / (1 - a) * (S - D)
    S = a * y[t] + (1 - a) * S
    D = a * S + (1 - a) * D
    F[t, 2] = S
  endloop
else
  scalar a = par[1]
  scalar b = par[2]
  scalar g = m == &quot;n&quot; ? 0 : par[3]
  scalar L = y[1]
  scalar Bt = 0
  matrix Sc = m == &quot;m&quot; ? ones(s, 1) : zeros(s, 1)
  if m != &quot;n&quot;
    matrix y1 = y[1:s]
    L = meanc(y1)
    Bt = T &gt; 2 * s ? (meanc(y[s+1:2*s]) - L) / s : 0
    Sc = m == &quot;m&quot; ? y1 / L : y1 - L
  endif
  loop t = 1..T
    scalar k = (t - 1) % s + 1
    if m == &quot;m&quot;
      F[t, 1] = (L + Bt) * Sc[k]
    elif m == &quot;a&quot;
      F[t, 1] = L + Bt + Sc[k]
    else
      F[t, 1] = L + Bt
    endif
    scalar Lold = L
    if m == &quot;m&quot;
      L = a * y[t] / Sc[k] + (1 - a) * (L + Bt)
      Bt = b * (L - Lold) + (1 - b) * Bt
      Sc[k] = g * y[t] / L + (1 - g) * Sc[k]
      F[t, 2] = (L + Bt) * Sc[k]
    elif m == &quot;a&quot;
      L = a * (y[t] - Sc[k]) + (1 - a) * (L + Bt)
      Bt = b * (L - Lold) + (1 - b) * Bt
      Sc[k] = g * (y[t] - L) + (1 - g) * Sc[k]
      F[t, 2] = L + Bt + Sc[k]
    else
      L = a * y[t] + (1 - a) * (L + Bt)
      Bt = b * (L - Lold) + (1 - b) * Bt
      F[t, 2] = L + Bt
    endif
  endloop
endif
return F
</code>
</gretl-function>
<gretl-function name="ev__ymd" type="matrix" private="1">
 <params count="1">
  <param name="d" type="scalar">
<description>EViews date number</description>
  </param>
 </params>
<code>scalar iso = isodate(d + 1)                 # epoch day = EViews date number + 1
scalar y = floor(iso / 10000)
scalar m = floor(iso / 100) - 100 * y
return {y, m, iso - 10000 * y - 100 * m}
</code>
</gretl-function>
<sample-script>
set verbose off
include EViewsCompat.gfn
open denmark --quiet

# EViews:  ls dlog(lrm) c dlog(lry) lrm(-1) ibo ide
bundle eq1 = ev_ls(&quot;dlog(LRM) c dlog(LRY) LRM(-1) IBO IDE&quot;, dataset)

# EViews:  eq1.wald c(4)=0, c(5)=0
bundle w = ev_wald(eq1, &quot;c(4)=0, c(5)=0&quot;)

# EViews:  View &gt; Residual Diagnostics
bundle d = ev_diag(eq1, 2)

# EViews:  White / HAC coefficient covariance
bundle eq2 = ev_ls(&quot;dlog(LRM) c dlog(LRY) LRM(-1)&quot;, dataset, &quot;hac&quot;)

# EViews:  series g = @pch(lry)  /  series sm = @movav(lry, 4)
series g = ev_gen(&quot;@pch(LRY)&quot;, dataset)
series sm = ev_gen(&quot;@movav(LRY, 4)&quot;, dataset)

# EViews:  Freeze the estimation table
ev_freeze(eq1, &quot;eq1.csv&quot;)
</sample-script>
</gretl-function-package>
</gretl-functions>
